helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	$[officename] Draw Features				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148797	1			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"main0503\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/main0503.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] Draw Features\"\>$[officename] Draw Features\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975	2			0	en-GB	$[officename] Draw lets you create simple and complex drawings and export them in a number of common image formats. You can also insert tables, charts, formulae and other items created in $[officename] programs into your drawings.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147435	11			0	en-GB	Vector Graphics				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3153142	12			0	en-GB	$[officename] Draw creates vector graphics using lines and curves defined by mathematical vectors. Vectors describe lines, ellipses, and polygons according to their geometry.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154320	14			0	en-GB	Creating 3-D Objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3145251	15			0	en-GB	You can create simple 3-D objects such as cubes, spheres, and cylinders in $[officename] Draw and even modify the light source of the objects.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154491	20			0	en-GB	Grids and Guides				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3149379	6			0	en-GB	Grids and guides provide a visual cue to help you align objects in your drawing. You can also choose to snap an object to a grid line, guide or to the edge of another object.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155601	16			0	en-GB	Connecting Objects to Show Relationships				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3149124	17			0	en-GB	You can connect objects in $[officename] Draw with special lines called "connectors" to show the relationship between objects. Connectors attach to glue points on drawing objects and remain attached when the connected objects are moved. Connectors are useful for creating organisation charts and technical diagrams.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155764	21			0	en-GB	Displaying Dimensions				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333	22			0	en-GB	Technical diagrams often show the dimensions of objects in the drawing. In $[officename] Draw, you can use dimension lines to calculate and display linear dimensions.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154705	18			0	en-GB	Gallery				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3154022	7			0	en-GB	The Gallery contains images, animations, sounds and other items that you can insert and use in your drawings as well as other $[officename] programs.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149207	19			0	en-GB	Graphic File Formats				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3155112	5			0	en-GB	$[officename] Draw can export to many common graphic file formats, such as BMP, GIF, JPG, and PNG.				20130618 17:22:18
