helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0209.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153191				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>rulers; in presentations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>origin of rulers\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0209.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153191	1			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/simpress/main0209.xhp\" name=\"Rulers\"\>Rulers\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0209.xhp	0	help	par_id3149666	2			0	en-GB	You can use vertical and horizontal rulers at the left and upper edges of the $[officename] Impress workspace to assist you in creating your slide. The sections of the rulers that cover the area of the slide are white.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0209.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963	4			0	en-GB	When you select an object, its dimensions are displayed on the rulers as grey double lines. To precisely resize the object, drag one of the double lines to a new location on the ruler.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0209.xhp	0	help	par_id3150206	8			0	en-GB	When you select a text object on a slide, indents and tabs are displayed on the horizontal ruler. To change the indent or tab settings for the text object, drag an indent or a tab stop marker to a new location on the ruler.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0209.xhp	0	help	par_id3150253	7			0	en-GB	You can also drag a \<link href=\"text/simpress/01/04030000.xhp\" name=\"snap line\"\>snap line\</link\> from a ruler to help you align objects on your slide. To insert a snap line using a ruler, drag the edge of a ruler into the slide.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0209.xhp	0	help	par_id3153820	3			0	en-GB	To show or hide the rulers, choose \<link href=\"text/simpress/01/03060000.xhp\" name=\"View - Rulers\"\>\<emph\>View - Rulers\</emph\>\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0209.xhp	0	help	par_id3148609	9			0	en-GB	To specify the measurement units for a ruler, right-click the ruler, and then choose a new unit from the list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0209.xhp	0	help	par_id3149129	6			0	en-GB	To change the origin (0 point) of the rulers, drag the intersection of the two rulers in the top left corner into the workspace. Vertical and horizontal guides appear. Continue to drag until the vertical and horizontal guides are where you want the new origin to be, and then release. To reset the origins of the rulers to the default values, double-click the intersection.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0209.xhp	0	help	par_id3154651	5			0	en-GB	To change the slide margins, drag the edge of the white areas in the rulers.				20130618 17:22:18
