helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3151248	60			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierCutLine\"\>The \<emph\>Split Curve\</emph\> icon splits a curve. Select the point or points at which you want to split the curve, then click the icon\</ahelp\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3153788				0	en-GB	\<image id=\"img_id3148489\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_beziercutline.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148489\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3152581	61			0	en-GB	Split Curve				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150345	62			0	en-GB	Convert To Curve				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3148420	63			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierConvert\"\>Converts a curve into a straight line or converts a straight line into a curve.\</ahelp\> If you select a single point, the curve before the point will be converted. If two points are selected, the curve between both points will be converted. If you select more than two points, each time that you click this icon, a different portion of the curve will be converted. If necessary, round points are converted into corner points and corner points are converted into round points.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304	64			0	en-GB	If a certain section of the curve is straight, the end points of the line have a maximum of one control point each. They cannot be modified to round points unless the straight line is converted back to a curve.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3158212				0	en-GB	\<image id=\"img_id3149036\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_bezierconvert.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149036\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3158445	65			0	en-GB	Convert To Curve				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153199	66			0	en-GB	Corner Point				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3148460	67			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierEdge\"\>Converts the selected point or points into corner points.\</ahelp\> Corner points have two movable control points, which are independent from each other. A curved line, therefore, does not go straight through a corner point, but forms a corner.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3154576				0	en-GB	\<image id=\"img_id3154201\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_bezieredge.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154201\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3166429	25			0	en-GB	Corner Point				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166436	27			0	en-GB	Smooth Transition				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3155510	29			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierSmooth\"\>Converts a corner point or symmetrical point into a smooth point.\</ahelp\> Both control points of the corner point are aligned in parallel, and can only be moved simultaneously. The control points may differentiate in length, allowing you to vary the degree of curvature.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3148813				0	en-GB	\<image id=\"img_id3151183\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_beziersmooth.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3151183\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3154258	28			0	en-GB	Smooth Transition				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159622	30			0	en-GB	Symmetric Transition				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3155812	32			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierSymmetric\"\>This icon converts a corner point or a smooth point into a symmetrical point.\</ahelp\> Both control points of the corner point are aligned in parallel and have the same length. They can only be moved simultaneously and the degree of curvature is the same in both directions.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3153818				0	en-GB	\<image id=\"img_id3159218\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_beziersymmetric.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3159218\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3146866	31			0	en-GB	Symmetric Transition				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146786	33			0	en-GB	Close Bézier				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3156032	35			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierClose\"\>Closes a line or a curve.\</ahelp\> A line is closed by connecting the last point with the first point, indicated by an enlarged square.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3154344				0	en-GB	\<image id=\"img_id3148607\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_bezierclose.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148607\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3147070	34			0	en-GB	Close Bézier				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156351	36			0	en-GB	Eliminate Points				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3149441	38			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierEliminatePoints\"\>Marks the current point or the selected points for deletion.\</ahelp\> This happens in the event that the point is located on a straight line. If you convert a curve or a polygon with the \<emph\>Convert to Curve\</emph\> icon into a straight line or you change a curve with the mouse so that a point lies on the straight line, it is removed. The angle from which the point reduction is to take place \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"DRAW\"\>can be set by choosing \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01070300.xhp\" name=\"Drawing - Grid\"\>\<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME Draw - Grid\</emph\>\</link\> in the Options dialogue box\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"IMPRESS\"\>can be set by choosing \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01070300.xhp\" name=\"Presentation - Grid\"\>\<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME Impress - Grid\</emph\>\</link\> in the Options dialogue box\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>is 15° by default.\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3148970				0	en-GB	\<image id=\"img_id3155385\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_beziereliminatepoints.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155385\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3152869	37			0	en-GB	Eliminate Points				20130618 17:22:18
