helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Positioning Objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147828				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>objects;anchoring options\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>positioning;objects (guide)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>anchors;objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>frames;anchoring options\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures;anchoring options\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>centring;images on HTML pages\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147828	45			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"anchor_object\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/anchor_object.xhp\" name=\"Positioning Objects\"\>Positioning Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3147251	46			0	en-GB	You can use anchors to position an object, graphic, or frame in a document. An anchored item remains in place, or moves when you modify the document. The following anchoring options are available:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145599	47			0	en-GB	Anchoring				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145622	48			0	en-GB	Effect				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145650	49			0	en-GB	As character				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151181	50			0	en-GB	Anchors the selected item as a character in the current text. If the height of the selected item is greater than the current font size, the height of the line containing the item is increased.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_idN10674				0	en-GB	To centre an image on an HTML page, insert the image, anchor it "as character", then centre the paragraph.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151212	51			0	en-GB	To character				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151235	52			0	en-GB	Anchors the selected item to a character.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155071	53			0	en-GB	To paragraph				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155094	54			0	en-GB	Anchors the selected item to the current paragraph.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155122	55			0	en-GB	To page				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155144	56			0	en-GB	Anchors the selected item to the current page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145674	57			0	en-GB	To frame				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145697	58			0	en-GB	Anchors the selected item to the surrounding frame.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145715	59			0	en-GB	When you insert an object, graphic, or frame, an anchor icon appears where the item is anchored. You can position an anchored item by dragging the item to another location. To change the anchoring options of an item, right-click the item, and then choose an option from the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Anchor\</item\> sub-menu.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Rearranging a Document by Using the Navigator				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149973				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>headings;rearranging\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rearranging headings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>moving;headings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>demoting heading levels\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>promoting heading levels\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Navigator;heading levels and chapters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>arranging;headings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>outlines;arranging chapters\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149973	58			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"arrange_chapters\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/arrange_chapters.xhp\" name=\"Rearranging a Document by Using the Navigator\"\>Arranging Chapters in the Navigator\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147795	59			0	en-GB	You can move headings and subordinate text up and down in a document text by using the Navigator. You can also promote and demote heading levels. To use this feature, format the headings in your document with one of the predefined heading paragraph styles. To use a custom paragraph style for a heading, choose \<emph\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</emph\>, select the style in the \<emph\>Paragraph Style\</emph\> box, and then double-click a number in the \<emph\>Levels\</emph\> list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3145652	62			0	en-GB	To quickly move the text cursor to a heading in the document, double-click the heading in the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\> list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155461	60			0	en-GB	To dock the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\>, drag the title bar to the edge of the workspace. To undock the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\>, double-click its frame.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151184	70			0	en-GB	To Move a Heading Up or Down in the Document				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id0915200809400790				0	en-GB	Ensure that all heading levels are shown in the Navigator. By default all levels are shown. See steps below how to change the heading levels that are shown.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3151206	71			0	en-GB	On the \<emph\>Standard Bar\</emph\>, click the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id5211883\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_navigator.png\" width=\"0.564cm\" height=\"0.564cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id5211883\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to open the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3151238	72			0	en-GB	On the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\>, click the \<emph\>Content View\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3156338\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20234.png\" width=\"0.564cm\" height=\"0.564cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156338\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155089	74			0	en-GB	Do one of the following:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155114	63			0	en-GB	Drag a heading to a new location in the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\> list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155139	75			0	en-GB	Click a heading in the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\> list, and then click the \<emph\>Promote Chapter\</emph\>\<image id=\"img_id4217546\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20174.png\" width=\"0.564cm\" height=\"0.564cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id4217546\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> or \<emph\>Demote Chapter\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id6505788\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20171.png\" width=\"0.564cm\" height=\"0.564cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id6505788\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3145758	64			0	en-GB	To move the heading without the subordinate text, hold down Ctrl while you drag or click the \<emph\>Promote Chapter\</emph\> or \<emph\>Demote Chapter\</emph\> icons.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155402	76			0	en-GB	To Promote or Demote the Level of a Heading				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155424	77			0	en-GB	Select the heading in the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\> list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_idN1081C				0	en-GB	Click the \<emph\>Promote Level\</emph\> \<image id=\"img_id5564488\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20172.png\" width=\"0.564cm\" height=\"0.564cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id5564488\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> or \<emph\>Demote Level\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3159363\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20173.png\" width=\"0.564cm\" height=\"0.564cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3159363\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155525	78			0	en-GB	To Change the Number of Heading Levels That Are Displayed				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3151352	79			0	en-GB	Click the \<emph\>Heading Levels Shown\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3151310\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20236.png\" width=\"0.564cm\" height=\"0.564cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3151310\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>, and then select a number from the list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Creating Numbered or Bulleted Lists as You Type				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147407				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>numbering; lists, while typing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bullet lists;creating while typing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lists;automatic numbering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers;lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic numbering; AutoCorrect function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bullets; using automatically\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic bullets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paragraphs; automatic numbering\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
