helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3147812	20			0	en-GB	Type the word in the \<emph\>Words with TWo INitial CApitals\</emph\> box and click \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3144875	17			0	en-GB	To quickly undo an AutoCorrect replacement, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Z. This also adds the word or abbreviation that you typed to the AutoCorrect exceptions list.				20130618 17:22:18
