helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155565	11			0	en-GB	You can also click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formula\</item\> icon on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formula\</item\> bar, and then choose a function for your formula.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id8316904				0	en-GB	To reference cells in a Writer text table, enclose the cell address or the cell range in angle brackets. For example, to reference cell A1 from another cell, enter =<A1> into the cell.				20130618 17:22:18
