helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id7748344				0	en-GB	Enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>1\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Value\</item\> box, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>.\<br/\>The Format list now displays a "General" format.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145645	63			0	en-GB	To Define a Condition and the Conditional Text				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145659	64			0	en-GB	The second part of the example is to define the condition that must be met, and to insert a placeholder for displaying the conditional text in your document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3151193	12			0	en-GB	Place the cursor where you want to insert the conditional text in your text.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3151212	65			0	en-GB	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Functions\</item\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3151250	13			0	en-GB	Click "Conditional text" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155936	14			0	en-GB	Type \<item type=\"literal\"\>Reminder EQ "3"\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Condition\</item\> box. In other words, the conditional text will be displayed when the variable in the field that you defined in the first part of this example is equal to three.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155969	15			0	en-GB	The quotation marks enclosing the "3" indicate that the variable that you defined in the first part of this example is a text string.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150446	16			0	en-GB	Type the text that you want to display when the condition is met in the \<emph\>Then\</emph\> box. There is almost no limit to the length of the text that you can enter. You can paste a paragraph into this box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150473	17			0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155073	66			0	en-GB	To Display the Conditional Text				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155086	67			0	en-GB	In this example, the conditional text is displayed when the value of the conditional variable is equal to 3.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155110	19			0	en-GB	Place your cursor in front of the field that you defined in the first part of this example, and then choose \<emph\>Edit - Fields\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155136	68			0	en-GB	Replace the number in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Value\</item\> box with 3, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Close\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155168	20			0	en-GB	If the field does not automatically update, press F9.				20130618 17:22:18
