helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	bm_id1163670				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>finding; text/text formats/styles/objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>replacing; text and text formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>styles;finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>searching, see also finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text formats; finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats; finding and replacing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>searching; formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>objects;finding by Navigator\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Asian languages;search options\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id8568681				0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"finding\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/finding.xhp\"\>Finding and Replacing in Writer\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id611285				0	en-GB	In text documents you can find words, formatting, styles, and more. You can navigate from one result to the next, or you can highlight all results at once, then apply another format or replace the words by other text.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id6226081				0	en-GB	The Find & Replace dialogue box				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6702780				0	en-GB	To find text within the whole document, open the Find & Replace dialogue box without any active text selection. If you want to search only a part of your document, first select that part of text, then open the Find & Replace dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158970				0	en-GB	To Find Text				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6957304				0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\> to open the Find & Replace dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2164677				0	en-GB	Enter the text to find in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id5684072				0	en-GB	Either click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4377269				0	en-GB	When you click \<emph\>Find\</emph\>, Writer will show you the next text that is equal to your entry. You can watch and edit the text, then click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> again to advance to the next found text.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id1371807				0	en-GB	If you closed the dialogue box, you can press a key combination (Ctrl+Shift+F) to find the next text without opening the dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id924100				0	en-GB	Alternatively, you can use the icons at the lower right of the document to navigate to the next text or to any other object in the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9359416				0	en-GB	When you click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Find All\</item\>, Writer selects all text that is equal to your entry. Now you can for example set all found text to bold, or apply a character style to all at once.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id5891598				0	en-GB	To Replace Text				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id1780755				0	en-GB	Unlike searching text, replacing text cannot be restricted to the current selection only.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2467421				0	en-GB	Choose Edit - Find & Replace to open the Find & Replace dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4286935				0	en-GB	Enter the text to search in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9959410				0	en-GB	Enter the text to replace the found text in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> text box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id24109				0	en-GB	Either click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\> or \<emph\>Replace All\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id703451				0	en-GB	When you click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\>, Writer will search the whole document for the text in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box, starting at the current cursor position. When text is found, Writer highlights the text and waits for your response. Click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\> to replace the highlighted text in the document with the text in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> text box. Click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> to advance to the next found text without replacing the current selection.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7540818				0	en-GB	When you click \<emph\>Replace All\</emph\>, Writer replaces all text that matches your entry.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id9908444				0	en-GB	To Find Styles				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id8413953				0	en-GB	You want to find all text in your document to which a certain Paragraph Style is assigned, for example the "Heading 2" style.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2696920				0	en-GB	Choose Edit - Find & Replace to open the Find & Replace dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
