helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3155858	20			0	en-GB	You can insert a cross-reference as a hyperlink in your document using the Navigator. You can even cross-reference items from other \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> documents. If you click the hyperlink when the document is opened in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>, you are taken to the cross-referenced item.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3149833	32			0	en-GB	Open the document(s) containing the items you want to cross-reference.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3148846	23			0	en-GB	On the Standard bar, click the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\> icon.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3156108	25			0	en-GB	Click the arrow next to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Drag Mode\</item\> icon, and ensure that \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert as Hyperlink\</item\> is selected.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153396	31			0	en-GB	In the list at the bottom of the Navigator, select the document containing the item that you want to cross-reference.				20130618 17:22:18
