helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147173	34			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Format - Sections - Section\</emph\> and under \<emph\>Write protection\</emph\> unmark the \<emph\>Protect\</emph\> check box. Enter the correct password.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146081	35			0	en-GB	Protecting Cells in a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer Table				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154480	36			0	en-GB	You can protect the contents of individual cells of a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer text table from changes.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id363170				0	en-GB	This protection is not intended for secure protection. It is just a switch to protect the cells against accidental changes.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154360	37			0	en-GB	Turning on protection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145643	38			0	en-GB	Place the cursor in a cell or select cells. Right-click to open the context menu, then choose \<emph\>Cell - Protect\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150042	39			0	en-GB	Turning off protection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3155178	40			0	en-GB	Place the cursor in the cell or select the cells. First, if necessary, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</emph\> and mark \<emph\>Cursor in protected areas - Enable\</emph\>. Then right-click the cell to open the context menu and choose \<emph\>Cell - Unprotect\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3151189	41			0	en-GB	Select the table in the Navigator, open the context menu and select \<emph\>Table - Unprotect\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147322	42			0	en-GB	Use Shift+Ctrl+T to remove protection for the entire current table or all selected tables.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149259	43			0	en-GB	Automatic Protection of Indexes and Tables				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153966	44			0	en-GB	Tables of contents and indexes created automatically in a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer text are automatically protected against accidental changes.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id814539				0	en-GB	This protection is not intended for secure protection. It is just a switch to protect the contents against accidental changes.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145767	45			0	en-GB	Turning on protection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153786	46			0	en-GB	Place the cursor in the index/table of contents.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3159088	47			0	en-GB	From the context menu choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>. On the Index/Table tab page, mark \<emph\>Protected against manual changes\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154118	48			0	en-GB	Turning off protection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3148463	49			0	en-GB	Place the cursor in the index. First of all, if necessary, under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</emph\>, mark \<emph\>Cursor in protected areas - Enable\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3152968	50			0	en-GB	From the context menu choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>. On the Index/Table tab page, unmark \<emph\>Protected against manual changes\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3152774	51			0	en-GB	In the Navigator, select the index, then open the context menu in the Navigator and select \<emph\>Index - Read-only\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
