helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149832	40			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"sections\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/sections.xhp\" name=\"Using Sections\"\>Using Sections\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3153128	2			0	en-GB	Sections are named blocks of text, including graphics or objects, that you can use in a number of ways:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149284	5			0	en-GB	To prevent text from being edited.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149630	4			0	en-GB	To show or hide text.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149647	20			0	en-GB	To reuse text and graphics from other $[officename] documents.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149612	38			0	en-GB	To insert sections of text that uses a different column layout than the current page style.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149855	7			0	en-GB	A section contains at least one paragraph. When you select some text and create a section, a paragraph break is automatically inserted at the end of the text.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149872	8			0	en-GB	You can insert sections from a text document, or an entire text document as a section into another text document. You can also insert sections from a text document as links in another text document, or in the same document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3153367	39			0	en-GB	To insert a new paragraph immediately before or after a section, click in front or behind the section, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154242	44			0	en-GB	Sections and Columns				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255	41			0	en-GB	You can insert sections into an existing section. For example, you can insert a section containing two columns into a section that contains one column.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3154845	42			0	en-GB	A section layout, for example on the number of columns, has priority over the page layout defined in a page style.				20130618 17:22:18
