helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Non-printing Characters				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154507	1			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"Non-printing Characters\"\>Non-printing Characters\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154646	2			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ControlCodes\"\>Shows non-printing characters in your text, such as paragraph marks, line breaks, tab stops, and spaces.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145410	5			0	en-GB	When you delete a paragraph mark, the paragraph that is merged takes on the formatting of the paragraph that the cursor is in.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147511	6			0	en-GB	To specify which non-printing characters are displayed, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040600.xhp\" name=\"Writer - Formatting Aids\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</link\>\</emph\>, and then select the options that you want in the \<emph\>Display of\</emph\> area.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03120000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Web Layout				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145243	1			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/03120000.xhp\" name=\"Web Layout\"\>Web Layout\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154646	2			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BrowseView\"\>Displays the document as seen in a Web browser.\</ahelp\> This is useful when you create HTML documents.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03130000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Print Layout				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03130000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150018	1			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/03130000.xhp\" name=\"Print Layout\"\>Print Layout\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145249	2			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:PrintLayout\"\>Displays how the document will look when you print it.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03140000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Hidden Paragraphs				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155959	1			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/03140000.xhp\" name=\"Hidden Paragraphs\"\>Hidden Paragraphs\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150251	2			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ShowHiddenParagraphs\"\>Shows or hides hidden paragraphs.\</ahelp\> This option only affects the screen display of hidden paragraphs, and not the printing of hidden paragraphs.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3157875	3			0	en-GB	To enable this feature, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040600.xhp\" name=\"Writer - Formatting Aids\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</link\>\</emph\>, and ensure that the \<emph\>Hidden paragraphs\</emph\> check box in the \<emph\>Display of\</emph\> area is selected.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154501	4			0	en-GB	Use the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"field command\"\>field command\</link\> "Hidden Paragraph" to assign a \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090200.xhp\" name=\"condition\"\>condition\</link\> that must be met to hide a paragraph. If the condition is not met, the paragraph is displayed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3083451	5			0	en-GB	When you hide a paragraph, footnotes and frames that are anchored to characters in the paragraph are also hidden.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Insert Manual Break				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145827	1			0	en-GB	Insert Manual Break				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147176	2			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"umbruch\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertBreak\"\>Inserts a manual line break, column break or a page break at the current cursor position.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151176	4			0	en-GB	Type				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145420	5			0	en-GB	Select the type of break that you want to insert.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154097	6			0	en-GB	Line Break				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149805	7			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_BREAK:RB_LINE\"\>Ends the current line, and moves the text found to the right of the cursor to the next line, without creating a new paragraph.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149685	8			0	en-GB	You can also insert a line break by pressing Shift+Enter.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148566	9			0	en-GB	Column Break				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155182	10			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_BREAK:RB_COL\"\>Inserts a manual column break (in a multiple column layout), and moves the text found to the right of the cursor to the beginning of the next \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05040500.xhp\" name=\"column\"\>column\</link\>. A manual column break is indicated by a non-printing border at the top of the new column.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149487	11			0	en-GB	Page Break				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149102	12			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_BREAK:RB_PAGE\"\>Inserts a manual page break, and moves the text found to the right of the cursor to the beginning of the next page. The inserted page break is indicated by a non-printing border at the top of the new page.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145758	13			0	en-GB	You can also insert a page break by pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter. However, if you want to assign the following page a different Page Style, you must use the menu command to insert a manual page break.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149175	14			0	en-GB	Style				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156275	15			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:DLG_BREAK:LB_COLL\"\>Select the page style for the page that follows the manual page break.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145782	16			0	en-GB	Change page number				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155917	17			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:DLG_BREAK:CB_PAGENUM\"\>Assigns the page number that you specify to the page that follows the manual page break. This option is only available if you assign a different page style to the page that follows manual page break.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151384	20			0	en-GB	Page number				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150700	21			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:NUMERICFIELD:DLG_BREAK:ED_PAGENUM\"\>Enter the new page number for the page that follows the manual page break.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150554	18			0	en-GB	To display manual breaks, choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"View - Non-printing Characters\"\>\<emph\>View - Non-printing Characters\</emph\>\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Insert Section				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154108	1			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"bereicheinfuegen\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04020000.xhp\" name=\"Insert Section\"\>Insert Section\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154480	2			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"bereich\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"FN_INSERT_COLUMN_SECTION\"\>Inserts a text section at the cursor position in the document. You can also select a block of text and then choose this command to create a section. You can use sections to insert blocks of text from other documents, to apply custom column layouts, or to protect or to hide blocks of text if a condition is met.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152955	3			0	en-GB	You can insert an entire document in a section, or a named section from another. You can also insert a section as a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#dde\" name=\"DDE\"\>DDE\</link\> link.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149684	5			0	en-GB	To edit a section, choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02170000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Sections\"\>\<emph\>Format - Sections\</emph\>\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155183	6			0	en-GB	The \<emph\>Insert Section\</emph\> dialogue box contains the following tabs:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151257	7			0	en-GB	Insert				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149102	8			0	en-GB	Inserts the section that you defined at the current cursor position in the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Section				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	bm_id5941038				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>sections;inserting sections by DDE\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>DDE; command for inserting sections\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157557	37			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04020100.xhp\" name=\"Section\"\>Section\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154644	38			0	en-GB	Sets the properties of the section.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151170	6			0	en-GB	New Section				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145420	7			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:COMBOBOX:TP_INSERT_SECTION:ED_RNAME\"\>Type a name for the new section.\</ahelp\> By default, $[officename] automatically assigns the name "Section X" to new sections, where X is a consecutive number.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154102	8			0	en-GB	Link				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149806	20			0	en-GB	Link				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154472	21			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_INSERT_SECTION:CB_FILE\"\>Inserts the contents of another document or section from another document in the current section.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153672	26			0	en-GB	DDE				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151310	27			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:MD_EDIT_REGION:CB_DDE\"\>Creates a \<emph\>DDE\</emph\> link. Mark this check box, and then enter the \<emph\>DDE\</emph\> command that you want to use. The \<emph\>DDE\</emph\> option is only available if the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> check box is selected.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3143280	34			0	en-GB	The general syntax for a DDE command is: "<Server> <Topic> <Item>", where server is the DDE name for the application that contains the data. Topic refers to the location of the Item (usually the file name), and Item represents the actual object.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149098	35			0	en-GB	For example, to insert a section named "Section1" from a $[officename] text document abc.sxw as a DDE link, use the command: "soffice x:\\abc.sxw Section1". To insert the contents of the first cell from a Microsoft Excel spreadsheet file called "abc.xls", use the command: "excel x:\\[abc.xls]Sheet1 z1s1". You can also copy the elements that you want to insert as a DDE link, and then \<emph\>Edit - Paste Special\</emph\>. You can then view the DDE command for the link, by selecting the contents and choosing \<emph\>Edit - Fields\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153640	28			0	en-GB	File name\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\> / DDE command \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145754	29			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:MD_EDIT_REGION:ED_FILE\"\>Enter the path and the filename for the file that you want to insert, or click the browse button (\<emph\>...\</emph\>) to locate the file.\</ahelp\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>If the \<emph\>DDE\</emph\> check box is selected, enter the DDE command that you want to use. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155136	39			0	en-GB	...				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156274	40			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:PUSHBUTTON:MD_EDIT_REGION:PB_FILE\"\>Locate the file that you want to insert as a link, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149180	23			0	en-GB	Section				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155910	24			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:COMBOBOX:MD_EDIT_REGION:LB_SUBREG\"\>Select the section in the file that you want to insert as a link.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151373	25			0	en-GB	When you open a document that contains linked sections, you are prompted to update the links.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150687	43			0	en-GB	Write Protection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150700	10			0	en-GB	Protected				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150110	11			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:TRISTATEBOX:MD_EDIT_REGION:CB_PROTECT\"\>Prevents the selected section from being edited.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145261	44			0	en-GB	With password				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149555	45			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_TP_INSERT_SECTION_CB_PASSWD\"\>Protects the selected section with a password. The password must have a minimum of 5 characters.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150549	46			0	en-GB	...				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147742	47			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_PUSHBUTTON_TP_INSERT_SECTION_PB_PASSWD\"\>Opens a dialogue box in which you can change the current password.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146333	48			0	en-GB	Hide				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149830	12			0	en-GB	Hide				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148849	13			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:TRISTATEBOX:MD_EDIT_REGION:CB_HIDE\"\>Hides and prevents the selected section from being printed.\</ahelp\> The components of a hidden sections appear grey in the Navigator. When you rest your mouse pointer over a hidden component in the Navigator, the Help tip "hidden" is displayed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155074	50			0	en-GB	You cannot hide a section if it is the only content on a page, or in a header, footer, footnote, frame, or table cell.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154323	16			0	en-GB	With condition				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154343	17			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:MD_EDIT_REGION:ED_CONDITION\"\>Enter the condition that must be met to hide the section.\</ahelp\> A condition is a \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090200.xhp\" name=\"logical expression\"\>logical expression\</link\>, such as "SALUTATION EQ Mr.". For example, if you use the \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/form_letters_main.xhp\" name=\"mail merge\"\>mail merge\</link\> form letter feature to define a database field called "Salutation" that contains "Mr.", "Ms.", or "Sir or Madam", you can then specify that a section will only be printed if the salutation is "Mr.".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150086	18			0	en-GB	Another example would be to create the field variable "x" and set its value to 1. Then specify a condition based on this variable for hiding a section, such as: "x eq 1". If you want to display the section, set the value of the variable "x" to "0".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_idN108DF				0	en-GB	Properties				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_idN108E3				0	en-GB	You see this area of the dialogue box when the current document is an XForms document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_idN108E6				0	en-GB	Editable in read-only document				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_idN108EA				0	en-GB	Select to allow editing of the section's contents even if the document is opened in read-only mode.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150032	19			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Field commands\"\>Field commands\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3158420	51			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090200.xhp\" name=\"Syntax for conditions\"\>Syntax for conditions\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Indents				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155898	1			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04020200.xhp\" name=\"Indents\"\>Indents\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155182	2			0	en-GB	Indents the section with a left and right margin.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149488	3			0	en-GB	Before section				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149824	4			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_METRICFIELD_TP_SECTION_INDENTS_MF_BEFORE\"\>Specifies the indents before the section, at the left margin.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149108	5			0	en-GB	After section				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148970	6			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_METRICFIELD_TP_SECTION_INDENTS_MF_AFTER\"\>Specifies the indents after the section, at the right margin.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149032	7			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Field commands\"\>Field commands\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04030000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Footnote/Endnote				20130618 17:22:18
