helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Fields				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151171	1			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Fields\"\>Fields\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149805	2			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"feldbefehltext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertField\"\>Inserts a field at the current cursor position.\</ahelp\> Fields contain information that can be automatically updated, such as the date, time, or page number. The dialogue box lists all available fields.\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155903	178			0	en-GB	Insert				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154190	179			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FIELD_INSERT\"\>Inserts the selected field at the current cursor position in the document. To close the dialogue box, click the \<emph\>Close\</emph\> button.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090000.xhp	0	help	par_id5591296				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Closes the dialogue box.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Document				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150017	1			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090001.xhp\" name=\"Document\"\>Document\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3147167	2			0	en-GB	Fields are used to insert information about the current document, for example, file name, template, statistics, user data, date, and time.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154470	3			0	en-GB	For the HTML export and import of date and time fields, \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090007.xhp#datumuhrzeit\" name=\"special $[officename] formats\"\>special $[officename] formats\</link\> are used.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151312	4			0	en-GB	Type				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153672	5			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FLD_DOK:LB_DOKTYPE\"\>Lists the available field types. To add a field to your document, click a field type, click a field in the \<emph\>Select\</emph\> list, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.\</ahelp\> The following fields are available:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155182	6			0	en-GB	Type				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3143272	7			0	en-GB	Meaning				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3151248	10			0	en-GB	Author				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148975	11			0	en-GB	Inserts the name of the user who first saved the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145759	18			0	en-GB	Chapter				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3149172	19			0	en-GB	Inserts the chapter number and/or the chapter name.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145771	14			0	en-GB	Date				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3151370	15			0	en-GB	Inserts the current date. You can insert the date as a fixed field - \<item type=\"literal\"\>Date (fixed)\</item\> - that does not change, or as a dynamic field - \<item type=\"literal\"\>Date\</item\> - that it is updated automatically. To manually update the \<item type=\"literal\"\>Date\</item\> field, press F9.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150699	12			0	en-GB	File name				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150122	13			0	en-GB	Inserts the filename and/or the directory path of the current document, as well as the filename without extension.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3147495	20			0	en-GB	Page				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145264	21			0	en-GB	Inserts the page number of the current, previous, or next page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150561	8			0	en-GB	Sender				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3146341	9			0	en-GB	Inserts fields containing user data. You can change the user data that is displayed by choosing \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010100.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] - User Data\"\>$[officename] - User Data\</link\>\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148863	22			0	en-GB	Statistics				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3151091	23			0	en-GB	Inserts document statistics, such as page and word counts, as a field. To view the statistics of a document, choose \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Statistics\</emph\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153302	16			0	en-GB	Templates				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3156123	17			0	en-GB	Inserts the filename, the path, or the filename without the file extension of the current template. You can also insert the names of the "Category" and the "Style" formats used in the current template. To view the names of the template categories and the styles used in the templates, choose \<emph\>File - Templates -\</emph\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110100.xhp\" name=\"Organise\"\>\<emph\>Organise\</emph\>\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3146939	24			0	en-GB	Time				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154340	25			0	en-GB	Inserts the current time. You can insert the time as a fixed field - \<item type=\"literal\"\>Time (fixed)\</item\> - that does not change, or as a dynamic field - \<item type=\"literal\"\>Time\</item\> - that it is updated automatically. To manually update the \<item type=\"literal\"\>Time\</item\> field, press F9.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154631	26			0	en-GB	The following fields can only be inserted if the corresponding field type is selected in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150660	27			0	en-GB	Select				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150678	28			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FLD_DOK:LB_DOKSELECTION\"\>Lists the available fields for the field type selected in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list. To insert a field, click the field, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155537	53			0	en-GB	To quickly insert a field from the list, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and double-click the field.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155359	30			0	en-GB	Fields				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154220	31			0	en-GB	Function				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145107	32			0	en-GB	Previous page				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3149595	33			0	en-GB	Inserts the page number of the previous page in the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3146896	34			0	en-GB	Next page				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148923	35			0	en-GB	Inserts the page number of the next page in the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3156032	36			0	en-GB	Page Number				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3159212	37			0	en-GB	Inserts the current page number.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3159229	38			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Format\</emph\>, click the numbering format that you want to use.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145188	39			0	en-GB	If you want, you can enter an \<emph\>Offset\</emph\> for the displayed page number. With an \<emph\>Offset\</emph\> value of 1, the field will display a number that is 1 more than the current page number, but only if a page with that number exists. On the last page of the document, this same field will be empty.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150891	45			0	en-GB	Offset				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155312	46			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:TP_FLD_DOK:ED_DOKVALUE\"\>Enter the offset value that you want to apply to a page number field, for example "+1".\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154948	54			0	en-GB	If you want to change the actual page number and not the displayed number, do not use the \<emph\>Offset\</emph\> value. To change page numbers, read the \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagenumbers.xhp\" name=\"Page Numbers\"\>\<emph\>Page Numbers\</emph\>\</link\> guide.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145595	41			0	en-GB	Format				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145613	42			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FLD_DOK:LB_DOKFORMAT\"\>Click the format that you want to apply to the selected field, or click "Additional formats" to define a custom format.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150138	49			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"datumuhrzeitformat\"\>When you click "Additional formats", the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Number Format\"\>\<emph\>Number Format\</emph\>\</link\> dialogue box opens, in which you can define a custom format. \</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154867	50			0	en-GB	If you choose "Chapter number without separator" for a chapter field, the separators that are specified for chapter number in \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/06060000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Chapter numbering\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Chapter numbering\</emph\>\</link\> are not displayed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3156079	63			0	en-GB	If you choose "chapter number" as the \<emph\>format\</emph\> for reference fields, only the number of the chapter heading containing the referenced object is displayed in the field. If the paragraph style for the chapter heading is not numbered, the field is left blank.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148682	56			0	en-GB	The following number range formats are for paragraphs formatted with numbered or bulleted lists:				20130618 17:22:18
