helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Database				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153536	1			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090006.xhp\" name=\"Database\"\>Database\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3154471	2			0	en-GB	You can insert fields from any database, for example, address fields, into your document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id090220080439090				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Lists the available field types. To add a field to your document, click a field type, click a field in the \<emph\>Select\</emph\> list, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3154196	3			0	en-GB	Field type				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3149484	4			0	en-GB	Meaning				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3149096	5			0	en-GB	Any Record				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3151257	6			0	en-GB	Inserts the contents of the database field that you specify in the \<emph\>Record Number\</emph\> box as a mail merge field if the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090200.xhp\" name=\"Condition\"\>\<emph\>Condition\</emph\>\</link\> that you enter is met. Only records selected by a multiple selection in the data source view are considered.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3147100	7			0	en-GB	You can use this field to insert several records into a document. Simply insert the \<emph\>Any Record\</emph\> field in front of the form letter fields that use a certain record.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3153632	8			0	en-GB	Database Name				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3152776	9			0	en-GB	Inserts the name of the database table selected in the \<emph\>Database selection\</emph\> box. The "Database Name" field is a global field, that is, if you insert a different database name in your document, the contents of all previously inserted "Database Name" fields are updated.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3149167	15			0	en-GB	Mail merge field				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3145779	16			0	en-GB	Inserts the name of a database field as a placeholder, so that you can create a mail merge document. The field content is automatically inserted when you print the form letter.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3151372	12			0	en-GB	Next record				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3150114	13			0	en-GB	Inserts the contents of the next mail merge field in your document, if the condition that you define is met. The records that you want to include must be selected in the data source view.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3155861	14			0	en-GB	You can use the "Next record" field to insert the contents of consecutive records between the mail merge fields in a document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3147412	10			0	en-GB	Record number				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3147495	11			0	en-GB	Inserts the number of the selected database record.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149565	17			0	en-GB	Database Selection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3145268	18			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DB_SELECTION_TLB\"\>Select the database table or the database query that you want the field to refer to.\</ahelp\> You can include fields from more than one database or query in a document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id0902200804391084				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>For fields linked to a condition, enter the criteria here.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3147739	19			0	en-GB	If you want, you can assign a condition that must be met before the contents of the "Any Record" and "Next Record" fields are inserted. The default condition is "True", that is, the condition is always true if you do not change the condition text.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146336	20			0	en-GB	Record number				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3149836	21			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:TP_FLD_DB:ED_DBSETNUMBER\"\>Enter the number of the record that you want to insert when the condition that you specify is met.\</ahelp\> The record number corresponds to the current selection in the data source view. For example, if you select the last 5 records in a database containing 10 records, the number of the first record will be 1, and not 6.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3153305	22			0	en-GB	If you refer to fields in a different database (or in a different table or query within the same database), $[officename] determines the record number relative to the current selection.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156109	23			0	en-GB	Format				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3156122	24			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Select the format of the field that you want to insert. This option is available for numeric, boolean, date and time fields.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150904	25			0	en-GB	From database				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3150922	26			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:TP_FLD_DB:RB_DBOWNFORMAT\"\>Uses the format defined in the selected database.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076E				0	en-GB	Browse				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_idN10772				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"878711313\"\>Opens a file open dialogue box in which you can select a database file (*.odb). The selected file is added to the Databases Selection list.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155084	27			0	en-GB	User-defined				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3154333	28			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:TP_FLD_DB:RB_DBFORMAT\"\>Applies the format that you select in the \<emph\>List of user-defined formats\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146948	29			0	en-GB	List of user-defined formats				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3150093	30			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FLD_DB:LB_DBFORMAT\"\>Lists the available user-defined formats.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_idN107FF				0	en-GB	Printing a form letter				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_idN10803				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>When you print a document that contains database fields, a dialogue box asks you if you want to print a form letter. If you answer Yes, the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/01150000.xhp\"\>Mail Merge\</link\> dialogue box opens in which you can select the database records to print.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_idN10812				0	en-GB	Do not show warning again				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_idN10816				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Suppresses this dialogue box from now on. There is no easy way to get it back!\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Special Tags				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154106				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>tags; in $[officename] Writer\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>$[officename] Writer; special HTML tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML;special tags for fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>fields;HTML import and export\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>time fields;HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>date fields;HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>DocInformation fields\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154106	1			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090007.xhp\" name=\"Special Tags\"\>Special Tags\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3153669	3			0	en-GB	When you save a document that contains fields as an HTML document, $[officename] automatically converts date, time, and DocInformation fields to special HTML tags. The field contents are inserted between the opening and closing HTML tags of the converted fields. These special HTML tags do not correspond to standard HTML tags.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3152960	4			0	en-GB	$[officename] Writer fields are identified by the <SDFIELD> tag in an HTML document. The field type, the format, and the name of the special field are included in the opening HTML tag. The format of a field tag that is recognised by an HTML filter depends on the field type.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154570	5			0	en-GB	Date and Time Fields				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3149696	6			0	en-GB	For "Date" and "Time" fields, the TYPE parameter equals DATETIME. The format of the date or the time is specified by the SDNUM parameter, for example, DD:MM:YY for dates, or HH:MM:SS for time.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3155183	7			0	en-GB	For fixed date and time fields, the date or the time is specified by the SDVAL parameter.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3149485	8			0	en-GB	Examples of date and time special HTML tags that are recognised by $[officename] as fields are shown in the following table:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3151257	9			0	en-GB	Fields				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3148970	10			0	en-GB	$[officename] Tag				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3147102	11			0	en-GB	Date is fixed				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3153634	12			0	en-GB	<SDFIELD TYPE=DATETIME SDVAL="35843,4239988426" SDNUM="1031;1031;DD/MM/YY">17/02/98</SDFIELD>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3155137	13			0	en-GB	Date is variable				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3156275	14			0	en-GB	<SDFIELD TYPE=DATETIME SDNUM="1031;1031;DD/MM/YY">17/02/98</SDFIELD>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3145774	15			0	en-GB	Time is fixed				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3155915	16			0	en-GB	<SDFIELD TYPE=DATETIME SDVAL="35843,4240335648" SDNUM="1031;1031;HH:MM:SS">10:10:36</SDFIELD>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3150110	17			0	en-GB	Time is variable				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3155862	18			0	en-GB	<SDFIELD TYPE=DATETIME SDNUM="1031;1031;HH:MM:SS">10:10:36</SDFIELD>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147409	23			0	en-GB	DocInformation Fields				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3147487	24			0	en-GB	For DocInformation fields, the TYPE parameter equals DOCINFO. The SUBTYPE parameter displays the specific field type, for example, for the "Created" DocInformation field, SUBTYPE=CREATE. For date and time DocInformation fields, the FORMAT parameter equals DATE or TIME, and the SDNUM parameter indicates the number format that is used. The SDFIXED parameter indicates if the content of the DocInformation field is fixed or not.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3147501	25			0	en-GB	The contents of a fixed date or time field are equal to the SDVAL parameter, otherwise the contents are equal to the text found between the SDFIELD HTML tags.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3149562	26			0	en-GB	Examples of DocInformation special HTML tags that are recognised by $[officename] as fields are shown in the following table:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3147738	27			0	en-GB	Fields				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3146334	28			0	en-GB	$[officename] Tag				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3149846	29			0	en-GB	Description (fixed content)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3148863	30			0	en-GB	<SDFIELD TYPE=DOCINFO SUBTYPE=COMMENT SDFIXED>Description</SDFIELD>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3151083	31			0	en-GB	Creation date				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3153298	32			0	en-GB	<SDFIELD TYPE=DOCINFO SUBTYPE=CREATE FORMAT=DATE SDNUM="1031;1031;QQ YY">1. Quarter 98</SDFIELD>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3150175	33			0	en-GB	Creation time (fixed content)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3156134	34			0	en-GB	<SDFIELD TYPE=DOCINFO SUBTYPE=CREATE FORMAT=TIME SDVAL="0" SDNUM="1031;1031;HH:MM:SS AM/PM" SDFIXED>03:58:35 PM</SDFIELD>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3155077	35			0	en-GB	Modification date				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3154330	36			0	en-GB	<SDFIELD TYPE=DOCINFO SUBTYPE=CHANGE FORMAT=DATE SDNUM="1031;1031;NN DD MMM, YY">Mo 23 Feb, 98</SDFIELD>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Input Field				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147515	1			0	en-GB	Input Field				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3146041	2			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FLD_INPUT\"\>Inserts a text field that you can open and edit by clicking it in the document.\</ahelp\> You can use input fields for text, or to assign a new value to a variable.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154470	7			0	en-GB	To change the content of an Input Field in a document, click the field, and then edit the text in the lower box of the dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153669	3			0	en-GB	Edit				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154571	4			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:MULTILINEEDIT:DLG_FLD_INPUT:ED_EDIT\"\>The upper box displays the name that you entered in the \<emph\>Reference\</emph\> box of the Input Field on the \<emph\>Functions\</emph\> tab of the \<emph\>Fields\</emph\> dialogue box. The lower box displays the contents of the field.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155897	5			0	en-GB	Next				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149691	6			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:PUSHBUTTON:DLG_FLD_INPUT:PB_NEXT\"\>Jumps to the next input field in the document.\</ahelp\> This button is only available when you position the cursor directly before an input field, and then press Shift+Ctrl+F9.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Defining Conditions				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145828				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>logical expressions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulating conditions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>conditions; in fields and sections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>fields;defining conditions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sections;defining conditions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>variables; in conditions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>user data;in conditions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases;in conditions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding; database fields\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145828	1			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"defining_conditions\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090200.xhp\"\>Defining Conditions\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145242	13			0	en-GB	Conditions are logical expressions that you can use to control the display of \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\"\>fields\</link\> and \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04020000.xhp\"\>sections\</link\> in your document. Although the following examples apply to fields, they also apply to sections.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147171	93			0	en-GB	You can define conditions for the following field types:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151185	14			0	en-GB	Conditional text: displays text A if the condition is true, or text B if the condition is false.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149289	15			0	en-GB	Hidden text: hides the content of the field if the condition is true.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145412	16			0	en-GB	Hidden paragraph: hides the paragraph if the condition is true.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147515	17			0	en-GB	Any record and next record: controls the access to database records.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149802	18			0	en-GB	The simplest way to define a condition is to type the logical expression directly in a \<emph\>Condition\</emph\> box using the following values:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153677	19			0	en-GB	TRUE				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152960	20			0	en-GB	The condition is always met. You can also enter any value not equal to 0 as the conditional text.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155900	21			0	en-GB	FALSE				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154191	22			0	en-GB	The condition is not met. You can also enter the value 0.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147090	23			0	en-GB	If you leave the \<emph\>Condition\</emph\> box empty, the condition is interpreted as not being met.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148980	24			0	en-GB	When you define a condition, use the same \<link href=\"text/swriter/02/14020000.xhp\"\>elements\</link\> for defining a formula, namely comparative operators, mathematical and statistical functions, number formats, variables and constants.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153638	25			0	en-GB	You can use the following types of variables when you define a condition:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155135	27			0	en-GB	Predefined \<link href=\"text/swriter/02/14020000.xhp\"\>$[officename] variables\</link\> that use statistics on document properties				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156273	26			0	en-GB	Custom variables, that are a created with the "Set variable" field				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149174	94			0	en-GB	Variables based on user data				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145781	28			0	en-GB	Variables based on the contents of database fields				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155916	29			0	en-GB	You cannot use internal variables, such as page and chapter numbers, in condition expression.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151375	30			0	en-GB	Conditions and Variables				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150122	31			0	en-GB	The following examples use a variable called "x":				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147417	32			0	en-GB	x == 1 or x EQ 1				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147500	33			0	en-GB	The condition is true if "x" is equal to 1.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145259	34			0	en-GB	x != 1 or x NEQ 1				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150551	35			0	en-GB	The condition is true if "x" does not equal 1.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147749	36			0	en-GB	sinx == 0				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146345	37			0	en-GB	The condition is true if "x" is a multiple of pi.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149846	38			0	en-GB	To use comparative operators with strings, the operands must be bounded by double quotation marks:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151078	39			0	en-GB	x == "ABC" or x EQ "ABC"				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150162	40			0	en-GB	Checks if variable "x" contains (true) the "ABC" string, or not (false).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153301	41			0	en-GB	x == "" or x EQ ""				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156120	90			0	en-GB	or				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156133	42			0	en-GB	!x or NOT x				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156112	44			0	en-GB	Checks if the variable "x" contains an empty string.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150097	45			0	en-GB	The "equal" comparative operator must be represented by two equal signs (==) in a condition. For example, if you define a variable "x" with the value of 1, you can enter the condition as x==1.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148791	95			0	en-GB	User Data				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150028	96			0	en-GB	You can include user data when you define conditions. To change your user data, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - User data\</emph\>. User data must be entered in the form of strings. You can query the user data with "==" (EQ), "!=" (NEQ), or "!"(NOT).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153124	97			0	en-GB	The following table lists user data variables and their meanings:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149632	130			0	en-GB	Variable				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150662	131			0	en-GB	Meaning				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154026	98			0	en-GB	user_firstname				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149953	99			0	en-GB	Forename				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147272	100			0	en-GB	user_lastname				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149601	101			0	en-GB	Surname				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150770	102			0	en-GB	user_initials				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155529	103			0	en-GB	Initials				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148705	104			0	en-GB	user_company				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148728	105			0	en-GB	Company				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155361	106			0	en-GB	user_street				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154222	107			0	en-GB	Street				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145108	108			0	en-GB	user_country				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146885	109			0	en-GB	Country				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149580	110			0	en-GB	user_zipcode				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156241	111			0	en-GB	Postcode				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148922	112			0	en-GB	user_city				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148945	113			0	en-GB	Post town				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156053	114			0	en-GB	user_title				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3159219	115			0	en-GB	Title				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156435	116			0	en-GB	user_position				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145178	117			0	en-GB	Position				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150797	118			0	en-GB	user_tel_work				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150820	119			0	en-GB	Business telephone number				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150894	120			0	en-GB	user_tel_home				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155320	121			0	en-GB	Home telephone number				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154400	122			0	en-GB	user_fax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153363	123			0	en-GB	Fax number				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153390	124			0	en-GB	user_email				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154948	125			0	en-GB	E-mail address				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145603	126			0	en-GB	user_state				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150129	127			0	en-GB	State (not in all $[officename] versions)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150147	128			0	en-GB	For example, to hide a paragraph, text, or a section from a user with a specific initial, such as "LM", enter the condition: user_initials=="LM".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154115	46			0	en-GB	Conditions and Database Fields				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154128	47			0	en-GB	You can define conditions for accessing databases, or database fields. For example, you can check the content of a database field from a condition, or use database fields in logical expressions. The following table lists a few more examples of using databases in conditions:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156066	132			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156088	133			0	en-GB	Meaning				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155948	48			0	en-GB	Database.Table.Company				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148673	91			0	en-GB	Database.Table.Company NEQ ""				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148687	92			0	en-GB	Database.Table.Company != ""				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155373	49			0	en-GB	The condition is true if the COMPANY field is not empty. (In the first example, no operator is required.)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149977	7			0	en-GB	!Database.Table.Company				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149991	129			0	en-GB	NOT Database.Table.Company				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150004	50			0	en-GB	Database.Table.Company EQ ""				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146911	9			0	en-GB	Database.Table.Company ==""				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148733	8			0	en-GB	Returns TRUE if the COMPANY field is empty.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148762	5			0	en-GB	Database.Table.Company !="Sun"				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153016	149			0	en-GB	Database.Table.Company NEQ "Sun"				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153040	6			0	en-GB	Returns TRUE if the current entry in the COMPANY field is not "Sun". (Exclamation sign represents a logical NOT.)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154605	51			0	en-GB	Database.Table.Forename AND Database.Table.Surname				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153059	52			0	en-GB	Returns TRUE if the record contains the forename and the surname.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3159247	53			0	en-GB	Note the difference between the boolean NOT "!" and the comparative operator not equal "!=" (NEQ).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876	54			0	en-GB	When you refer to a database field in a condition, use the form Databasename.Tablename.Fieldname. If one of the names contains a character that is an operator, such as a minus sign (-), enclose the name in square brackets, for example, Databasename.[Table-name].Fieldname. Never use spaces inside field names.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153891	55			0	en-GB	Example: Hiding an Empty Database Field				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150051	56			0	en-GB	You may want to create a condition that hides an empty field, for example, if the COMPANY field is empty for some of the data records.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150067	57			0	en-GB	Select the \<emph\>Hidden Paragraph\</emph\> list entry, and type the following condition: Addressbook.Addresses.Company EQ ""				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147110	150			0	en-GB	or type the following				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147123	151			0	en-GB	NOT Addressbook.Addresses.Company				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147136	152			0	en-GB	If the COMPANY database field is empty, the condition is true and the paragraph is hidden.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150232	58			0	en-GB	To display hidden paragraphs on the screen, you can choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</emph\>, and unmark the \<emph\>Fields: Hidden paragraphs\</emph\> check box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145218	59			0	en-GB	Examples of Conditions in Fields				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145231	60			0	en-GB	The following examples use the Conditional text field, although they can be applied to any fields that can be linked to a condition. The syntax used for conditions is also used for the Hidden text, Hidden paragraph, Any record or Next record fields.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150311	61			0	en-GB	To display conditional text based on the number of pages:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150333	136			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Functions\</emph\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147471	62			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, click "Conditional text".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154294	63			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Condition\</emph\> box, type "page == 1".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319	64			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Then\</emph\> box, type "There is only one page".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150640	65			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Or\</emph\> box, type "There are several pages".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153086	137			0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155814	67			0	en-GB	To display conditional text based on a user-defined Variable				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155836	138			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Variables\</emph\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155109	68			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, click "Set Variable".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008	139			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box, type "Profit".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147032	140			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Value\</emph\> box, type "5000".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152974	141			0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152998	70			0	en-GB	Click the \<emph\>Functions\</emph\> tab, and click "Conditional text" in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150952	142			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Condition\</emph\> box, type "Profit < 5000".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156291	71			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Then\</emph\> box, type "Target is not met".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156317	72			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Or\</emph\> box, type "Target is met".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366	143			0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154389	73			0	en-GB	To edit the contents of the "Profit" variable, double-click the variable field.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155573	74			0	en-GB	To display conditional text based on the content of a database field:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155587	144			0	en-GB	The first part of this example inserts a space between the "Forename" and "Surname" fields in a document, and the second part inserts text based on the content of a field. This example requires that an address data source is registered with $[officename].				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150523	145			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Database\</emph\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148811	75			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, click "Mail merge fields".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148841	76			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Database selection\</emph\> box, double-click an address book, click "Forename", and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>. Repeat for "Surname".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147549	78			0	en-GB	In the document, place the cursor between the two fields, press Space, and then return to the \<emph\>Fields\</emph\> dialogue box:				20130618 17:22:18
