helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147404	15			0	en-GB	When you apply automatic formats, the following rules apply:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155625	3			0	en-GB	AutoCorrect for Headings				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154505	4			0	en-GB	A paragraph is formatted as a heading when the following conditions are met:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145241	19			0	en-GB	paragraph begins with a capital letter				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148386	20			0	en-GB	paragraph does not end with a punctuation mark				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150564	21			0	en-GB	empty paragraph above and below the paragraph				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149030	8			0	en-GB	AutoCorrect for Bullets / Numbering				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156316	9			0	en-GB	To create a bulleted list, type a hyphen (-), star (*), or plus sign (+), followed by a space or tab at the beginning of a paragraph.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150763	18			0	en-GB	To create a numbered list, type a number followed by a full stop (.), followed by a space or tab at the beginning of a paragraph.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147507	16			0	en-GB	Automatic numbering is only applied to paragraphs formatted with the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\>, \<emph\>Text body\</emph\> or \<emph\>Text body indent\</emph\> paragraph styles.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152941	10			0	en-GB	AutoCorrect for Separator Lines				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154105	11			0	en-GB	If you type three or more hyphens (---), underscores (___) or equal signs (===) on line and then press Enter, the paragraph is replaced by a horizontal line as wide as the page. The line is actually the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030500.xhp\" name=\"lower border\"\>lower border\</link\> of the preceding paragraph. The following rules apply:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153530	12			0	en-GB	Three hyphens (-) yield a single line (0.05 pt thick, gap 0.75 mm).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154477	13			0	en-GB	Three underscore (_) yield a single line (1 pt thick, gap 0.75 mm).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150982	14			0	en-GB	Three equal signs (=) yield a double line (1.10 pt thick, gap 0.75 mm).				20130618 17:22:18
