helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154657	1			0	en-GB	Hyphenation				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148572	2			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"silben\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Inserts hyphens in words that are too long to fit at the end of a line.\</ahelp\> $[officename] searches the document and suggests hyphenation that you can accept or reject. If text is selected, the Hyphenation dialogue box works on the selected text only. If no text is selected, the Hyphenation dialogue box works on the whole document.\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153811	3			0	en-GB	To automatically hyphenate the current or selected paragraphs, choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph\</emph\>, and then click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05030200.xhp\" name=\"Text Flow\"\>Text Flow\</link\> tab. You can also apply automatic hyphenation to a paragraph style. In text where automatic hyphenation is enabled, the Hyphenation dialogue box will not find any word to hyphenate.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151389	5			0	en-GB	When $[officename] finds a word that requires hyphenation, do one of the following options:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155622	36			0	en-GB	To accept the hyphenation of the displayed word, click \<emph\>Hyphenate\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154558	37			0	en-GB	To change the hyphenation of the displayed word, click the left or right arrow below the word, and then click \<emph\>Hyphenate\</emph\>. The left and right buttons are enabled for words with multiple hyphenation points.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150017	38			0	en-GB	To reject the hyphenation of the displayed word, click \<emph\>Skip\</emph\>. This word will not be hyphenated.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150018	38			0	en-GB	To automatically hyphenate the remaining part of the selection or the document, click \<emph\>Hyphenate All\</emph\> and answer "Yes" to the following question.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150019	38			0	en-GB	To end hyphenation, click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>. The hyphenation that is applied already will not be reverted. You can use \<emph\>Edit - Undo\</emph\> to undo all hyphenation that was applied while the Hyphenation dialogue box was open.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147562	19			0	en-GB	To exclude paragraphs from the automatic hyphenation, select the paragraphs, choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph\</emph\>, click the Text Flow tab, and then unmark the \<emph\>Automatically\</emph\> check box in the Hyphenation area.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154276	18			0	en-GB	To disable the Hyphenation dialogue box and always hyphenate automatically, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010400.xhp\" name=\"Language Settings - Writing Aids\"\>Language Settings - Writing Aids\</link\>\</emph\>, and mark the \<emph\>Hyphenate without inquiry\</emph\> check box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152950	17			0	en-GB	To manually enter a hyphen directly in the document, click in the word into which you want to add the hyphen, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Minus sign (-).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147523	32			0	en-GB	To insert a non-breaking (protected) hyphen directly in the document, click in the word that you want to hyphenate, and then press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>+Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Minus sign(-).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154573	33			0	en-GB	To hide custom hyphens, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040600.xhp\" name=\"Text Document - Formatting Aids\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</link\>\</emph\>, and then unmark the \<emph\>Custom hyphens\</emph\> check box.				20130618 17:22:18
