helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148388	4			0	en-GB	A separator, such as a tab, marks the column boundaries in the selected text. Each paragraph in the selection is converted into a row in the table. Similarly, when you convert a table into text, the column markers are changed to the character that you specify, and each row is converted into a separate paragraph.				20130618 17:22:18
