helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3004547				0	en-GB	The open, low, high, and closing values of a row build together one data unit in the chart. A stock price data series consists of several rows containing such data units. The column containing the transaction volume builds an optional second data series.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id6401867				0	en-GB	Depending on the chosen variant, you do not need all columns.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id18616				0	en-GB	Stock Chart Variants				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id6138492				0	en-GB	Choose the \<emph\>Stock\</emph\> chart type on the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart wizard\</link\>. Then select one of the four variants.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id4569231				0	en-GB	Type 1				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id291451				0	en-GB	Based on \<emph\>low\</emph\> \<emph\>and high\</emph\> columns, Type 1 shows the distance between bottom price (low) and top price (high) by a vertical line.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3341776				0	en-GB	Based on \<emph\>low, high\</emph\> and \<emph\>close\</emph\> columns, Type 1 shows an additional horizontal mark for the closing price.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id5947141				0	en-GB	Type 2				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id1911679				0	en-GB	Based on \<emph\>open, low, high\</emph\>, and \<emph\>close\</emph\> columns, Type 2 generates the traditional "candle stick" chart. Type 2 draws the vertical line between the bottom and top price and adds a rectangle in front, which visualises the range between the opening and closing price. If you click on the rectangle you will see more information in the status bar. %PRODUCTNAME uses different fill colours for rising values (the opening price is lower than the closing price) and falling values.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id9364909				0	en-GB	Type 3				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id4473403				0	en-GB	Based on \<emph\>volume, low, high\</emph\>, and \<emph\>close\</emph\> columns, Type 3 draws a chart like Type 1, with additional columns for the transaction volume.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id4313791				0	en-GB	Type 4				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id4331797				0	en-GB	Based on all five data columns \<emph\>volume, open, low, high\</emph\>, and \<emph\>close\</emph\>, Type 4 combines a chart of Type 2 with a column chart for the transaction volume.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id4191717				0	en-GB	Because measurement for transaction volume might be "units", a second y-axis is introduced in chart Type 3 and Type 4. The price axis is shown on the right side and the volume axis on the left side.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id2318796				0	en-GB	Setting the Data Source				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id399182				0	en-GB	Charts based on its own data				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id5298318				0	en-GB	To change the data series of a chart having its own data, choose \<link href=\"text/schart/01/03010000.xhp\"\>Chart Data Table\</link\> from the View menu or from the context menu of the chart in edit mode.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id7588732				0	en-GB	In an embedded chart data table, the data series are always organised in columns.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id95828				0	en-GB	For a new stock chart first use a column chart. Add the columns you need and enter your data in the order shown in the example, omitting any columns not required for the desired variant. Use Move Series Right to change the column order. Close the chart data table. Now use the Chart Type dialogue box to change to the stock chart variant. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id6182744				0	en-GB	If you have already got a stock chart and you want to change the variant, then first change the chart type to a column chart, add or remove columns so that it fits to the variant, and then change the chart type back to a stock chart.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3496200				0	en-GB	Do not write the name of a data series in a row. Write the name into the field above the role name.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id7599108				0	en-GB	The order of the rows determines how the categories are arranged in the chart. Use Move Row Down to change the order.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id888698				0	en-GB	Charts based on Calc or Writer tables				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3394573				0	en-GB	You can choose or alter a data range on the second page of the Chart wizard or in the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_data_range.xhp\"\>Data Range\</link\> dialogue box. For fine tuning use the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_data_series.xhp\"\>Data Series\</link\> dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id7594225				0	en-GB	To specify a data range do one of the following:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id5081637				0	en-GB	Enter the data range in the text box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id9759514				0	en-GB	In Calc, an example data range would be "$Sheet1.$B$3:$B$14". Note that a data range may consist of more than one region in a spreadsheet, e.g. "$Sheet1.A1:A5;$Sheet1.D1:D5" is also a valid data range. In Writer, an example data range would be "Table1.A1:E4".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id1614429				0	en-GB	As long as the syntax is not correct, %PRODUCTNAME shows the text in red.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id1589098				0	en-GB	In Calc, click \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> to minimise the dialogue box, then drag to select the data range. When you release the mouse, the data are entered. Click \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> again to add a data range. In the input field of the minimised dialogue box, click after the entry and type a semicolon. Then drag to select the next range.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id8746910				0	en-GB	Click one of the options for data series in rows or in columns. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id9636524				0	en-GB	Your stock chart data are "in columns", if the information in a row belongs to the same "candle stick".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id5675527				0	en-GB	Fine Tuning the Data Ranges of Table Based Stock Charts				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3486434				0	en-GB	You can organise data series and edit the source for parts of single data series on the third page of the Chart wizard or on the page Data Series in the Data Range dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id3068636				0	en-GB	Organise Data Series				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id2480849				0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>data series\</emph\> area on the left side of the dialogue box, you can organise the data series of the actual chart. A stock chart has at least one data series containing the prices. It might have a second data series for transaction volume.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id4181951				0	en-GB	If you have more than one price data series, use the Up and Down arrow buttons to order them. The order determines the arrangement in the chart. Do the same for volume data series. You cannot switch price and volume data series.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id2927335				0	en-GB	To remove a data series, select the data series in the list and click \<emph\>Remove\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id2107303				0	en-GB	To add a data series, select one of the existing data series and click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>. You get an empty entry below the selected one, which has the same type. If you have no price data series or no volume data series, you must first select a range for these series in the \<emph\>Data Range\</emph\> dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id4071779				0	en-GB	Setting Data Ranges				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id7844477				0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Data Ranges\</emph\> dialogue box you can set or change the data range of each component of the selected data series.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id6478469				0	en-GB	In the upper list you will see the role name of the components and the current values. When you have selected a role, you can change the value in the text box below the list. The label shows the selected role.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id9038972				0	en-GB	Enter the range into the text box or click on \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> to minimise the dialogue box and select the range with the mouse.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id7985168				0	en-GB	Select Open Values, Close Values, High Values, and Low Values in any order. Specify only the ranges for those roles which you need for the chosen variant of the stock chart. The ranges need not be next to each other in the table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id876186				0	en-GB	Legend				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3939634				0	en-GB	The legend displays the labels from the first row or column or from the special range that you have set in the \<emph\>Data Series\</emph\> dialogue box. If your chart does not contain labels, the legend displays text like "Row 1, Row 2, ...", or "Column A, Column B, ..." according to the row number or column letter of the chart data.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id2377697				0	en-GB	The legend shows the value from the range, which you entered in the \<emph\>Range for Name\</emph\> field in the \<emph\>Data Range\</emph\> dialogue box. The default entry is the column header of the closing price column.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id2188787				0	en-GB	Select one of the position options. When the chart is finished, you can specify other positions using the Format menu.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Chart Type X-Y				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	bm_id84231				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>scatter charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>X-Y charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chart types;X-Y (scatter)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>error indicators in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>error bars in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>averages in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>statistics in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>variances in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>standard deviation in charts\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id9346598				0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"type_xy\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_xy.xhp\"\>Chart Type X-Y (Scatter)\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id2003845				0	en-GB	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id7757194				0	en-GB	X-Y (Scatter)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id5977965				0	en-GB	An X-Y chart in its basic form is based on one data series consisting of a name, a list of x‑values, and a list of y‑values. Each value pair (x|y) is shown as a point in a coordinate system. The name of the data series is associated with the y‑values and shown in the legend.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id4381847				0	en-GB	Choose an X-Y chart for the following example tasks:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id1336710				0	en-GB	scale the x‑axis				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id1221655				0	en-GB	generate a parametric curve, for example a spiral				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id3397320				0	en-GB	draw the graph of a function				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id7657399				0	en-GB	explore the statistical association of quantitative variables				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id8925138				0	en-GB	Your X-Y chart may have more than one data series.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id5461897				0	en-GB	X-Y Chart Variants				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id8919339				0	en-GB	You can choose an X-Y chart variant on the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\>, or by choosing \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Chart Type \</item\>for a chart in edit mode.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id4634235				0	en-GB	The chart is created with default settings. After the chart is finished, you can edit its properties to change the appearance. Line styles and icons can be changed on the \<emph\>Line\</emph\>tab page of the data series properties dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id5482039				0	en-GB	Double-click any data point to open the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data Series\</item\> dialogue box. In this dialogue box, you can change many properties of the data series.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id0805200810492449				0	en-GB	For 2-D charts, you can choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - y-Error Bars\</item\> to enable the display of error bars.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id6221198				0	en-GB	You can enable the display of mean value lines and trend lines using commands on the Insert menu.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id1393475				0	en-GB	Points only				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id6571550				0	en-GB	Each data point is shown by an icon. %PRODUCTNAME uses default icons with different forms and colours for each data series. The default colours are set in \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Charts - Default Colours\</item\>. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id5376140				0	en-GB	Lines Only				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id4408093				0	en-GB	This variant draws straight lines from one data point to the next. The data points are not shown by icons. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id7261268				0	en-GB	The drawing order is the same as the order in the data series. Mark \<emph\>Sort by x-values\</emph\> to draw the lines in the order of the x-values. This sorting applies only to the chart, not to the data in the table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id6949369				0	en-GB	Points and Lines				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id9611499				0	en-GB	This variant shows points and lines at the same time.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id6765953				0	en-GB	3-D Lines				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id7422711				0	en-GB	The lines are shown like tapes. The data points are not shown by icons. In the finished chart choose \<link href=\"text/schart/01/three_d_view.xhp\"\>3-D View\</link\> to set properties like illumination and angle of view.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id239265				0	en-GB	Smooth Lines				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id7957396				0	en-GB	Mark \<emph\>Smooth Lines\</emph\> to draw curves instead of straight line segments.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id1202124				0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> to set details for the curves.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id5989562				0	en-GB	\<emph\>Cubic spline\</emph\> interpolates your data points with polynomials of degree 3. The transitions between the polynomial pieces are smooth, having the same slope and curvature. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id6128421				0	en-GB	The \<emph\>Resolution\</emph\> determines how many line segments are calculated to draw a piece of polynomial between two data points. You can see the intermediate points if you click any data point.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id9280373				0	en-GB	\<emph\>B-spline\</emph\> uses the data points as control points to form a B-spline curve. Those curves are built piecewise from polynomials. The \<emph\>Data points order\</emph\> sets the degree k of these polynomials. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Chart Wizard - Chart Elements				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	hd_id70802				0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"wiz_chart_elements\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_elements.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard - Chart Elements\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id8746604				0	en-GB	On this page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose the chart elements to be shown.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id6437269				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter a title for your chart.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id9469893				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter a subtitle for your chart.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id130008				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter a label for the x-axis (horizontal).\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id5821710				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter a label for the y-axis (vertical).\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id2871791				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter a label for the z-axis. This option is only available for three-dimensional charts.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id7333597				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Displays a legend in your chart.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id9976195				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Positions the legend to the left of the chart.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id2507400				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Positions the legend to the top of the chart.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id216681				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Positions the legend to the right of the chart.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id7709585				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Positions the legend to the bottom of the chart.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id4309518				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Displays grid lines that are perpendicular to the x-axis.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id206610				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Displays grid lines that are perpendicular to the y-axis.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id6917020				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Displays grid lines that are perpendicular to the z-axis. This option is only available for three-dimensional charts.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id9969481				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter a label for the secondary x-axis. This option is only available for charts that support a secondary x-axis.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id816675				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter a label for the secondary y-axis. This option is only available for charts that support a secondary y-axis.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	hd_id4411145				0	en-GB	To enter chart elements				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id3274941				0	en-GB	Enter titles or click the elements that you want to be shown on the current chart.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	hd_id9804681				0	en-GB	Titles				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id3614917				0	en-GB	If you enter some text for a title, subtitle, or any axis, the necessary space will be reserved to display the text next to the chart. If you do not enter any text, no space will be reserved, leaving more space to display the chart.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id156865				0	en-GB	It is not possible to link the title text to a cell. You must enter the text directly.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id6034424				0	en-GB	When the chart is finished, you can change the position and other properties by the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> menu.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id9033783				0	en-GB	Legend				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id1069368				0	en-GB	The legend displays the labels from the first row or column, or from the range that you have set in the Data Series dialogue box. If your chart does not contain labels, the legend displays text like "Row 1, Row 2, ...", or "Column A, Column B, ..." according to the row number or column letter of the chart data.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id6998809				0	en-GB	You cannot enter the text directly, it is automatically generated from the Name cell range.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id71413				0	en-GB	Select one of the position options. When the chart is finished, you can specify other positions using the Format menu.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id4776757				0	en-GB	Grids				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id6737876				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Displays grid lines that are perpendicular to the x-axis.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id1058992				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Displays grid lines that are perpendicular to the y-axis.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id7366557				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Displays grid lines that are perpendicular to the z-axis. This option is only available for three-dimensional charts.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id6527298				0	en-GB	The visible grid lines can help to estimate the data values in the chart.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id2924283				0	en-GB	The distance of the grid lines corresponds to the interval settings in the Scale tab of the axis properties.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id5781731				0	en-GB	Grid lines are not available for pie charts.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	hd_id6942045				0	en-GB	Additional elements				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id4721823				0	en-GB	For additional elements use the Insert menu of the chart in edit mode. There you can define the following elements:				20130618 17:22:18
