helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id9719229				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enables a 3-D look for the data values.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id3860896				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select the type of 3-D look.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id4041871				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a shape from the list.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id9930722				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Displays stacked series for Line charts.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id5749687				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Stack series display values on top of each other.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id79348				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Stack series display values as percent.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id2414014				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The lines are shown as curves.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id7617114				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens a dialogue box to set the curve properties.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id6649372				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Connects points by ascending x-values, even if the order of values is different, in an X-Y scatter diagram.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id7334208				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Set the number of lines for the Column and Line chart type.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id4485000				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens the Chart Type dialogue box.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Chart Wizard - Data Range				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	bm_id2429578				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>data ranges in charts\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	hd_id8313852				0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"wiz_data_range\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_data_range.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard - Data Range\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id8829309				0	en-GB	On this page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can select one single source of data range. This range may consist of more than one rectangular range of cells.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id6401867				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens the Data Ranges dialogue box in which you can edit Data Range and Data Series.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id2025818				0	en-GB	Use the Chart Wizard - Data Series page if you need more control over the data ranges.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id8466139				0	en-GB	This dialogue box is only available for charts based on a Calc or Writer table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	hd_id1877193				0	en-GB	To specify a data range				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id5924863				0	en-GB	Select the data range. Do one of the following:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id4357432				0	en-GB	Enter the data range in the text box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id5626392				0	en-GB	In Calc, an example data range would be "$Sheet1.$B$3:$B$14". Note that a data range may consist of more than one region in a spreadsheet, e.g. "$Sheet1.A1:A5;$Sheet1.D1:D5" is also a valid data range. In Writer, an example data range would be "Table1.A1:E4".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id1363872				0	en-GB	In Calc, click \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> to minimise the dialogue box, then dragover a cell area  to select the data range.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id6823938				0	en-GB	If you want a data range of multiple cell areas that are not next to each other, enter the first range, then manually add a semicolon at the end of the text box, then enter the other ranges. Use a semicolon as delimiter between ranges.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id1434369				0	en-GB	Click one of the options for data series in rows or in columns.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id7524033				0	en-GB	Check whether the data range has labels in the first row or in the first column or both.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id5256508				0	en-GB	In the preview you can see how the final chart will look.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id379650				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the data range that you want to include in your chart. To minimise this dialogue box while you select the data range in Calc, click the \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> button.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id953703				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Data series obtain their data from consecutive rows in the selected range. For scatter charts, the first data series will contain x-values for all series. All other data series are used as y-values, one for each series.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id4496597				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Data series obtain their data from consecutive columns in the selected range. For scatter charts, the first data column will contain x-values for all series. All other data columns are used as y-values, one for each series.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id2898953				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>For data series in columns: The first row in the range is used as names for data series. For data series in rows: The first row in the range is used as categories. The remaining rows comprise the data series. If this check box is not marked, all rows are data series.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id7546311				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>For data series in columns: The first column in the range is used as names for data series. For data series in rows: The first column in the range is used as categories. The remaining columns comprise the data columns. If this check box is not marked, all columns are data columns.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Chart Wizard - Data Series				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	bm_id8641621				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>order of chart data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data series\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	hd_id6124149				0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"wiz_data_series\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_data_series.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard - Data Series\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id9651478				0	en-GB	On this page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can change the source range of all data series separately, including their labels. You can also change the range of the categories. You can first select the data range on the Data Range page and then remove unnecessary data series or add data series from other cells here.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id6326487				0	en-GB	If there seem to be too many options on this page, just define the data range on the Chart Wizard - Data Range page and skip this page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id686361				0	en-GB	This dialogue box is only available for charts based on a Calc or Writer table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	hd_id9241615				0	en-GB	Organising data series				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id7159337				0	en-GB	In the Data Series list box you will see a list of all data series in the current chart.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id4921720				0	en-GB	To organise the data series, select an entry in the list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id6627094				0	en-GB	Click Add to add another data series below the selected entry. The new data series has the same type as the selected entry.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id2926419				0	en-GB	Click Remove to remove the selected entry from the Data Series list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id4443800				0	en-GB	Use the Up and Down arrow buttons to move the selected entry in the list up or down. This does not change the order in the data source table, but changes only the arrangement in the chart.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	hd_id9777520				0	en-GB	Editing data series				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id1474654				0	en-GB	Click an entry in the list to view and edit the properties for that entry.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id4855189				0	en-GB	In the Data Ranges list box you will see the role names and cell ranges of the data series components. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id9475081				0	en-GB	Click an entry, then edit the contents in the text box below. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id4695272				0	en-GB	The label next to the text box states the currently selected role. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3931699				0	en-GB	Enter the range or click \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> to minimise the dialogue box and select the range with the mouse.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id8626667				0	en-GB	If you want a data range of multiple cell areas that are not next to each other, enter the first range, then manually add a semicolon at the end of the text box, then enter the other ranges. Use a semicolon as delimiter between ranges.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id5971556				0	en-GB	The range for a data role, like y-Values, must not include a label cell.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	hd_id7622608				0	en-GB	Editing categories or data labels				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id9222693				0	en-GB	Enter or select a cell range that will be used as text for categories or data labels. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id9500106				0	en-GB	Depending on the chart type, the text strings are shown on the x-axis or as data labels. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id5201879				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows a list of all data series in the chart. Click an entry to view and edit that data series. Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> to insert a new series into the list after the selected entry.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id2571794				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows all the data ranges used by the data series that is selected in the Data Series list box. Each data range shows the role name and the source range address.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id2254402				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows the source range address from the second column of the Data Range list box. You can change the range in the text box or by dragging in the document. To minimise this dialogue box while you select the data range in Calc, click the \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> button.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id2419507				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows the source range address of the categories (the text strings that you can see on the x-axis of a category chart). For an X-Y chart, the text box contains the source range of the data labels which are displayed for the data points. To minimise this dialogue box while you select the data range in Calc, click the \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> button.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id1091647				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Adds a new entry below the current entry in the Data Series list. If an entry is selected, the new data series gets the same chart type.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id8831446				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Removes the selected entry from the Data Series list.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id7022309				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Moves up the selected entry in the Data Series list.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id2844019				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Moves down the selected entry in the Data Series list.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
