helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3145802	2			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_ATTRIBUTES_CAT\"\>You can choose from various attributes for \<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME\</emph\> \<emph\>Math\</emph\> formulae. Some attributes are displayed in the lower part of the Formula Elements window.\</ahelp\> These attributes are also listed in the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000001.xhp#kontextmenue\" name=\"context menu\"\>context menu\</link\> of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window. All attributes not contained in the Formula Elements window or in the context menu must be typed manually in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3155962	3			0	en-GB	The following is a complete list of all attributes available in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Math. The symbol next to the attribute indicates that it can be accessed through the Formula Elements window (choose \<emph\>View - Formula Elements\</emph\>) or through the context menu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149604	4			0	en-GB	In describing the following attribute functions, the letter "a" in the icon refers to the placeholder that you would like to assign to the respective attribute. You can substitute this character with any other character that you choose.				20130618 17:22:18
