helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151075	1			0	en-GB	Edit Symbols				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154513	2			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_MODALDIALOG_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG\"\>Use this dialogue box to add symbols to a symbol set, to edit symbol sets, or to modify symbol notations.\</ahelp\> You can also define new symbol sets, assign names to symbols, or to modify existing symbol sets.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146066	3			0	en-GB	Old Symbol				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153965	4			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_COMBOBOX_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_1\"\>Select the name of the current symbol.\</ahelp\> The symbol, the name of the symbol, and the set that the symbol belongs to are displayed in the left preview pane at the bottom of the dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154020	7			0	en-GB	Old Symbol Set				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150209	8			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_COMBOBOX_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_2\"\>This list box contains the name of the current symbol set. If you want, you can also select a different symbol set.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145386	23			0	en-GB	Symbol				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148870	25			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_COMBOBOX_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_4\"\>Lists the names for the symbols in the current symbol set. Select a name from the list or type a name for a newly added symbol.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150215	28			0	en-GB	Adding a New Symbol				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3143233	6			0	en-GB	To add a symbol to a symbol set, select a font in the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> box, and then click a symbol in symbols pane. In the \<emph\>Symbol\</emph\> box, type a name for the symbol. In the \<emph\>Symbol set\</emph\> list box, select a symbol set, or type a new name to create a new symbol set. The right preview pane displays the symbol that you selected. Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> and then \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151389	29			0	en-GB	Modifying the Name of a Symbol				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147296	21			0	en-GB	To change the name of a symbol, select the old name in the \<emph\>Old symbol\</emph\> list box. Then enter the new name in the \<emph\>Symbol\</emph\> box. Check that the desired character is in the preview window before you click the \<emph\>Modify\</emph\> button. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157870	24			0	en-GB	Symbol Set				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145825	26			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_COMBOBOX_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_5\"\>The \<emph\>Symbol set\</emph\> list box contains the names of all existing symbol sets. You can modify a symbol set or create a new one.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154554	30			0	en-GB	Creating a New Symbol Set				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145594	22			0	en-GB	To create a new symbol set, type a name for it in the \<emph\>Symbol set\</emph\> list box and add at least one symbol. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to close the dialogue box. The new symbol set is now available under the new name.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153736	10			0	en-GB	Font				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147374	11			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_LISTBOX_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_1\"\>Displays the name of the current font and enables you to select a different font.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150564	32			0	en-GB	Subset				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145295	33			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_LISTBOX_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_LB_FONTS_SUBSET\"\>If you selected a non-symbol font in the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> list box, you can select a Unicode subset in which to place your new or edited symbol. When a subset has been selected, all symbols belonging to this subset of the current symbol set are displayed in the symbols list above.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148386	19			0	en-GB	Typeface				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155366	20			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_COMBOBOX_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_3\"\>The current typeface is displayed. You can change the typeface by selecting one from the list box.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156262	12			0	en-GB	Add				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153922	13			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_1\"\>Click this button to add the symbol shown in the right preview window to the current symbol set.\</ahelp\> It will be saved under the name displayed in the \<emph\>Symbol\</emph\> list box. You must specify a name under \<emph\>Symbol\</emph\> or \<emph\>Symbol Set\</emph\> to be able to use this button. Names cannot be used more than once.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150756	14			0	en-GB	Modify				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147570	15			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_2\"\>Click this button to replace the name of the symbol shown in the left preview window (the old name is displayed in the \<emph\>Old symbol\</emph\> list box) with the new name you have entered in the \<emph\>Symbol\</emph\> list box.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154640	31			0	en-GB	Moving a Symbol to Another Symbol Set				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151174	27			0	en-GB	As an example, to transfer the large ALPHA from the "Greek" set to the "Special" set, select the old set (Greek) and then the ALPHA symbol using the two top list boxes. The symbol appears in the left preview window. In the \<emph\>Symbol set\</emph\> list box, select the "Special" set. Click \<emph\>Modify\</emph\> and then \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The ALPHA symbol is now only in the "Special" symbol set.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145414	16			0	en-GB	Delete				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154258	17			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_3\"\>Click to remove the symbol shown in the left preview window from the current symbol set.\</ahelp\> There will be no security query. Deleting the last remaining symbol of a symbol set also deletes the symbol set.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527	18			0	en-GB	You can also click \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\> at any time to close the dialogue box without saving any of the changes.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Import formula				20130618 17:22:18
