helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	bm_id3125863				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>arranging; objects (guide)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>objects;aligning\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>distributing draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>aligning;draw objects\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863	17			0	en-GB	Arranging Objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3153727	18			0	en-GB	Each object that you place in your document is successively stacked on the preceding object. To rearrange the stacking order of a selected object proceed as follows.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D5				0	en-GB	Click the object that you want to rearrange.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3150327	78			0	en-GB	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\> to bring up the context menu and choose one of the arrange options:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107E6				0	en-GB	\<emph\>Bring to Front\</emph\> places the object on top of all other objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107EC				0	en-GB	\<emph\>Bring Forwards\</emph\> places the object one place forwards in the stack of objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F2				0	en-GB	\<emph\>Send Backwards\</emph\> places the object one place backwards in the stack of objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F8				0	en-GB	\<emph\>Send to Back\</emph\> places the object behind all other objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107FE				0	en-GB	\<emph\>Behind Object\</emph\> places the object behind another object that you select				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155766	79			0	en-GB	Arranging an Object Behind Another Object				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN10811				0	en-GB	Click the object whose position you want to change.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3154253	80			0	en-GB	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\> to open the context menu and choose \<emph\>Behind Object\</emph\>. The mouse pointer changes to a hand.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3149126	81			0	en-GB	Click the object behind which you want to place the selected object.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145789	20			0	en-GB	Reversing The Stacking Order of Two Objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3154022	83			0	en-GB	Shift-click both objects to select them.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3155114	84			0	en-GB	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\> to open the context menu and choose \<emph\>Reverse\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166425	21			0	en-GB	Aligning Objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3152994	22			0	en-GB	The \<emph\>Alignment\</emph\> function enables you to align objects relative to each other or relative to the page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A3				0	en-GB	Select an object to align it to the page or select multiple objects to align them relative to each other.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A7				0	en-GB	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Alignment\</item\> and select one of the alignment options.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108AE				0	en-GB	Distributing Objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3151390	71			0	en-GB	If you select three or more objects in Draw, you can also use the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05360000.xhp\" name=\"Distribution\"\>\<emph\>Distribution\</emph\>\</link\> command to distribute the vertical and horizontal spacing evenly between the objects.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108CE				0	en-GB	Select three or more objects to be distributed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108D2				0	en-GB	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Distribution\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108DA				0	en-GB	Select the horizontal and vertical distribution option and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3150535	72			0	en-GB	Selected objects are distributed evenly along the horizontal or vertical axis. The two outermost objects are used as reference points and do not move when the \<emph\>Distribution\</emph\> command is applied.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Defining Custom Colours				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149263				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>colours; defining and saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>user-defined colours\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>custom colours\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149263	7			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"color_define\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/color_define.xhp\" name=\"Defining Custom Colours\"\>Defining Custom Colours\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3154511	8			0	en-GB	If you want, you can mix a custom colour and add it to a colour table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155600	9			0	en-GB	To define a custom colour				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3150327	25			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Colours\</emph\> tab. A table of the predefined colours is displayed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3154657	13			0	en-GB	Changes made to the standard colour table are permanent and are saved automatically.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3166425	14			0	en-GB	Click a colour in the table that is similar to the one you want to mix. The colour appears in the upper preview box to the right of the table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3152992	15			0	en-GB	Select either the RGB or CMYK colour model in the box below the preview boxes.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id4979705				0	en-GB	%PRODUCTNAME uses only the RGB colour model for printing in colour. The CMYK controls are provided only to ease the input of colour values using CMYK notation.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3152987	16			0	en-GB	The RGB colour model mixes red, green and blue light to create colours on a computer screen. In the RGB model, the three colour components are additive and can have values ranging from 0 (black) to 255 (white). The CMYK colour model combines Cyan (C), Magenta (M), Yellow (Y), and blacK (K, also used for "Key") to create colours for printing. The four colours of the CMYK models are subtractive and are defined as percentages. Black corresponds to 100 % and white to 0 %.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3145386	17			0	en-GB	Enter a numeric value in the boxes next to the colour components. The new colour appears in the preview box directly above the colour model box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3152871	18			0	en-GB	You can also create a colour using a colour spectrum. Click the \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> button to open the \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010501.xhp\" name=\"Colour\"\>\<emph\>Colour\</emph\>\</link\> dialogue box. Click a colour and click OK. Use the Hue, Saturation, and Brightness boxes to adjust your colour selection.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3153011	19			0	en-GB	Do one of the following:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3147244	26			0	en-GB	If you want to replace the colour in the standard colour table that your custom colour is based on, click \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3145116	20			0	en-GB	If you want to add your custom colour to the standard colour table, enter a name in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> text box and click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3145236	23			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/03170000.xhp\" name=\"Colour bar\"\>Colour bar\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
