helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150715	17			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"cross_fading\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/cross_fading.xhp\" name=\"Cross-Fading Two Objects\"\>Cross-Fading Two Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3154754	18			0	en-GB	Cross-fading creates shapes and distributes them by uniform increments between two drawing objects.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3155112	41			0	en-GB	The cross-fading command is only available in $[officename] Draw. You can, however, copy and paste cross-faded objects into $[officename] Impress.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149209	20			0	en-GB	To cross-fade two objects:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3150370	45			0	en-GB	Hold down Shift and click each object.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3166428	22			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Cross-fading\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3156450	44			0	en-GB	Enter a value to specify the number of objects between the start and end of the cross-fade in the \<emph\>Increments\</emph\> box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3149405	23			0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3151240	24			0	en-GB	A group containing the two original objects and the specified number (increments) of cross-faded objects is displayed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3159203				0	en-GB	\<image id=\"img_id3150210\" src=\"res/helpimg/ueberblenden.png\" width=\"74.88mm\" height=\"65.62mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150210\"\>Illustration for cross-fading\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3154766	25			0	en-GB	You can edit the individual objects of a group by selecting the group and pressing F3. Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F3 to exit the group editing mode.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3155760	42			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/02150000.xhp\" name=\"Editing - Cross-fading\"\>Editing - Cross-fading\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Drawing Sectors and Segments				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146974				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>sectors of circles/ellipses\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>segments of circles/ellipses\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>circles; segments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ellipses; segments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawing; sectors and segments\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146974	30			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"draw_sector\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/draw_sector.xhp\" name=\"Drawing Sectors and Segments\"\>Drawing Sectors and Segments\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396	31			0	en-GB	The \<emph\>Ellipse\</emph\> toolbar contains tools for drawing ellipses and circles. You can also draw segments and sectors of circles and ellipses.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151075	32			0	en-GB	To draw a sector of a circle or an ellipse:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335	33			0	en-GB	Open the \<emph\>Ellipses\</emph\> toolbar and click either the \<emph\>Circle Pie\</emph\> or the \<emph\>Ellipse Pie\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3155768\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_circlepie_unfilled.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155768\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>. The mouse pointer changes to a cross hair with a small icon of a sector.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3150199	34			0	en-GB	Position the pointer at the edge of the circle you want to draw and drag to create the circle.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3148868	35			0	en-GB	To create a circle by dragging from the centre, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while dragging.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3145361	36			0	en-GB	Release the mouse button when the circle has reached the size you want. A line corresponding to the circle radius appears in the circle.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3149872	37			0	en-GB	Position the pointer where you want to place the first boundary of the sector and click.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3157871	51			0	en-GB	As the radius line that follows the pointer is constrained to the circle boundaries, you can click anywhere in the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3146874	38			0	en-GB	Position the pointer where you want to place the second boundary of the sector and click. The completed sector is displayed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3148581	41			0	en-GB	To draw a segment of a circle or ellipse, follow the steps for creating a sector based on a circle.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3153084	42			0	en-GB	To draw an arc based on an ellipse, choose one of the arc icons and follow the same steps for creating a sector based on a circle.				20130618 17:22:18
