helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792	3			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"gradient\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/gradient.xhp\" name=\"Creating Gradient Fills\"\>Creating Gradient Fills\</link\> \</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3154012	4			0	en-GB	A gradient fill is an incremental blend of two different colours, or shades of the same colour, that you can apply to a drawing object.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147436	61			0	en-GB	To apply a gradient:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974	5			0	en-GB	Select a drawing object.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3154491	6			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\> and select \<emph\>Gradient\</emph\> as the \<emph\>Fill\</emph\> type.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3153415	7			0	en-GB	Select a gradient style from the list and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154702	8			0	en-GB	Creating Custom Gradients				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3145791	9			0	en-GB	You can define your own gradients and modify existing gradients, as well as save and load a list of gradient files.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145384	62			0	en-GB	To create a custom gradient:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3151242	11			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Gradients\</emph\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3150046	12			0	en-GB	Select a gradient from the list to use as the basis for your new gradient and click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3145116	13			0	en-GB	Type a name for the gradient in the text box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id6535843				0	en-GB	The name appears at the end of the gradient list and is selected for editing.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391	15			0	en-GB	Set the gradient properties and click \<emph\>Modify\</emph\> to save the gradient.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3156396	16			0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>OK.\</emph\> 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149947	40			0	en-GB	Using Gradients and Transparency				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3157905	41			0	en-GB	You can adjust the properties of a gradient as well as the transparency of a drawing object with your mouse.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150653	63			0	en-GB	To adjust the gradient of a drawing object:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3154844	42			0	en-GB	Select a drawing object with the gradient that you want to modify.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3145592	43			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Gradients\</emph\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_idN107BE				0	en-GB	Adjust the values for the gradient to suit your needs and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3150659	46			0	en-GB	To adjust the transparency of an object, select the object, choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Transparency\</emph\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
