helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Grouping Objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150793				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>grouping; draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; grouping\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150793	26			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"groups\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/groups.xhp\" name=\"Grouping Objects\"\>Grouping Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3153728	27			0	en-GB	You can combine several objects into a group so that they act as a single object. You can move and transform all objects in a group as a single unit. You can also change the properties (for example, line size, fill colour) of all objects in a group as a whole or for individual objects in a group. Groups can be temporary or assigned:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434	64			0	en-GB	Temporary - group only lasts as long as all of the combined objects are selected.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490	65			0	en-GB	Assigned - group lasts until it is ungrouped through a menu command.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252	66			0	en-GB	Groups can also be grouped in other groups. Actions applied to a group do not affect the relative position of the individual objects to each other in the group.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150716	28			0	en-GB	To group objects:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018				0	en-GB	\<image id=\"img_id3145643\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formatgroup.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3145643\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147346	29			0	en-GB	Select the objects you want to group and choose \<emph\>Modify - Group\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3148485	30			0	en-GB	For example, you can group all of the objects in a company logo to move and resize the logo as a single object.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147002	31			0	en-GB	After you have grouped objects, selecting any part of the group selects the entire group.				20130618 17:22:18
