helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CD				0	en-GB	If there is an arrow next to the icon, the drawing tool opens a sub-toolbar. Press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Up\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Down\</item\> arrow key to open the sub-toolbar, then press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Right\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Left\</item\> key to select an icon.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338	8			0	en-GB	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154705	7			0	en-GB	The object is created at the centre of the current document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155962	6			0	en-GB	To return to the document, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155062	5			0	en-GB	You can use the arrow keys to position the object where you want. To choose a command from the context menu for the object, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+F10\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
