helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Print Statement [Run-time]				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147230				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>Print statement\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147230	1			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03010103.xhp\" name=\"Print Statement [Run-time]\"\>Print Statement [Run-time]\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3156281	2			0	en-GB	Outputs the specified strings or numeric expressions in a dialogue box or to a file.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145785	3			0	en-GB	Syntax:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188	4			0	en-GB	Print [#FileName,] Expression1[{;|,} [Spc(Number As Integer);] [Tab(pos As Integer);] [ExpressionN[...]] 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147348	5			0	en-GB	Parameter:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id2508621				0	en-GB	\<emph\>FileName:\</emph\> A numeric expression that contains the file number that was set by the Open statement for the respective file.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3163712	6			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Expression:\</emph\> A numeric or string expression to be printed. Multiple expressions can be separated by a semicolon. If separated by a comma, the expressions are indented to the next tab stop. The tab stops cannot be adjusted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153092	7			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Number:\</emph\> Number of spaces to be inserted by the \<emph\>Spc\</emph\> function.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145364	8			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Pos:\</emph\> Spaces are inserted until the specified position.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319	9			0	en-GB	If a semicolon or comma appears after the last expression to be printed, $[officename] Basic stores the text in an internal buffer and continues program execution without printing. When another Print statement without a semicolon or comma at the end is encountered, all text to be printed is printed at once.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272	10			0	en-GB	Positive numeric expressions are printed with a leading space. Negative expressions are printed with a leading minus sign. If a certain range is exceeded for floating-point values, the respective numeric expression is printed in exponential notation.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011	11			0	en-GB	If the expression to be printed exceeds a certain length, the display will automatically wrap to the next line.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969	12			0	en-GB	You can insert the Tab function, enclosed by semicolons, between arguments to indent the output to a specific position, or you can use the \<emph\>Spc\</emph\> function to insert a specified number of spaces.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146912	13			0	en-GB	Example:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153711	14			0	en-GB	Sub ExamplePrint				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153764	15			0	en-GB	Print "ABC"				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155764	16			0	en-GB	Print "ABC","123"				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id5484176				0	en-GB	i = FreeFile()				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id2904141				0	en-GB	Open \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>"C:\\Temp.txt"\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>"~/temp.txt"\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> For Output As i				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id36317				0	en-GB	Print #i, "ABC"				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id7381817				0	en-GB	Close #i				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3147339	17			0	en-GB	end Sub				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Functions for Screen Input				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149456	1			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03010200.xhp\" name=\"Functions for Screen Input\"\>Functions for Screen Input\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150398	2			0	en-GB	This section describes Run-time functions used to control screen input.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	InputBox Function [Runtime]				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148932				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>InputBox function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148932	1			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03010201.xhp\" name=\"InputBox Function [Runtime]\"\>InputBox Function [Runtime]\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	par_id3151262	2			0	en-GB	Displays a prompt in a dialogue box at which the user can enter text. The input is assigned to a variable.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	par_id3151100	3			0	en-GB	The \<emph\>InputBox\</emph\> statement is a convenient method of entering text through a dialogue box. Confirm the input by clicking OK or pressing Return. The input is returned as the function return value. If you close the dialogue box with Cancel, \<emph\>InputBox\</emph\> returns a zero-length string ("").				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152347	4			0	en-GB	Syntax:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	par_id3159201	5			0	en-GB	InputBox (Msg As String[, Title As String[, Default As String[, x_pos As Integer, y_pos As Integer]]]]) 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150713	6			0	en-GB	Return value:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	par_id3145090	7			0	en-GB	String				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149346	8			0	en-GB	Parameter:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153311	9			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Msg:\</emph\> String expression displayed as the message in the dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315	10			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Title:\</emph\> String expression displayed in the title bar of the dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154307	11			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Default:\</emph\> String expression displayed in the text box as default if no other input is given.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	par_id3147573	12			0	en-GB	\<emph\>x_pos:\</emph\> Integer expression that specifies the horizontal position of the dialog. The position is an absolute coordinate and does not refer to the window of the office application.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	par_id3156024	13			0	en-GB	\<emph\>y_pos:\</emph\> Integer expression that specifies the vertical position of the dialog. The position is an absolute coordinate and does not refer to the window of the office application.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153897	14			0	en-GB	If \<emph\>x_pos\</emph\> and \<emph\>y_pos\</emph\> are omitted, the dialog is centred on the screen. The position is specified in \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/00000002.xhp#twips\" name=\"twips\"\>twips\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149456	15			0	en-GB	Example:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153379	16			0	en-GB	Sub ExampleInputBox				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149656	17			0	en-GB	Dim sText As String				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154367	18			0	en-GB	sText = InputBox("Please enter a phrase:", "Dear User")				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	par_id3151042	19			0	en-GB	MsgBox(sText, 64, "Confirmation of phrase")				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150768	20			0	en-GB	End Sub				20130618 17:22:18
