helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041	8			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Number:\</emph\> A numeric expression for which you want to calculate the natural logarithm.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869	9			0	en-GB	The natural logarithm is the logarithm to the base e. The constant e has an value of approximately 2.71828182845904...				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968	10			0	en-GB	You can calculate logarithms to any base (n) for any number (x) by dividing the natural logarithm of x by the natural logarithm of n, as follows:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3145420	11			0	en-GB	Log n(x) = Log(x) / Log(n)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155131	12			0	en-GB	Example:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3152463	13			0	en-GB	Sub ExampleLogExp				20130618 17:22:18
