helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090401.xhp	0	help	par_id3148946	7			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Parameter:\</emph\> Parameters to pass to the procedure. The type and number of parameters is dependent on the routine that is executing.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090401.xhp	0	help	par_id3154216	8			0	en-GB	A keyword is optional when you call a procedure. If a function is executed as an expression, the parameters must be enclosed by brackets ( ) in the statement. If a DLL is called, it must first be specified in the \<emph\>Declare Statement\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
