helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149415	8			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Text:\</emph\> Any valid string expression. Only the first character in the string is relevant.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145609	9			0	en-GB	Use the Asc function to replace keys with values. If the Asc function encounters a blank string, $[officename] Basic reports a run-time error. In addition to 7 bit ASCII characters (Codes 0-127), the ASCII function can also detect non-printable key codes in ASCII code. This function can also handle 16 bit unicode characters.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159413	10			0	en-GB	Example:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149457	11			0	en-GB	Sub ExampleASC				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150792	12			0	en-GB	Print ASC("A") REM returns 65				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148797	13			0	en-GB	Print ASC("Z") REM returns 90				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120101.xhp	0	help	par_id3163800	14			0	en-GB	Print ASC("Blackpool") REM returns 66, since only the first character is taken into account				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148674	15			0	en-GB	End Sub				20130618 17:22:18
