helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Converting 2-D Objects to Curves, Polygons, and 3-D Objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150207				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>3-D rotation objects; generating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>3-D objects; generating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>3-D scenes; creating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting; to curves, polygons, 3-D\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>extrusion objects\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150207	32			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"3d_create\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/3d_create.xhp\" name=\"Converting 2-D Objects to Curves, Polygons, and 3-D Objects\"\>Converting 2-D Objects to Curves, Polygons, and 3-D Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3153914	33			0	en-GB	You can convert two dimensional (2D) objects to create different shapes. $[officename] can convert 2-D objects to the following object types:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150210	49			0	en-GB	Curved object based on Bézier curves				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154762	50			0	en-GB	Polygon object consisting of straight line segments				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150051	51			0	en-GB	3D object with shading and a light source				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149873	52			0	en-GB	3D rotation object with shading and a light source				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id31490481				0	en-GB	Two types of 3-D objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id31472951				0	en-GB	The Status bar displays "3-D scene selected". The 3-D scenes are built from objects which have dimensions in x, y and z coordinates. Examples are the objects inserted by the 3-D Objects toolbar, and rectangles, ellipses, or text that got created by the Rectangle, Ellipse, or Text icons left on the Drawing toolbar, or any Custom Shapes, and that got converted to 3-D by using the context menu "Convert - To 3D". These 3-D scenes can be entered (for example, by pressing F3), and the objects can be rotated in 3-D. Microsoft Office doesn't know these real 3-D objects. When exporting these 3-D scenes to Microsoft Office formats, a snapshot of the current view will be exported as a bitmap. 3-D bars in charts are of this type, too.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id31506541				0	en-GB	The Status bar displays "Shape selected". The Custom Shapes can be viewed in a 2-D mode or in a 3-D mode. At any time, you can switch the view between the two modes. You use the Basic Shapes, Symbol Shapes, and the following icons on the Drawing toolbar to create Custom Shapes. The Custom Shapes can be changed using the 3-D Settings toolbar. They do not form a 3-D scene, they cannot be illuminated by more than one light source, they show no reflections, and there are some more limitations. You can convert them to a 3-D scene, but then they are no longer Custom Shapes. Custom Shapes in 2-D or 3-D mode can be exported to and imported from Microsoft Office formats.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149048	34			0	en-GB	To convert an object to a curved shape:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3147295	35			0	en-GB	Select a 2-D object on the slide or page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150654	54			0	en-GB	Right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To Curve\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145828	55			0	en-GB	To modify the shape of the object, click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon\<image id=\"img_id1027558\" src=\"svx/res/cd015.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1027558\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, and drag the handles of the object. You can also drag the control points of a handle to modify the shape of the curve.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153738	56			0	en-GB	To convert a 2-D object to a polygon:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145241	57			0	en-GB	Select a 2-D object on the slide or page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148774	59			0	en-GB	Right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To Polygon.\</emph\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3155368	39			0	en-GB	To modify the shape of the object, click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon\<image id=\"img_id7219458\" src=\"svx/res/cd015.png\" width=\"0.2201inch\" height=\"0.2201inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7219458\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, and drag the handles of the object.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153919	60			0	en-GB	To convert a 2-D object to a 3-D object:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3147172	62			0	en-GB	Select a 2-D object on the slide or page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN1088B				0	en-GB	Click the \<emph\>Extrusion On/Off\</emph\> icon\<image id=\"img_id2490920\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_extrusiontoggle.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id2490920\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar, or right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To 3-D\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148828	41			0	en-GB	To edit the properties of the 3-D object, use the \<emph\>Line and Filling\</emph\> toolbar and the \<emph\>3-D Settings\</emph\> toolbar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN108C5				0	en-GB	To convert a text object to 3-D, use the \<emph\>Fontwork\</emph\> icon\<image id=\"img_id3821222\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_fontworkgalleryfloater.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3821222\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145410	65			0	en-GB	To convert a 2-D object to a 3-D rotation object:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154260	66			0	en-GB	A 3-D rotation object is created by rotating the selected object around its vertical axis.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3147506	67			0	en-GB	Select a 2-D object on the slide or page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3151318	69			0	en-GB	Right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To 3-D Rotation Object\</emph\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3146125	70			0	en-GB	To edit the properties of the 3-D object, use the Line and Filling toolbar and the 3-D Settings toolbar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149336	43			0	en-GB	You can rotate the 2-D object before converting it to create a more complex shape.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Creating Animated GIF Images				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153188				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>cross-fading; creating cross-fades\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>GIF images; animating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>animated GIFs\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153188	55			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"animated_gif_create\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/animated_gif_create.xhp\" name=\"Creating Animated GIF Images\"\>Creating Animated GIF Images\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377	3			0	en-GB	You can animate drawing objects, text objects, and graphic objects (images) on your slides to make your presentation more interesting. $[officename] Impress provides you with a simple animation editor with which you can create animation images (frames) by assembling objects from your slide. The animation effect is achieved by rotating through the static frames that you create.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154657	57			0	en-GB	If you create a bitmap animation (animated GIF), you can assign a delay time to each frame, and specify the number of times the animation is played.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150250	58			0	en-GB	To create an animated GIF:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148703	59			0	en-GB	Select an object or group of objects that you want to include in your animation and choose \<emph\>Insert - Animated Image\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149601	60			0	en-GB	Do one of the following:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145086	97			0	en-GB	Click the \<emph\>Apply Object\</emph\> button \<image id=\"img_id3148489\" src=\"sd/res/get1obj.png\" width=\"0.423cm\" height=\"0.423cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148489\"\>Note Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to add a single object or a group of objects to the current animation frame.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150860	98			0	en-GB	Click the \<emph\>Apply Objects Individually\</emph\> button \<image id=\"img_id3149355\" src=\"sd/res/getallob.png\" width=\"0.423cm\" height=\"0.423cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149355\"\>Tip Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to create a separate animation frame for each of the selected objects.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148391	61			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Animation Group\</emph\> area, select \<emph\>Bitmap object\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154871	99			0	en-GB	Use the animation timeline to specify the duration for displaying a frame and the number of times an animation sequence is presented (looping).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154644	62			0	en-GB	Enter a frame number in the \<emph\>Image Number\</emph\> box (left box).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150756	63			0	en-GB	Enter the number of seconds you want the frame to display in the \<emph\>Duration\</emph\> box (middle box).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3151182	64			0	en-GB	Repeat the last two steps for each frame in your animation.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3151177	100			0	en-GB	You can preview your animation by using the controls to the left of the \<emph\>Image Number\</emph\> box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154939	65			0	en-GB	Select the number of times you want the animation sequence to repeat in the \<emph\>Loop count\</emph\> box (right box).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145421	88			0	en-GB	Select an alignment option for the objects in the \<emph\>Alignment\</emph\> box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154285	101			0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>Create\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
