helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Importing HTML Pages Into Presentations				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146121				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>importing; presentations with HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; importing HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML; importing into presentations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text documents;inserting in slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; text in presentations\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146121	1			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"html_import\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/html_import.xhp\" name=\"Importing HTML Pages Into Presentations \"\>Importing HTML Pages Into Presentations \</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3150750	2			0	en-GB	You can import any text file, including text in HTML documents, into a slide.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155443	11			0	en-GB	To insert text from a file into a slide:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3146313	4			0	en-GB	In the slide into which you want to insert the text, choose \<emph\>Insert - File\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3150207	5			0	en-GB	Select "Text" or "HTML Document" as the \<emph\>File type\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3148610	12			0	en-GB	Locate the file containing the text that you want to add, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3153915	6			0	en-GB	If the text file contains more text than can be inserted into a single slide, you can divide the text over several slides.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3149126	7			0	en-GB	Double-click in the inserted text to enter edit mode.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3143228	8			0	en-GB	Select all of the text that lies below the visible slide area and press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+X.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3153811	9			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Insert – Slide\</emph\>, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3147297	10			0	en-GB	Repeat steps 1 to 3 until all of the text is on slides.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Creating a Custom Slide Show				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146119				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>slide shows; custom\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>custom slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>starting; always with the current slide\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>starting;custom slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding;slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>showing;hidden slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hidden pages;showing\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146119	55			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"individual\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/individual.xhp\" name=\"Creating a Custom Slide Show\"\>Creating a Custom Slide Show\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3150344	71			0	en-GB	You can create custom slide shows to meet the needs of your audience using slides within the current presentation.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150715	72			0	en-GB	To create a custom slide show:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3153712	61			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Custom Slide Shows\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3153966	62			0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\> and enter a name for your slide show in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3150249	73			0	en-GB	Under \<emph\>Existing Slides\</emph\>, select the slides you want to add to your slide show, and click the \<emph\>>>\</emph\> button. Hold down Shift to select a range of slides, or Ctrl to select multiple slides.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3153916	64			0	en-GB	You can change the order of the slides in your custom slide show, by dragging-and-dropping the slides under \<emph\>Selected Slides\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151387	74			0	en-GB	To start a custom slide show:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3147403	75			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Custom Slide Show\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3150538	76			0	en-GB	Select the show you want to start from the list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3149943	77			0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>Start\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3145593	56			0	en-GB	If you want the selected custom slide show to start when you click the \<emph\>Slide Show\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Presentation\</emph\> toolbar, or when you press F5, select \<emph\>Use Custom Slide Show\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145169	78			0	en-GB	Options for Running a Slide Show				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150335	65			0	en-GB	To always start a slide show from the current slide:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3150014	66			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Impress - General\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3155932	67			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Start presentation\</emph\> area, mark the \<emph\>Always with current page\</emph\> check box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3155372	68			0	en-GB	Do not select this option if you want to run a custom slide show.				20130618 17:22:18
