helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\13050700.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974	2			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:convert_to_contour\"\>Converts the selected object to a polygon, or a group of polygons.\</ahelp\> If the conversion creates a group of polygons (for example, when you convert a text object), then press F3 to enter the group before you can select an individual polygon.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\13050700.xhp	0	help	par_id3155601	3			0	en-GB	Once you convert a line or a text object to a contour, you can no longer edit it as you normally would. Instead, you can edit the contour as you would any polygon, including using the \<emph\>Edit – Points\</emph\> command to adjust its shape.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\13140000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Combine				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\13140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150012	1			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/13140000.xhp\" name=\"Combine\"\>Combine\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\13140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974	2			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Combine\"\>Combines two or more selected objects into a single shape.\</ahelp\>Unlike \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05290000.xhp\" name=\"grouping\"\>grouping\</link\>, a combined object takes on the properties of the lowermost object in the stacking order. You can \<link href=\"text/simpress/01/13150000.xhp\" name=\"split\"\>split\</link\> apart combined objects, but the original object properties are lost.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\13140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876	3			0	en-GB	When you combine objects, the drawing elements are replaced by Bézier curves and holes appear where the objects overlap.				20130618 17:22:18
