helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150199	6			0	en-GB	Rotate				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148489	40			0	en-GB	Rotates or skews the selected 2-D object(s) around a pivot point. Drag a corner handle of the object in the direction you want to rotate it. To skew an object, drag a centre handle in the direction you want to skew it.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154022	9			0	en-GB	Each slide has only one pivot point. Double-click an object to move the pivot point to the centre of the object. You can also drag the pivot point to a new location on the screen, and then rotate the object.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153914	10			0	en-GB	If you select a group that includes a 3-D object, only the 3-D object is rotated. You cannot skew a 3-D object, instead, you can rotate it about the x- and y-axes by dragging the centre handles.				20130618 17:22:18
