helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3405255				0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"cell_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cell_enter.xhp\"\>Entering Values\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id7147129				0	en-GB	Calc can simplify entering data and values into multiple cells. You can change some settings to conform to your preferences.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id5621509				0	en-GB	To Enter Values Into a Range of Cells Manually				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id8200018				0	en-GB	There are two features that assist you when you enter a block of data manually.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id1867427				0	en-GB	Area Detection for New Rows				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id7908871				0	en-GB	In the row below a heading row, you can advance from one cell to the next with the Tab key. After you enter the value into the last cell in the current row, press Enter. Calc positions the cursor below the first cell of the current block.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id6196783				0	en-GB	\<image id=\"img_id6473586\" src=\"res/helpimg/area1.png\" width=\"4.8335in\" height=\"1.5937in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id6473586\"\>area detection\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id8118839				0	en-GB	In row 3, press Tab to advance from cell B3 to C3, D3, and E3. Then press Enter to advance to B4.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3583788				0	en-GB	Area Selection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id2011780				0	en-GB	Use drag-and-drop to select the area into which you want to input values. But start dragging from the last cell of the area and release the mouse button when you have selected the first cell. Now you can start to input values. Always press the Tab key to advance to the next cell. You will not leave the selected area.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id7044282				0	en-GB	\<image id=\"img_id2811365\" src=\"res/helpimg/area2.png\" width=\"4.8335in\" height=\"1.5937in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id2811365\"\>area selection\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3232520				0	en-GB	Select the area from E7 to B3. Now B3 is waiting for your input. Press Tab to advance to the next cell within the selected area.				20130618 17:22:18
