helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3156444	17			0	en-GB	With the help of the Navigator you can reference cells from one sheet to another sheet in the same document or in a different document. The cells can be inserted as a copy, link or hyperlink. The range to be inserted must be defined with a name in the original file so that it can be inserted in the target file.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576	25			0	en-GB	Open the document that contains the source cells.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011	26			0	en-GB	To set the source range as the range, select the cells and choose \<emph\>Insert - Names - Define\</emph\>. Save the source document, and do not close it.				20130618 17:22:18
