helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id809961				0	en-GB	If you switch back to Sheet1, you will see the same content in cell A1 there. If the contents of Sheet2.A1 change, then the contents of Sheet1.A1 also changes.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	hd_id9209570				0	en-GB	To Reference a Cell in Another Document				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id5949278				0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>, to load an existing spreadsheet document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8001953				0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>, to open a new spreadsheet document. Set the cursor in the cell into which you want to insert the external data and enter an equals sign to indicate that you want to begin a formula.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8571123				0	en-GB	Now switch to the document you have just loaded. Click the cell with the data that you want to insert in the new document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8261665				0	en-GB	Switch back to the new spreadsheet. In the input line you will now see how $[officename] Calc has added the reference to the formula for you. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id5888241				0	en-GB	The reference to a cell of another document contains the name of the other document in single inverted commas, then a hash #, then the name of the sheet of the other document, followed by a point and the name of the cell.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id7697683				0	en-GB	Confirm the formula by clicking the green tick mark.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id7099826				0	en-GB	If you drag the box in the lower right corner of the active cell to select a range of cells, $[officename] automatically inserts the corresponding references in the adjacent cells. As a result, the sheet name is preceded with a "$" sign to designate it as an absolute reference.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id674459				0	en-GB	If you examine the name of the other document in this formula, you will notice that it is written as a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#url\" name=\"URL\"\>URL\</link\>. This means that you can also enter a URL from the Internet.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	References to Other Sheets and Referencing URLs				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150441				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>HTML; in sheet cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>references; URL in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; Internet references\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>URL; in Calc\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150441	15			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"cellreferences_url\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellreferences_url.xhp\" name=\"Referencing URLs\"\>Referencing URLs\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id1955626				0	en-GB	For example, if you found an Internet page containing current stock exchange information in spreadsheet cells, you can load this page in $[officename] Calc by using the following procedure:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3152993	39			0	en-GB	In a $[officename] Calc document, position the cursor in the cell into which you want to insert the external data.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3145384	40			0	en-GB	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Link to External Data\</item\>. The \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"External Data\"\>\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>External Data\</item\>\</link\> dialogue box will appear.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3152892	41			0	en-GB	Enter the URL of the document or Web page in the dialogue box. The URL must be in the format: http://www.my-bank.com/table.html. The URL for local or local area network files is the path seen in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Open\</item\> dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153068	42			0	en-GB	$[officename] loads the Web page or file in the "background", that is, without displaying it. In the large list box of the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>External Data\</item\> dialogue box, you can see the name of all the sheets or named ranges you can choose from.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153914	43			0	en-GB	Select one or more sheets or named ranges. You can also activate the automatic update function every "n" seconds and click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3157979	44			0	en-GB	The contents will be inserted as a link in the $[officename] Calc document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3144768	30			0	en-GB	Save your spreadsheet. When you open it again later, $[officename] Calc will update the linked cells following an inquiry.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3159204	38			0	en-GB	Under \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040900.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - General\"\>\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - General\</item\>\</link\> you can choose to have the update, when opened, automatically carried out either always, upon request or never. The update can be started manually in the dialogue box under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Links\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Assigning Formats by Formula				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145673				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>formats; assigning by formulae\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell formats; assigning by formulae\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>STYLE function example\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell styles;assigning by formulae\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulae;assigning cell formats\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145673	13			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"cellstyle_by_formula\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellstyle_by_formula.xhp\" name=\"Assigning Formats by Formula\"\>Assigning Formats by Formula\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275	14			0	en-GB	The STYLE() function can be added to an existing formula in a cell. For example, together with the CURRENT function, you can colour a cell depending on its value. The formula =... + STYLE(IF(CURRENT() > 3; "Red"; "Green")) applies the cell style "Red" to cells if the value is greater than 3, otherwise the cell style "Green" is applied.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3151385	15			0	en-GB	If you would like to apply a formula to all cells in a selected area, you can use the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Find & Replace\</item\> dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149456	16			0	en-GB	Select all the desired cells.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3148797	17			0	en-GB	Select the menu command \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767	18			0	en-GB	For the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Search for\</item\> term, enter: .\<item type=\"literal\"\>*\</item\>            				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153770	19			0	en-GB	".*" is a regular expression that designates the contents of the current cell.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153143	20			0	en-GB	Enter the following formula in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Replace with\</item\> field: \<item type=\"literal\"\>=&+STYLE(IF(CURRENT()>3;"Red";"Green"))\</item\>            				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975	21			0	en-GB	The "&" symbol designates the current contents of the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> field. The line must begin with an equal sign, since it is a formula. It is assumed that the cell styles "Red" and "Green" already exist.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149262	22			0	en-GB	Mark the fields \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100000.xhp\" name=\"Regular expressions\"\>\<emph\>Regular expressions\</emph\>\</link\> and \<emph\>Current selection only\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3144767	24			0	en-GB	All cells with contents that were included in the selection are now highlighted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3147127	23			0	en-GB	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Replace all\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Applying Conditional Formatting				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149263				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>conditional formatting; cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; conditional formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting; conditional formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>styles;conditional styles\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell formats; conditional\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>random numbers;examples\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell styles; copying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; cell styles\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; copying cell styles\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149263	24			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"cellstyle_conditional\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellstyle_conditional.xhp\" name=\"Applying Conditional Formatting\"\>Applying Conditional Formatting\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3159156	25			0	en-GB	Using the menu command \<emph\>Format - Conditional formatting\</emph\>, the dialogue box allows you to define up to three conditions per cell, which must be met in order for the selected cells to have a particular format.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id8039796				0	en-GB	To apply conditional formatting, AutoCalculate must be enabled. Choose \<emph\>Tools - Cell Content - AutoCalculate\</emph\> (a tick mark is present next to the command when AutoCalculate is enabled).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944	26			0	en-GB	With conditional formatting, you can, for example, highlight the totals that exceed the average value of all totals. If the totals change, the formatting changes correspondingly, without having to apply other styles manually.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id4480727				0	en-GB	To Define the Conditions				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490	27			0	en-GB	Select the cells to which you want to apply a conditional style.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3155603	28			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Format - Conditional Formatting\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969	29			0	en-GB	Enter the condition(s) into the dialogue box. The dialogue box is described in detail in \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05120000.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] Help\"\>$[officename] Help\</link\>, and an example is provided below:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155766	38			0	en-GB	Example of Conditional Formatting: Highlighting Totals Above/Under the Average Value				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id4341868				0	en-GB	Step1: Generate Number Values				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3150043	39			0	en-GB	You want to give certain values in your tables particular emphasis. For example, in a table of turnovers, you can show all the values above the average in green and all those below the average in red. This is possible with conditional formatting.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3155337	40			0	en-GB	First of all, write a table in which a few different values occur. For your test you can create tables with any random numbers:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3149565	41			0	en-GB	In one of the cells enter the formula =RAND(), and you will obtain a random number in the range 0.0 to 1.0. If you want integers in the range 0 to 50, enter the formula =INT(RAND()*50).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3149258	42			0	en-GB	Copy the formula to create a row of random numbers. Click the bottom right corner of the selected cell, and drag to the right until the desired cell range is selected.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3159236	43			0	en-GB	In the same way as described above, drag down the corner of the rightmost cell in order to create more rows of random numbers.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149211	44			0	en-GB	Step 2: Define Cell Styles				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3154659	45			0	en-GB	The next step is to apply a cell style to all values that represent above-average turnover, and one to those that are below the average. Ensure that the Styles and Formatting window is visible before proceeding.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3150883	46			0	en-GB	Click in a blank cell and select the command \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> in the context menu.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3155529	47			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialogue box on the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab, select a background colour. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3154484	48			0	en-GB	In the Styles and Formatting window, click the \<emph\>New Style from Selection\</emph\> icon. Enter the name of the new style. For this example, name the style "Above".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3152889	49			0	en-GB	To define a second style, click again in a blank cell and proceed as described above. Assign a different background colour for the cell and assign a name (for this example, "Below").				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148704	60			0	en-GB	Step 3: Calculate Average				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3148837	51			0	en-GB	In our particular example, we are calculating the average of the random values. The result is placed in a cell:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3144768	52			0	en-GB	Set the cursor in a blank cell, for example, J14, and choose \<emph\>Insert - Function\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3156016	53			0	en-GB	Select the AVERAGE function. Use the mouse to select all your random numbers. If you cannot see the entire range, because the Function Wizard is obscuring it, you can temporarily shrink the dialogue box using the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000001.xhp#eingabesymbol\" name=\"Shrink or Maximise\"\>\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Shrink / Maximise\</item\>\</link\> icon.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3153246	54			0	en-GB	Close the Function Wizard with \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149898	50			0	en-GB	Step 4: Apply Cell Styles				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3149126	55			0	en-GB	Now you can apply the conditional formatting to the sheet:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3150049	56			0	en-GB	Select all cells with the random numbers.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3153801	57			0	en-GB	Choose the \<emph\>Format - Conditional Formatting\</emph\> command to open the corresponding dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3153013	58			0	en-GB	Define the condition as follows: If cell value is less than J14, format with cell style "Below", and if cell value is greater than or equal to J14, format with cell style "Above".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155761	61			0	en-GB	Step 5: Copy Cell Style				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3145320	62			0	en-GB	To apply the conditional formatting to other cells later:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3153074	63			0	en-GB	Click one of the cells that has been assigned conditional formatting.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3149051	64			0	en-GB	Copy the cell to the clipboard.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3150436	65			0	en-GB	Select the cells that are to receive this same formatting.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3147298	66			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste Special\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Paste Special\</emph\> dialogue box will appear.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3166465	67			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> area, mark only the \<emph\>Formats\</emph\> check box. All other check boxes must be unmarked. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3159123	68			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05120000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Conditional formatting\"\>Format - Conditional formatting\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Highlighting Negative Numbers				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147434				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbers; highlighting negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>highlighting;negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>colours;negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>number formats;colours for negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147434	31			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"cellstyle_minusvalue\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp\" name=\"Highlighting Negative Numbers\"\>Highlighting Negative Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3153878	33			0	en-GB	You can format cells with a number format that highlights negative numbers in red. Alternatively, you can define your own number format in which negative numbers are highlighted in other colours.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3155600	34			0	en-GB	Select the cells and choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969	35			0	en-GB	On the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab, select a number format and mark \<emph\>Negative numbers red\</emph\> check box. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640	36			0	en-GB	The cell number format is defined in two parts. The format for positive numbers and zero is defined in front of the semicolon; after the semicolon the formula for negative numbers is defined. You can change the code (RED) under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format code\</item\>. For example, instead of RED, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>YELLOW\</item\>. If the new code appears in the list after clicking the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Add\</item\> icon, this is a valid entry.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Consolidating Data				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150791				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>consolidating data\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>ranges; combining\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>combining;cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; combining\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>data; merging cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>merging;data ranges\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150791	5			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"consolidate\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/consolidate.xhp\" name=\"Consolidating Data\"\>Consolidating Data\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153191	34			0	en-GB	During consolidation, the contents of the cells from several sheets will be combined in one place.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	hd_id892056				0	en-GB	To Combine Contents of Cells				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073	6			0	en-GB	Open the document that contains the cell ranges to be consolidated.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3154513	7			0	en-GB	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Consolidate\</item\> to open the \<emph\>Consolidate\</emph\> dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147345	8			0	en-GB	From the \<emph\>Source data area\</emph\> box select a source cell range to consolidate with other areas.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149209	9			0	en-GB	If the range is not named, click in the field next to the \<emph\>Source data area\</emph\>. A blinking text cursor will appear. Type a reference for the first source data range or select the range with the mouse.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155529	10			0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> to insert the selected range in the \<emph\>Consolidation areas\</emph\> field.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153816	11			0	en-GB	Select additional ranges and click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> after each selection.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3157983	12			0	en-GB	Specify where you want to display the result by selecting a target range from the \<emph\>Copy results to\</emph\> box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3150215	13			0	en-GB	If the target range is not named, click in the field next to \<emph\>Copy results to\</emph\> and enter the reference of the target range. Alternatively, you can select the range using the mouse or position the cursor in the top left cell of the target range.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153813	14			0	en-GB	Select a function from the \<emph\>Function\</emph\> box. The function specifies how the values of the consolidation ranges are linked. The "Sum" function is the default setting.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149315	15			0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to consolidate the ranges.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_idN107DE				0	en-GB	Additional Settings				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147250	16			0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>More\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Consolidate\</emph\> dialogue box to display additional settings:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3156400	17			0	en-GB	Select \<emph\>Link to source data\</emph\> to insert the formulae that generate the results in the target range, rather than the actual results. If you link the data, any values modified in the source range are automatically updated in the target range.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3150538	18			0	en-GB	The corresponding cell references in the target range are inserted in consecutive rows, which are automatically ordered and then hidden from view. Only the final result, based on the selected function, is displayed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149945	19			0	en-GB	Under \<emph\>Consolidate by\</emph\>, select either \<emph\>Row labels\</emph\> or \<emph\>Column labels\</emph\> if the cells of the source data range are not to be consolidated corresponding to the identical position of the cell in the range, but instead according to a matching row label or column label.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3157871	20			0	en-GB	To consolidate by row labels or column labels, the label must be contained in the selected source ranges.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3150478	21			0	en-GB	The text in the labels must be identical, so that rows or columns can be accurately matched. If the row or column label does not match any that exist in the target range, it will be appended as a new row or column.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147468	22			0	en-GB	The data from the consolidation ranges and target range will be saved when you save the document. If you later open a document in which consolidation has been defined, this data will again be available.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153039	33			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12070000.xhp\" name=\"Data - Consolidate\"\>Data - Consolidate\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	 Importing and Exporting CSV Files 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	bm_id892361				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>number series import\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data series import\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting; tables as text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing; tables as text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>delimited values and files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>comma separated files and values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text file import and export\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>CSV files;importing and exporting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; importing/exporting as text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text documents; importing to spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>opening;text CSV files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving;as text csv\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10862				0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"csv_files\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/csv_files.xhp\"\>Opening and Saving Text CSV Files\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10880				0	en-GB	Comma Separated Values (CSV) is a text file format that you can use to exchange data from a database or a spreadsheet between applications. Each line in a Text CSV file represents a record in the database, or a row in a spreadsheet. Each field in a database record or cell in a spreadsheet row is usually separated by a comma. However, you can use other characters to delimit a field, such as semicolon or tab characters.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10886				0	en-GB	If the field or cell contains a comma, its content \<emph\>must\</emph\> be enclosed by single quotes (') or double quotes (").				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10890				0	en-GB	To Open a Text CSV File in Calc				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10897				0	en-GB	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Open\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1089F				0	en-GB	Locate the CSV file that you want to open.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A2				0	en-GB	If the file has a *.csv extension, select the file.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A5				0	en-GB	If the CSV file has another extension, select the file, and then select "Text CSV" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File type\</item\> box				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082D				0	en-GB	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Open\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10834				0	en-GB	The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text Import\</item\> dialogue box opens.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108B1				0	en-GB	Specify the options to divide the text in the file into columns.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108BB				0	en-GB	You can preview the layout of the imported data at the bottom of the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text Import\</item\> dialogue box. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_id8444166				0	en-GB	Right-click a column in the preview to set the format or to hide the column.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108E2				0	en-GB	Mark the text delimiter check box that matches the character used as text delimiter in the file. In case of an unlisted delimiter, type the character into the input box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108C5				0	en-GB	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108FA				0	en-GB	To Save a Sheet as a Text CSV File				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FC				0	en-GB	When you export a spreadsheet to CSV format, only the data on the current sheet is saved. All other information, including formulae and formatting, is omitted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10901				0	en-GB	Open the Calc sheet that you want to save as a Text CSV file.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AF				0	en-GB	Only the current sheet can be exported.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10905				0	en-GB	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Save as\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10915				0	en-GB	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File name\</item\> box, enter a name for the file.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1090D				0	en-GB	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File type\</item\> box, select "Text CSV".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107DD				0	en-GB	(Optional) Set the field options for the Text CSV file.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1091C				0	en-GB	Select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit filter settings\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107ED				0	en-GB	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Export of text files\</item\> dialogue box, select the options that you want.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F4				0	en-GB	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107FC				0	en-GB	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Save\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
