helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Importing and Exporting Text Files				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153726				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>CSV files;formulae\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulae; importing/exporting as CSV files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting;formulae as CSV files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing;CSV files with formulae\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153726	1			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"csv_formula\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/csv_formula.xhp\" name=\"Importing and Exporting Text Files\"\>Importing and Exporting CSV Text Files with Formulae\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149402	2			0	en-GB	Comma separated values (CSV) files are text files that contain the contents of cells of a single sheet. Commas, semicolons, or other characters can be used as the field delimiters between the cells. Text strings are put in quotation marks, numbers are written without quotation marks.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150715	15			0	en-GB	To Import a CSV File				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153709	16			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3155445	17			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> field, select the format "Text CSV". Select the file and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>. When a file has the .csv extension, the file type is automatically recognised.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149565	18			0	en-GB	You will see the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text Import\</item\> dialogue box. Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149255	19			0	en-GB	If the CSV file contains formulae, but you want to import the results of those formulae, then choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\> and unmark the \<emph\>Formulae\</emph\> check box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154022	3			0	en-GB	To Export Formulae and Values as CSV Files				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150342	4			0	en-GB	Click the sheet to be written as a CSV file.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3166423	5			0	en-GB	If you want to export the formulae as formulae, for example, in the form =SUM(A1:B5), proceed as follows:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3155111	6			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150200	7			0	en-GB	Under \<emph\>Display\</emph\>, mark the \<emph\>Formulae\</emph\> check box. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154484	8			0	en-GB	If you want to export the calculation results instead of the formulae, do not mark \<emph\>Formulae\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3148702	9			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>File - Save as\</emph\>. You will see the \<emph\>Save as\</emph\> dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153912	10			0	en-GB	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File type\</item\> field select the format "Text CSV".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3157978	13			0	en-GB	Enter a name and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3152869	23			0	en-GB	From the \<emph\>Export of text files\</emph\> dialogue box that appears, select the character set and the field and text delimiters for the data to be exported, and confirm with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3146781	12			0	en-GB	If the numbers use commas as decimal separators or thousands separators, do not select the comma as the field delimiter. If the text contains double quotation marks, you must select the single quotation mark as separator.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150050	14			0	en-GB	If necessary, after you have saved, unmark the \<emph\>Formulae\</emph\> check box to see the calculated results in the table again.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153487	20			0	en-GB	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060100.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - View\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153008	21			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000207.xhp\" name=\"Export text files\"\>Export text files\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3155595	22			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000208.xhp\" name=\"Import text files\"\>Import text files\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Cells in Currency Format				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156329				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>currency formats; spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>international currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats; currency formats in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>currencies; default currencies\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defaults;currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;currency formats\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156329	46			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"currency_format\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/currency_format.xhp\" name=\"Cells in Currency Format\"\>Cells in Currency Format\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968	47			0	en-GB	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc you can give numbers any currency format. When you click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Currency\</item\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3150791\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_currencyfield.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150791\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formatting\</item\> bar to format a number, the cell is given the default currency format set under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language Settings - Languages\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010	48			0	en-GB	Exchanging \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc documents can lead to misunderstandings, if your \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc document is loaded by a user who uses a different default currency format.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3156442	52			0	en-GB	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc you can define that a number that you have formatted as "1,234.50 €", still remains in euro in another country and does not become dollars.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3151075	49			0	en-GB	You can change the currency format in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format Cells\</item\> dialogue box (choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</item\> tab) by two country settings. In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Language\</item\> combo box select the basic setting for currency symbol, decimal and thousands separators. In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format\</item\> list box you can select possible variations from the default format for the language.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749	50			0	en-GB	For example, if the language is set to "Default" and you are using a German locale setting, the currency format will be "1.234,00 €". A dot-on-the-line is used after the thousand digits and a comma before the decimal places. If you now select the subordinate currency format "$ English (US)" from the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format\</item\> list box, you will get the following format: "$ 1.234,00". As you can see, the separators have remained the same. Only the currency symbol has been changed and converted, but the underlying format of the notation remains the same as in the locale setting.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640	51			0	en-GB	If, under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Language\</item\>, you convert the cells to "English (US)", the English-language locale setting is also transferred and the default currency format is now "$ 1,234.00".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255	53			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cells - Numbers\"\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Defining Database Ranges				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154758				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>tables; database ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>database ranges; defining\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ranges; defining database ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;database ranges\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154758	31			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"database_define\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/database_define.xhp\" name=\"Defining Database Ranges\"\>Defining a Database Range\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768	81			0	en-GB	You can define a range of cells in a spreadsheet to use as a database. Each row in this database range corresponds to a database record and each cell in a row corresponds to a database field. You can sort, group, search, and perform calculations on the range as you would in a database.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3145801	82			0	en-GB	You can only edit and access a database range in the spreadsheet that contains the range. You cannot access the database range in the %PRODUCTNAME Data Sources view. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_idN10648				0	en-GB	To Define a Database Range				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064	41			0	en-GB	Select the range of cells that you want to define as a database range.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_idN10654				0	en-GB	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Define Range\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3153715	72			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box, enter a name for the database range.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066A				0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>More\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3154253	42			0	en-GB	Specify the options for the database range.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_idN10675				0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Filtering Cell Ranges 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153541				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>cell ranges;applying/removing filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filtering;cell ranges/database ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>database ranges;applying/removing filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>removing;cell range filters\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153541	47			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"database_filter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/database_filter.xhp\" name=\"Filtering Cell Ranges\"\>Filtering Cell Ranges\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145069	48			0	en-GB	You can use several filters to filter cell ranges in spreadsheets. A standard filter uses the options that you specify to filter the data. An AutoFilter filters data according to a specific value or string. An advanced filter uses filter criteria from specified cells.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	en-GB	To Apply a Standard Filter to a Cell Range				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150398	50			0	en-GB	Click in a cell range.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10693				0	en-GB	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Filter - Standard Filter\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422	51			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Standard Filter\</emph\> dialogue box, specify the filter options that you want.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A5				0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153143	52			0	en-GB	The records that match the filter options that you specified are shown.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153728	53			0	en-GB	To Apply an AutoFilter to a Cell Range				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764	54			0	en-GB	Click in a cell range or a database range.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id9303872				0	en-GB	If you want to apply multiple AutoFilters to the same sheet, you must first define database ranges, then apply the AutoFilters to the database ranges.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944	55			0	en-GB	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Filter - AutoFilter\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DB				0	en-GB	An arrow button is added to the head of each column in the database range.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153878	56			0	en-GB	Click the arrow button in the column that contains the value or string that you want to set as the filter criteria.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10749				0	en-GB	Select the value or string that you want to use as the filter criteria.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1074C				0	en-GB	The records that match the filter criteria that you selected are shown.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E8				0	en-GB	To Remove a Filter From a Cell Range				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075C				0	en-GB	Click in a filtered cell range.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EC				0	en-GB	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Filter - Remove Filter\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id4525284				0	en-GB	\<link href=\"http://wiki.services.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Defining_a_Data_Range\"\>Wiki page about defining a data range\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Sorting Data 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150767				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>database ranges; sorting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sorting; database ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data;sorting in databases\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150767	44			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"database_sort\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/database_sort.xhp\" name=\"Sorting Database Ranges\"\>Sorting Data\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id3145751	45			0	en-GB	Click in a database range.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id121020081121549				0	en-GB	If you select a range of cells, only these cells will get sorted. If you just click one cell without selecting, then the whole database range will get sorted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_idN10635				0	en-GB	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Sort\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id121020081121547				0	en-GB	The range of cells that will get sorted is shown in inverted colours.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_idN10645				0	en-GB	Select the sort options that you want.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_idN1063D				0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id1846980				0	en-GB	\<link href=\"http://wiki.services.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Defining_a_Data_Range\"\>Wiki page about defining a data range\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Pivot Table				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150448				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; introduction\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>DataPilot, see pivot table function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150448	7			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"datapilot\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot.xhp\" name=\"Pivot Table\"\>Pivot Table\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	par_id3156024	2			0	en-GB	The \<emph\>pivot table\</emph\> (formerly known as \<emph\>DataPilot\</emph\>) allows you to combine, compare, and analyze large amounts of data. You can view different summaries of the source data, you can display the details of areas of interest, and you can create reports.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	par_id3145069	9			0	en-GB	A table that has been created as a \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090000.xhp\" name=\"pivot table\"\>pivot table\</link\> is an interactive table. Data can be arranged, rearranged or summarized according to different points of view.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Creating Pivot Tables				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148491				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>DataPilot tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; calling up and applying\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148491	7			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"datapilot_createtable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_createtable.xhp\" name=\"Creating Pivot Tables\"\>Creating Pivot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3156023	8			0	en-GB	Position the cursor within a range of cells containing values, row and column headings.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147264	9			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Data - Pivot Table - Create\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Select Source\</emph\> dialogue box will appear. Choose \<emph\>Current selection\</emph\> and confirm with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The table headings are shown as buttons in the \<emph\>Pivot Table\</emph\> dialogue box. Drag these buttons as required and drop them into the layout areas "Page Fields", "Column Fields", "Row Fields" and "Data Fields".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868	10			0	en-GB	Drag the desired buttons into one of the four areas.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id7599414				0	en-GB	Drag a button to the \<emph\>Page Fields\</emph\> area to create a button and a list box on top of the generated pivot table. The list box can be used to filter the pivot table by the content of the selected item. You can use drag-and-drop within the generated pivot table to use another page field as a filter.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011	11			0	en-GB	If the button is dropped in the \<emph\>Data Fields\</emph\> area it will be given a caption that also shows the formula that will be used to calculate the data.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974	16			0	en-GB	By double-clicking on one of the fields in the \<emph\>Data Fields\</emph\> area you can call up the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090105.xhp\" name=\"Data Field\"\>\<emph\>Data Field\</emph\>\</link\> dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286	17			0	en-GB	Use the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data Field\</item\> dialogue box to select the calculations to be used for the data. To make a multiple selection, press the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while clicking the desired calculation.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150329	13			0	en-GB	The order of the buttons can be changed at any time by moving them to a different position in the area with the mouse.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714	14			0	en-GB	Remove a button by dragging it back to the area of the other buttons at the right of the dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338	15			0	en-GB	To open the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090105.xhp\" name=\"Data Field\"\>\<emph\>Data Field\</emph\>\</link\> dialogue box, double-click one of the buttons in the \<emph\>Row\</emph\> or \<emph\>Column\</emph\> area. Use the dialogue box to select if and to what extent \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> calculates display subtotals.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154020	18			0	en-GB	Exit the Pivot Table dialogue box by pressing OK. A \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> button will now be inserted, or a page button for every data field that you dropped in the \<emph\>Page Fields\</emph\> area. The pivot table is inserted further down.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_deletetable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Deleting Pivot Tables				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_deletetable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153726				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; deleting tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_deletetable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153726	31			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"datapilot_deletetable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_deletetable.xhp\" name=\"Deleting Pivot Tables\"\>Deleting Pivot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_deletetable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154014	32			0	en-GB	In order to delete a pivot table, click any cell in the pivot table, then choose \<emph\>Delete\</emph\> in the context menu.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Editing Pivot Tables				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148663				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; editing tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148663	25			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"datapilot_edittable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_edittable.xhp\" name=\"Editing Pivot Tables\"\>Editing Pivot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868	26			0	en-GB	Click one of the buttons in the pivot table and hold the mouse button down. A special symbol will appear next to the mouse pointer.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786	27			0	en-GB	By dragging the button to a different position in the same row you can alter the order of the columns. If you drag a button to the left edge of the table into the row headings area, you can change a column into a row.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id1648915				0	en-GB	In the Pivot Table dialogue box, you can drag a button to the \<emph\>Page Fields\</emph\> area to create a button and a list box on top of the pivot table. The list box can be used to filter the pivot table by the contents of the selected item. You can use drag-and-drop within the pivot table to use another page field as a filter.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434	29			0	en-GB	To remove a button from the table, just drag it out of the pivot table. Release the mouse button when the mouse pointer positioned within the sheet has become a 'not allowed' icon. The button is deleted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id3156442	40			0	en-GB	To edit the pivot table, click a cell inside the pivot table and open the context menu. In the context menu you find the command \<emph\>Edit Layout\</emph\>, which displays the \<emph\>Pivot Table\</emph\> dialogue box for the current pivot table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id2666096				0	en-GB	In the pivot table, you can use drag-and-drop or cut/paste commands to rearrange the order of data fields.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id266609688				0	en-GB	You can assign custom display names to fields, field members, subtotals (with some restrictions), and grand totals inside pivot tables. A custom display name is assigned to an item by overwriting the original name with another name.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Filtering Pivot Tables				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150792				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; filtering tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filtering;pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"datapilot_filtertable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_filtertable.xhp\" name=\"Filtering Pivot Tables\"\>Filtering Pivot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	en-GB	You can use filters to remove unwanted data from a pivot table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150441				0	en-GB	Click the \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> button in the sheet to call up the dialog for the filter conditions. Alternatively, call up the context menu of the pivot table and select the \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> command. The \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090103.xhp\" name=\"Filter\"\>\<emph\>Filter\</emph\>\</link\> dialogue box appears. Here you can filter the pivot table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id315044199				0	en-GB	You can also click the arrow on a button in the pivot table to show a pop-up window. In this pop-up window, you can edit the visibility settings of the associated field.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344485				0	en-GB	The pop-up window displays a list of field members associated with that field. A check box is placed to the left of each field member name. When a field has an alternative display name that differs from its original name, that name is displayed in the list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344449				0	en-GB	Enable or disable a check box to show or hide the associated field member in the pivot table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344493				0	en-GB	Enable or disable the \<emph\>All\</emph\> check box to show all or none of the field members.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344431				0	en-GB	Select a field member in the pop-up window and click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Show only the current item\</item\> button to show only the selected field member. All other field members are hidden in the pivot table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344484				0	en-GB	Select a field member in the pop-up window and click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Hide only the current item\</item\> button to hide only the selected field member. All other field members are shown in the pivot table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344578				0	en-GB	Commands enable you to sort the field members in ascending order, descending order, or using a custom sort list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344584				0	en-GB	To edit the custom sort lists, open \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - Sort Lists.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344811				0	en-GB	The arrow to open the pop-up window is normally black. When the field contains one or more hidden field members, the arrow is blue and displays a tiny square at its lower-right corner.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344884				0	en-GB	You can also open the pop-up window by positioning the cell cursor at the button and pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+D.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Grouping Pivot Tables				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	bm_id4195684				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>grouping; pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function;grouping table entries\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ungrouping entries in pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10643				0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"datapilot_grouping\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_grouping.xhp\"\>Grouping Pivot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10661				0	en-GB	The resulting pivot table can contain many different entries. By grouping the entries, you can improve the visible result.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10667				0	en-GB	Select a cell or range of cells in the pivot table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066B				0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Data - Group and Outline - Group\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066E				0	en-GB	Depending on the format of the selected cells, either a new group field is added to the pivot table, or you see one of the two \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090400.xhp\"\>Grouping\</link\> dialogue boxes, either for numeric values, or for date values.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_id3328653				0	en-GB	The pivot table must be organised in a way that grouping can be applied.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	en-GB	To remove a grouping, click inside the group, then choose \<emph\>Data - Group and Outline - Ungroup\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Selecting Pivot Table Output Ranges				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148663				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; preventing data overwriting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>output ranges of pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148663	19			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"datapilot_tipps\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_tipps.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Pivot Table Output Ranges\"\>Selecting Pivot Table Output Ranges\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3154123	20			0	en-GB	Click the button \<emph\>More\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Pivot Table\</emph\> dialogue box. The dialogue box will be extended.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3153771	21			0	en-GB	You can select a named range in which the pivot table is to be created, from the \<emph\>Results to\</emph\> box. If the results range does not have a name, enter the coordinates of the upper left cell of the range into the field to the right of the \<emph\>Results to\</emph\> box. You can also click on the appropriate cell to have the coordinates entered accordingly.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974	23			0	en-GB	If you mark the \<emph\>Ignore empty rows\</emph\> check box, they will not be taken into account when the pivot table is created.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273	24			0	en-GB	If the \<emph\>Identify categories\</emph\> check box is marked, the categories will be identified by their headings and assigned accordingly when the pivot table is created.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_updatetable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Updating Pivot Tables				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_updatetable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150792				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>pivot table import\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; refreshing tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>recalculating;pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating;pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_updatetable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792	33			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"datapilot_updatetable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_updatetable.xhp\" name=\"Updating Pivot Tables\"\>Updating Pivot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_updatetable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684	34			0	en-GB	If the data of the source sheet has been changed, $[officename] recalculates the pivot table. To recalculate the table, choose \<emph\>Data - Pivot Table - Refresh\</emph\>. Do the same after you have imported an Excel pivot table into $[officename] Calc.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Importing and Exporting dBASE Files 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	bm_id1226844				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>exporting;spreadsheets to dBASE\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>importing;dBASE files\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>dBASE import/export\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; importing from/exporting to dBASE files\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables in databases;importing dBASE files\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10738				0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"dbase_files\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/dbase_files.xhp\"\>Importing and Exporting dBASE Files\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10756				0	en-GB	You can open and save data in the dBASE file format (*.dbf file extension) in $[officename] Base or a spreadsheet. In %PRODUCTNAME Base, a dBASE database is a folder that contains a collection of files with the .dbf file extension. Each file corresponds to a table in the database. Formulae and formatting are not transferred when you open and save a dBASE file from %PRODUCTNAME.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10759				0	en-GB	To Import a dBASE File Into a Spreadsheet				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10760				0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071F				0	en-GB	Locate the *.dbf file that you want to import. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10768				0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10730				0	en-GB	The \<emph\>Import dBASE files\</emph\> dialogue box opens.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10774				0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10777				0	en-GB	The dBASE file opens as a new Calc spreadsheet.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1074E				0	en-GB	If you want to save the spreadsheet as a dBASE file, do not alter or delete the first row in the imported file. This row contains information that is required by a dBASE database.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077A				0	en-GB	To Import a dBASE File Into a Database Table				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076C				0	en-GB	A %PRODUCTNAME Base database table is actually a link to an existing database.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10796				0	en-GB	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - New - Database\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10786				0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box of the \<emph\>Save As\</emph\> dialogue box, enter a name for the database.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10792				0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1079A				0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Database type\</emph\> box of the \<emph\>Database Properties\</emph\> dialogue box, select "dBASE".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A6				0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AE				0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>Browse\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B6				0	en-GB	Locate the directory that contains the dBASE file, and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107BE				0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>Create\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F1				0	en-GB	To Save a Spreadsheet as a dBASE File				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F8				0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10800				0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>File format\</emph\> box, select "dBASE file".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F9				0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box, type a name for the dBASE file.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10801				0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10808				0	en-GB	Only the data on the current sheet is exported.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Selecting Themes for Sheets				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150791				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>theme selection for sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>layout;spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell styles; selecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;formatting themes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets;formatting themes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats;themes for sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;themes for sheets\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150791	6			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"design\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/design.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Themes for Sheets\"\>Selecting Themes for Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786	13			0	en-GB	$[officename] Calc comes with a predefined set of formatting themes that you can apply to your spreadsheets.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490	16			0	en-GB	It is not possible to add themes to Calc, and they cannot be modified. However, you can modify their styles after you apply them to a spreadsheet.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3154757	17			0	en-GB	Before you format a sheet with a theme, you have to apply at least one custom cell style to the cells on the sheet. You can then change the cell formatting by selecting and applying a theme in the \<emph\>Theme Selection\</emph\> dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382	18			0	en-GB	To apply a custom cell style to a cell, you can open the Styles and Formatting window and, in its lower list box, set the Custom Styles view. A list of the existing custom defined cell styles will be displayed. Double-click a name from the Styles and Formatting window to apply this style to the selected cells.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963	19			0	en-GB	To apply a theme to a spreadsheet:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3146920	15			0	en-GB	Click the \<emph\>Choose Themes\</emph\> icon in the \<emph\>Tools\</emph\> bar. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488	20			0	en-GB	The \<emph\>Theme Selection\</emph\> dialogue box will appear. This dialogue box lists the available themes for the whole spreadsheet and the Styles and Formatting window lists the custom styles for specific cells.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3155114	9			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Theme Selection\</emph\> dialogue box, select the theme that you want to apply to the spreadsheet.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3150090	21			0	en-GB	Click OK				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3150201	22			0	en-GB	As soon as you select another theme in the \<emph\>Theme Selection\</emph\> dialogue box, some of the properties of the custom style will be applied to the current spreadsheet. The modifications will be immediately visible in your spreadsheet.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3146979	12			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/scalc/02/06080000.xhp\" name=\"Theme selection\"\>Theme selection\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Copying to Multiple Sheets				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149456				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>copying;values, to multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;values in multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data;inserting in multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\> \<bookmark_value\>sheets; simultaneous multiple filling\</bookmark_value\> 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149456	3			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"edit_multitables\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/edit_multitables.xhp\" name=\"Copying to Multiple Sheets\"\>Copying to Multiple Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868	6			0	en-GB	In $[officename] Calc, you can insert values, text or formulae that are simultaneously copied to other selected sheets of your document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768	8			0	en-GB	Select all desired sheets by holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key and clicking the corresponding register tabs that are still grey at the bottom margin of the workspace. All selected register tabs are now white.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10614				0	en-GB	You can use Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Page Up or Page Down to select multiple sheets using the keyboard.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3147435	7			0	en-GB	Now when you insert values, text or formulae into the active sheet, they will also appear in the identical positions in the other selected sheets. For example, data entered in cell A1 of the active sheet is automatically entered into cell A1 of any other seleted sheet.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Applying Filters				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153896				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>filters; applying/removing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows;removing/redisplaying with filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>removing;filters\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153896	70			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"filters\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/filters.xhp\" name=\"Applying Filters\"\>Applying Filters\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869	2			0	en-GB	Filters and advanced filters allow you to work on certain filtered rows (records) of a data range. In the spreadsheets in $[officename] there are various possibilities for applying filters.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131	3			0	en-GB	One use for the \<emph\>AutoFilter\</emph\> function is to quickly restrict the display to records with identical entries in a data field.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119	4			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Standard Filter\</emph\> dialogue box, you can also define ranges which contain the values in particular data fields. You can use the standard filter to connect up to three conditions with either a logical AND or a logical OR operator.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010	5			0	en-GB	The \<emph\>Advanced filter\</emph\> allows up to a total of eight filter conditions. With advanced filters you enter the conditions directly into the sheet.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id9384746				0	en-GB	To remove a filter, so that you see all cells again, click inside the area where the filter was applied, then choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Filter - Remove Filter\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_idN10663				0	en-GB	When you select multiple rows from an area where a filter was applied, then this selection can include rows that are visible and rows that are hidden by the filter. If you then apply formatting, or delete the selected rows, this action then applies only to the visible rows. The hidden rows are not affected. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id218817				0	en-GB	This is the opposite to rows that you have hidden manually by the \<emph\>Format - Rows - Hide Rows\</emph\> command. Manually hidden rows are deleted when you delete a selection that contains them.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Finding and Replacing in Calc				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	bm_id3769341				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>searching, see also finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>finding;formulae/values/text/objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>replacing; cell content\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;multiple cell texts\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149204				0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"finding\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/finding.xhp\"\>Finding and Replacing in Calc\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9363689				0	en-GB	In spreadsheet documents you can find words, formulae, and styles. You can navigate from one result to the next, or you can highlight all matching cells at once, then apply another format or replace the cell content by other content.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3610644				0	en-GB	The Find & Replace dialogue box				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2224494				0	en-GB	Cells can contain text or numbers that were entered directly as in a text document. But cells can also contain text or numbers as the result of a calculation. For example, if a cell contains the formula =1+2 it displays the result 3. You must decide whether to search for the 1 respective 2, or to search the 3.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id2423780				0	en-GB	To find formulae or values				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2569658				0	en-GB	You can specify in the Find & Replace dialogue box either to find the parts of a formula or the results of a calculation.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6394238				0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\> to open the Find & Replace dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7214270				0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\> to expand the dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2186346				0	en-GB	Select "Formulae" or "Values" in the \<emph\>Search in\</emph\> list box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id1331217				0	en-GB	With "Formulae" you will find all parts of the formulae. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id393993				0	en-GB	With "Values" you will find the results of the calculations. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id3163853				0	en-GB	Cell content can be formatted in different ways. For example, a number can be formatted as a currency, to be displayed with a currency symbol. You will see the currency symbol in the cell, but you cannot search for it.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id7359233				0	en-GB	Finding text				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6549272				0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\> to open the Find & Replace dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6529740				0	en-GB	Enter the text to find in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9121982				0	en-GB	Either click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id3808404				0	en-GB	When you click \<emph\>Find\</emph\>, Calc will select the next cell that contains your text. You can watch and edit the text, then click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> again to advance to the next found cell. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2394482				0	en-GB	If you closed the dialogue box, you can press a key combination (\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+F) to find the next cell without opening the dialogue box. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id631733				0	en-GB	By default, Calc searches the current sheet. Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\>, then enable \<emph\>Search in all sheets\</emph\> to search through all sheets of the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7811822				0	en-GB	When you click \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>, Calc selects all cells that contain your entry. Now you can for example set all found cells to bold, or apply a Cell Style to all at once.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id8531449				0	en-GB	The Navigator				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9183935				0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>View - Navigator\</emph\> to open the Navigator window.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id946684				0	en-GB	The Navigator is the main tool for finding and selecting objects.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9607226				0	en-GB	Use the Navigator for inserting objects and links within the same document or from other open documents.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Formatting Spreadsheets				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154125				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>text in cells; formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets;formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>backgrounds;cells and pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders;cells and pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; formatting options for selected cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; number formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>currencies;formats\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154125	6			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"format_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_table.xhp\" name=\"Designing Spreadsheets\"\>Formatting Spreadsheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153912	13			0	en-GB	Formatting Text in a Spreadsheet 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3144772	14			0	en-GB	Select the text you want to format.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155268	15			0	en-GB	Choose the desired text attributes from the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> Bar. You can also choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialogue box will appear in which you can choose various text attributes on the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> tab page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149899	16			0	en-GB	Formatting Numbers in a Spreadsheet				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3159226	17			0	en-GB	Select the cells containing the numbers you want to format.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3150046	18			0	en-GB	To format numbers in the default currency format or as percentages, use the icons on the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> Bar. For other formats, choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\>. You can choose from the preset formats or define your own on the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153483	19			0	en-GB	Formatting Borders and Backgrounds for Cells and Pages				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3154733	20			0	en-GB	You can assign a format to any group of cells by first selecting the cells (for multiple selection, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key when clicking), and then activating the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialogue box in \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Cell\</item\>. In this dialogue box, you can select attributes such as shadows and backgrounds.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3145116	21			0	en-GB	To apply formatting attributes to an entire sheet, choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>. You can define headers and footers, for example, to appear on each printed page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3145389	22			0	en-GB	An image that you have loaded with \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page - Background\</item\> is only visible in print or in the page preview. To display a background image on screen as well, insert the graphic image by choosing \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Picture - From File\</item\> and arrange the image behind the cells by choosing \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Arrange - To Background\</item\>. Use the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\> to select the background image.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id2837916				0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\"\>Number Formatting Options\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id2614215				0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/background.xhp\"\>Backgrounds for Cells\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Formatting Numbers With Decimals				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145367				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>numbers; formatting decimals\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats; numbers in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; number formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defaults; number formats in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>decimal places;formatting numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;numbers with decimals\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;adding/deleting decimal places\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number formats; adding/deleting decimal places in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting; decimal places\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>decimal places; adding/deleting\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145367	4			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"format_value\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_value.xhp\" name=\"Formatting Numbers With Decimals\"\>Formatting Numbers With Decimals\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576	5			0	en-GB	Enter a number into the sheet, for example, 1234.5678. This number will be displayed in the default number format, with two decimal places. You will see 1234.57 when you confirm the entry. Only the display in the document will be rounded off; internally, the number retains all four decimal places after the decimal point.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3154012	12			0	en-GB	To format numbers with decimals:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394	6			0	en-GB	Set the cursor at the number and choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> to start the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3153157	9			0	en-GB	On the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab you will see a selection of predefined number formats. In the bottom right in the dialogue box you will see a preview of how your current number would look if you were to give it a particular format.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3155766				0	en-GB	\<image id=\"img_id3149021\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_numberformatincdecimals.png\" width=\"0.222in\" height=\"0.222in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149021\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3149256	10			0	en-GB	If you only want to modify the number of decimal places displayed, the easiest method is to use the \<emph\>Number Format: Add Decimal Place\</emph\> or \<emph\>Number Format: Delete Decimal Place\</emph\> icons on the Formatting Bar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	User-Defined Number Formats				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143268				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>numbers;user-defined formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting; user-defined numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number formats; millions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>format codes; user-defined number formats\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143268	26			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"format_value_userdef\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_value_userdef.xhp\" name=\"User-Defined Number Formats\"\>User-Defined Number Formats\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150400	1			0	en-GB	You can define your own number formats to display numbers in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767	2			0	en-GB	As an example, to display the number 10,200,000 as 10.2 Million:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868	3			0	en-GB	Select the cells to which you want to apply a new, user-defined format.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664	4			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260	5			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Categories\</emph\> list box select "User-defined".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3148646	6			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Format code\</emph\> text box enter the following code:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3152596	7			0	en-GB	0.0,, "Million"				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764	8			0	en-GB	Click OK.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3155417	9			0	en-GB	The following table shows the effects of rounding, thousands delimiters (,), decimal delimiters (.) and the placeholders # and 0.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3146971	10			0	en-GB	Number				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3154757	11			0	en-GB	.#,, "Million"				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338	12			0	en-GB	0.0,, "Million"				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3146920	13			0	en-GB	#,, "Million"				20130618 17:22:18
