helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Copying Formulae				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151113				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>formulae; copying and pasting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; formulae\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;formulae\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151113	54			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"formula_copy\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/formula_copy.xhp\" name=\"Copying Formulae\"\>Copying Formulae\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3156424	11			0	en-GB	There are various ways to copy a formula. One suggested method is:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150439	30			0	en-GB	Select the cell containing the formula.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319	31			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Copy\</emph\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C to copy it.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3159155	32			0	en-GB	Select the cell into which you want the formula to be copied.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3153728	33			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\> \<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\> \<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\> \</switchinline\>+V. The formula will be positioned in the new cell.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3149961	34			0	en-GB	If you want to copy a formula into multiple cells, there is a quick and easy way to copy into adjacent cell areas:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400	12			0	en-GB	Select the cell containing the formula.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154018	13			0	en-GB	Position the mouse on the bottom right of the highlighted border of the cell, and continue holding down the mouse button until the pointer changes to a cross-hair symbol.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749	14			0	en-GB	With the mouse button pressed, drag it down or to the right over all the cells into which you want to copy the formula.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714	15			0	en-GB	When you release the mouse button, the formula will be copied into the cells and automatically adjusted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3156385	53			0	en-GB	If you do not want values to be automatically adjusted, then hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key when dragging. Formulae, however, are always adjusted accordingly.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Entering Formulae 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150868				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>formula bar; input line\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>input line in formula bar\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulae; inputting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;formulae\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150868	9			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"formula_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/formula_enter.xhp\" name=\"Entering Formulae\"\>Entering Formulae\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id6848353				0	en-GB	You can enter formulae in several ways: using the icons, or by typing on the keyboard, or by a mixture of both methods.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145364	10			0	en-GB	Click the cell in which you want to enter the formula.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150012	11			0	en-GB	Click the \<emph\>Function\</emph\> icon on the Formula Bar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3156441	12			0	en-GB	You will now see an equals sign in the input line and you can begin to enter the formula.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726	3			0	en-GB	After entering the required values, press Enter or click \<emph\>Accept\</emph\> to insert the result in the active cell. If you want to clear your entry in the input line, press Escape or click \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394	8			0	en-GB	You can also enter the values and the formulae directly into the cells, even if you cannot see an input cursor. Formulae must always begin with an equals sign.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id4206976				0	en-GB	You can also press the + or - key on the numeric keypad to start a formula. NumLock must be "on". For example, press the following keys in succession:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id1836909				0	en-GB	+ 5 0 - 8 Enter				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id8171330				0	en-GB	You will see the result \<item type=\"literal\"\>42\</item\> in the cell. The cell contains the formula \<item type=\"literal\"\>=+50-8\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155764	6			0	en-GB	If you are editing a formula with references, the references and the associated cells will be highlighted with the same colour. You can now resize the reference border using the mouse, and the reference in the formula displayed in the input line also changes. \<emph\>Show references in colour\</emph\> can be deactivated under \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060300.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - View\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149210	7			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"tip\"\>If you would like to view the calculation of individual elements of a formula, select the respective elements and press F9. For example, in the formula =SUM(A1:B12)*SUM(C1:D12) select the section SUM(C1:D12) and press F9 to view the subtotal for this area.\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304	5			0	en-GB	If an error occurs when creating the formula, an \<link href=\"text/scalc/05/02140000.xhp\" name=\"error message\"\>error message\</link\> appears in the active cell.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3152993	13			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/scalc/main0206.xhp\" name=\"Formula bar\"\>Formula bar\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Displaying Formulae or Values				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153195				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>formulae; displaying in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>values; displaying in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; displaying formulae/values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>results display vs. formulae display\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>displaying; formulae instead of results\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153195	1			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"formula_value\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/formula_value.xhp\" name=\"Displaying Formulae or Values\"\>Displaying Formulae or Values\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010	2			0	en-GB	If you want to display the formulae in the cells, for example in the form =SUM(A1:B5), proceed as follows:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3151116	3			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120	4			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Display\</emph\> area mark the \<emph\>Formulae\</emph\> check box. Click OK.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396	5			0	en-GB	If you want to view the calculation results instead of the formula, do not mark the Formulae check box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3153157	6			0	en-GB	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060100.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - View\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Calculating With Formulae				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155411				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>formulae;calculating with\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating; with formulae\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>examples;formula calculation\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155411	20			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"formulas\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/formulas.xhp\" name=\"Calculating With Formulae\"\>Calculating With Formulae\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3156281	21			0	en-GB	All formulae begin with an equals sign. The formulae may contain numbers, text, arithmetic operators, logic operators or functions. Other data is also possible, such as format details.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272	39			0	en-GB	Remember that the basic arithmetic operators (+, -, *, /) can be used in formulae using the "Multiplication and Division before Addition and Subtraction" rule. Instead of writing =SUM(A1:B1) you can write =A1+B1.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119	42			0	en-GB	Parentheses (round brackets) can also be used. The result of the formula =(1+2)*3 produces a different result from =1+2*3.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3156285	23			0	en-GB	Here are a few examples of $[officename] Calc formulae:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3154015	24			0	en-GB	=A1+10				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146972	25			0	en-GB	Displays the contents of cell A1 plus 10.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3145643	45			0	en-GB	=A1*16%				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255	46			0	en-GB	Displays 16% of the contents of A1.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146917	47			0	en-GB	=A1 * A2				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146315	48			0	en-GB	Displays the result of the multiplication of A1 and A2.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3154022	26			0	en-GB	=ROUND(A1;1)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150363	27			0	en-GB	Displays the contents of cell A1 rounded to one decimal place.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150209	28			0	en-GB	=EFFECTIVE(5%;12)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150883	29			0	en-GB	Calculates the effective interest for 5% annual nominal interest with 12 payments a year.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146114	33			0	en-GB	=B8-SUM(B10:B14)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3154486	34			0	en-GB	Calculates B8 minus the sum of the cells B10 to B14.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3152890	35			0	en-GB	=SUM(B8; SUM(B10:B14))				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3159171	36			0	en-GB	Calculates the sum of cells B10 to B14 and adds the value to B8.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150109	30			0	en-GB	It is also possible to nest functions in formulae, as shown in the example. You can also nest functions within functions. The Function Wizard assists you with nested functions.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213	44			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060100.xhp\" name=\"Functions list\"\>Functions list\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3152869	43			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060000.xhp\" name=\"Function Wizard\"\>Function Wizard\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Entering Fractions 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155411				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>fractions; entering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; entering fractions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;fractions\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155411	41			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"fraction_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/fraction_enter.xhp\" name=\"Entering Fractions \"\>Entering Fractions \</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968	40			0	en-GB	You can enter a fractional number in a cell and use it for calculation:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155133	42			0	en-GB	Enter "0 1/5" in a cell (without the quotation marks) and press the input key. In the input line above the spreadsheet you will see the value 0.2, which is used for the calculation.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750	43			0	en-GB	If you enter "0 1/2" AutoCorrect causes the three characters 1, / and 2 to be replaced by a single character. The same applies to 1/4 and 3/4. This replacement is defined in \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options - Options\</emph\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145367	44			0	en-GB	If you want to see multi-digit fractions such as "1/10", you must change the cell format to the multi-digit fraction view. Open the context menu of the cell, and choose \<emph\>Format cells\</emph\>. Select "Fraction" from the \<emph\>Category\</emph\> field, and then select "-1234 10/81". You can then enter fractions such as 12/31 or 12/32 - the fractions are, however, automatically reduced, so that in the last example you would see 3/8.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Applying Goal Seek				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145068				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>goal seeking;example\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>equations in goal seek\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating;variables in equations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>variables;calculating equations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>examples;goal seek\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145068	22			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"goalseek\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/goalseek.xhp\" name=\"Applying Goal Seek\"\>Applying Goal Seek\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171	2			0	en-GB	With the help of Goal Seek you can calculate a value that, as part of a formula, leads to the result you specify for the formula. You thus define the formula with several fixed values and one variable value and the result of the formula.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153966	14			0	en-GB	Goal Seek Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3150871	4			0	en-GB	To calculate annual interest (I), create a table with the values for the capital (C), number of years (n), and interest rate (i). The formula is:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3152596	5			0	en-GB	I = C * n* i				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335	15			0	en-GB	Let us assume that the interest rate \<item type=\"literal\"\>i\</item\> of 7.5% and the number of years \<item type=\"literal\"\>n\</item\> (1) will remain constant. However, you want to know how much the investment capital \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\> would have to be modified in order to attain a particular return \<item type=\"literal\"\>I\</item\>. For this example, calculate how much capital \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\> would be required if you want an annual return of £15,000.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960	6			0	en-GB	Enter each of the values for Capital \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\> (an arbitrary value like \<item type=\"literal\"\>£100,000\</item\>), number of years \<item type=\"literal\"\>n \</item\>(\<item type=\"literal\"\>1\</item\>), and interest rate \<item type=\"literal\"\>i\</item\> (\<item type=\"literal\"\>7.5%\</item\>) in one cell each. Enter the formula to calculate the interest \<item type=\"literal\"\>I\</item\> in another cell. Instead of \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\>, \<item type=\"literal\"\>n\</item\>, and \<item type=\"literal\"\>i\</item\> use the \<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/relativ_absolut_ref.xhp\"\>reference to the cell\</link\> with the corresponding value.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3147001	16			0	en-GB	Place the cursor in the cell containing the interest \<item type=\"literal\"\>I\</item\>, and choose \<emph\>Tools - Goal Seek\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Goal Seek\</emph\> dialogue box will appear.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088	17			0	en-GB	The correct cell is already entered in the field \<emph\>Formula Cell\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3166426	18			0	en-GB	Place the cursor in the field \<emph\>Variable Cell\</emph\>. In the sheet, click in the cell that contains the value to be changed, in this example it is the cell with the capital value \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3150369	19			0	en-GB	Enter the expected result of the formula in the \<emph\>Target Value\</emph\> text box. In this example, the value is 15,000. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3146978	20			0	en-GB	A dialogue box appears informing you that the Goal Seek was successful. Click \<emph\>Yes\</emph\> to enter the result in the cell with the variable value.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3149409	23			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06040000.xhp\" name=\"Goal Seek\"\>Goal Seek\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Saving and Opening Sheets in HTML				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150542				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>HTML; sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving; sheets in HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>opening; sheets in HTML\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150542	1			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"html_doc\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/html_doc.xhp\" name=\"Saving and Opening Sheets in HTML\"\>Saving and Opening Sheets in HTML\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154124	2			0	en-GB	Saving Sheets in HTML				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3145785	3			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc saves all the sheets of a Calc document together as an HTML document. At the beginning of the HTML document, a heading and a list of hyperlinks are automatically added which lead to the individual sheets within the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854	4			0	en-GB	Numbers are shown as written. In addition, in the <SDVAL> HTML tag, the exact internal number value is written so that after opening the HTML document with \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> you know you have the exact values.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188	5			0	en-GB	To save the current Calc document as HTML, choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3148645	6			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> list box, in the area with the other \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc filters, choose the file type "HTML Document (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc)".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3154729	7			0	en-GB	Enter a \<emph\>File name\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149379	8			0	en-GB	Opening Sheets in HTML				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3149959	10			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> offers various filters for opening HTML files, which you can select under \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Files of type\</emph\> list box:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969	15			0	en-GB	Choose the file type "HTML Document (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc)" to open in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155446	16			0	en-GB	All \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc options are now available to you. However, not all options that \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc offers for editing can be saved in HTML format.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150370	17			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"File - Open\"\>File - Open\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150199	18			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070000.xhp\" name=\"File - Save As\"\>File - Save As\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Entering a Number with Leading Zeros				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147560				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>zero values; entering leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbers; with leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>integers with leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; changing text/number formats\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formats; changing text/number\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text in cells; changing to numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>converting;text with leading zeros, into numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147560	67			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"integer_leading_zero\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/integer_leading_zero.xhp\" name=\"Entering a Number with Leading Zeros\"\>Entering a Number with Leading Zeros\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3153194	55			0	en-GB	There are various ways to enter integers starting with a zero:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119	56			0	en-GB	Enter the number as a text string. The easiest way is to enter the number starting with an apostrophe (for example, \<item type=\"input\"\>'0987\</item\>). The apostrophe will not appear in the cell, and the number will be formatted as a text string. Because it is a text string, however, you cannot calculate with this number.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154013	57			0	en-GB	Format a cell with a number format such as \<item type=\"input\"\>\\0000\</item\>. This format can be assigned in the \<emph\>Format code\</emph\> field under the \<emph\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</emph\> tab, and defines the cell display as "always put a zero first and then the integer, having at least three places, and filled with zeros at the left if fewer than three digits".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3153158	58			0	en-GB	If you want to apply a numeric format to a column of numbers in text format (for example, text "000123" becomes number "123"), do the following:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377	59			0	en-GB	Select the column in which the digits are found in text format. Set the cell format in that column as "Number".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944	60			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\>               				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510	61			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box, enter \<item type=\"input\"\>^[0-9]\</item\>               				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3155068	62			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> box, enter \<item type=\"input\"\>&\</item\>               				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018	63			0	en-GB	Check \<emph\>Regular expressions\</emph\>               				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382	64			0	en-GB	Check \<emph\>Current selection only\</emph\>               				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3146916	65			0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>Replace All\</emph\>               				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Shortcut Keys (%PRODUCTNAME Calc Accessibility)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145120				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility; %PRODUCTNAME Calc shortcuts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>shortcut keys;%PRODUCTNAME Calc accessibility\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145120	1			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"keyboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/keyboard.xhp\" name=\"Shortcut Keys (%PRODUCTNAME Calc Accessibility)\"\>Shortcut Keys (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc Accessibility)\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760	13			0	en-GB	Refer also to the lists of shortcut keys for \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> in general.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153360	12			0	en-GB	Cell Selection Mode				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150870				0	en-GB	\<image id=\"img_id3150439\" src=\"formula/res/refinp1.png\" width=\"0.1327inch\" height=\"0.1327inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150439\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319	11			0	en-GB	In a text box that has a button to minimise the dialogue box, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F2\</item\> to enter the cell selection mode. Select any number of cells, then press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F2\</item\> again to show the dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272	10			0	en-GB	In the cell selection mode, you can use the common navigation keys to select cells.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148646	14			0	en-GB	Controlling the Outline				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120	15			0	en-GB	You can use the keyboard in \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080000.xhp\" name=\"Outline\"\>Outline\</link\>:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394	16			0	en-GB	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F6\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+F6\</item\> until the vertical or horizontal outline window has the focus.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149379	17			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"keycode\"\>Tab\</item\> - cycle through all visible buttons from top to bottom or from left to right.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286	18			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+Tab\</item\> - cycle through all visible buttons in the opposite direction.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149403	19			0	en-GB	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+1 to Command+8\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl+1 to Ctrl+8\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - show all levels up to the specified number; hide all higher levels.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150329	20			0	en-GB	Use \<item type=\"keycode\"\>+\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>-\</item\> to show or hide the focused outline group.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155446	21			0	en-GB	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> to activate the focused button.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154253	22			0	en-GB	Use \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Up\</item\>, \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Down\</item\>, \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Left\</item\>, or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Right\</item\> arrow to cycle through all buttons in the current level.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147343	8			0	en-GB	Selecting a Drawing Object or a Graphic				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AA				0	en-GB	Choose View - Toolbars - Drawing to open the Drawing toolbar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333	7			0	en-GB	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F6\</item\> until the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar is selected.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150345	4			0	en-GB	If the selection tool is active, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter. This selects the first drawing object or graphic in the sheet.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3159240	3			0	en-GB	With \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6 you move the focus to the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155379	2			0	en-GB	Now you can use \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Tab\</item\> to select the next drawing object or graphic and \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+Tab\</item\> to select the previous one.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Freezing Rows or Columns as Headers				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154684				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>tables; freezing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>title rows; freezing during table split\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows; freezing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; freezing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>freezing rows or columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headers; freezing during table split\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>scrolling prevention in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>windows; splitting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; splitting windows\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154684	1			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"line_fix\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/line_fix.xhp\" name=\"Freezing Rows or Columns as Headers\"\>Freezing Rows or Columns as Headers\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576	2			0	en-GB	If you have long rows or columns of data that extend beyond the viewable area of the sheet, you can freeze some rows or columns, which allows you to see the frozen columns or rows as you scroll through the rest of the data.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3156441	3			0	en-GB	Select the row below, or the column to the right of the row or column that you want to be in the frozen region. All rows above, or all columns to the left of the selection are frozen.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3153158	13			0	en-GB	To freeze both horizontally and vertically, select the \<emph\>cell\</emph\> that is below the row and to the right of the column that you want to freeze.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286	4			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Window - Freeze\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073	5			0	en-GB	To deactivate, choose \<emph\>Window - Freeze\</emph\> again.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335	7			0	en-GB	If the area defined is to be scrollable, apply the \<emph\>Window - Split\</emph\> command.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3147345	8			0	en-GB	If you want to print a certain row on all pages of a document, choose \<emph\>Format - Print ranges - Edit\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3147004	9			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/07090000.xhp\" name=\"Window - Freeze\"\>Window - Freeze\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088	10			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/07080000.xhp\" name=\"Window - Split\"\>Window - Split\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304	11			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05080300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Print ranges - Edit\"\>Format - Print ranges - Edit\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
