helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153361	1			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"mark_cells\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/mark_cells.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Multiple Cells\"\>Selecting Multiple Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145272	2			0	en-GB	Select a rectangular range				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149261	3			0	en-GB	With the mouse button pressed, drag from one corner to the diagonally opposed corner of the range.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151119	4			0	en-GB	Mark a single cell				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975	19			0	en-GB	Do one of the following:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3163710	20			0	en-GB	Click, then Shift-click the cell.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149959	5			0	en-GB	Pressing the mouse button, drag a range across two cells, do not release the mouse button, and then drag back to the first cell. Release the mouse button. You can now move the individual cell by drag-and-drop.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154942	6			0	en-GB	Select various dispersed cells				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id1001200901072060				0	en-GB	Do one of the following:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3156284	7			0	en-GB	Mark at least one cell. Then while pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, click each of the additional cells.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id1001200901072023				0	en-GB	Click the STD / EXT / ADD area in the status bar until it shows ADD. Now click all cells that you want to select.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146971	8			0	en-GB	Switch marking mode				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064	9			0	en-GB	On the status bar, click the box with the legend STD / EXT / ADD to switch the marking mode:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3159264	10			0	en-GB	Field contents				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3155337	11			0	en-GB	Effect of clicking the mouse				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149568	12			0	en-GB	STD				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3148486	13			0	en-GB	A mouse click selects the cell you have clicked on. Unmarks all marked cells.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3150090	14			0	en-GB	EXT				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3150305	15			0	en-GB	A mouse click marks a rectangular range from the current cell to the cell you clicked. Alternatively, Shift-click a cell.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3145587	16			0	en-GB	ADD				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368	17			0	en-GB	A mouse click in a cell adds it to the already marked cells. A mouse click in a marked cell unmarks it. Alternatively, \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>-click the cells.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3154487	18			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/scalc/main0208.xhp\" name=\"Status bar\"\>Status bar\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Entering Matrix Formulae				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153969				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>matrices; entering matrix formulae\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulae; matrix formulae\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;matrix formulae\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153969	13			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"matrixformula\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/matrixformula.xhp\" name=\"Entering Matrix Formulae\"\>Entering Matrix Formulae\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153144	14			0	en-GB	The following is an example of how you can enter a matrix formula, without going into the details of matrix functions.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188	15			0	en-GB	Assume you have entered 10 numbers in Columns A and B (A1:A10 and B1:B10), and would like to calculate the sum of each row in Column C.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154321	16			0	en-GB	Using the mouse, select the range C1:C10, in which the results are to be displayed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260	17			0	en-GB	Press F2, or click in the input line of the Formula bar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944	18			0	en-GB	Enter an equal sign (=).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252	19			0	en-GB	Select the range A1:A10, which contains the first values for the sum formula.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3144767	20			0	en-GB	Press the (+) key on the numeric keypad.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154018	21			0	en-GB	Select the numbers in the second column in cells B1:B10.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150716	22			0	en-GB	End the input with the matrix key combination: Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640	23			0	en-GB	The matrix area is automatically protected against modifications, such as deleting rows or columns. It is, however, possible to edit any formatting, such as the cell background.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Moving Cells by Drag-and-Drop 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155686				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>drag-and-drop; moving cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; moving by drag-and-drop \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns;moving by drag-and-drop\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>moving;cells by drag-and-drop\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;cells, by drag-and-drop\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	hd_id986358				0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"move_dragdrop\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/move_dragdrop.xhp\"\>Moving Cells by Drag-and-Drop\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2760093				0	en-GB	When you drag-and-drop a selection of cells on a Calc sheet, the cells normally overwrite the existing cells in the area where you drop. This is the normal \<emph\>overwrite mode\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id9527268				0	en-GB	When you hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while releasing the mouse button, you enter the \<emph\>insert mode\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id79653				0	en-GB	In insert mode, the existing cells where you drop will be shifted to the right or to the bottom, and the dropped cells are inserted into the now empty positions without overwriting. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id8676717				0	en-GB	The surrounding box of the moved cells looks different in insert mode. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3968932				0	en-GB	In overwrite mode you see all four borders around the selected area. In insert mode you see only the left border when target cells will be shifted to the right. You see only the upper border when target cells will be shifted down. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id7399517				0	en-GB	Whether the target area will be shifted to the right or to the bottom depends on the distance between source and target cells, if you move within the same sheet. It depends on the number of horizontal or vertical cells in the moved area, if you move to a different sheet.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id8040406				0	en-GB	If you move cells in insert mode within the same row (only horizontally), then after insertion of the cells, all cells will be shifted to the left to fill the source area.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2586748				0	en-GB	In both modes, you can hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key, or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift keys while you release the mouse button to insert a copy or a link, respectively.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id5814081				0	en-GB	Keys pressed while releasing the mouse button				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id6581316				0	en-GB	Result				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id9906613				0	en-GB	No key				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2815637				0	en-GB	Cells are moved and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells are emptied.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id6161687				0	en-GB	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id4278389				0	en-GB	Cells are copied and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells stay as they are.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2805566				0	en-GB	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift keys				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id5369121				0	en-GB	Links to the source cells are inserted and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells stay as they are.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id9518723				0	en-GB	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2926419				0	en-GB	Cells are moved and shift the cells in the target area to the right or to the bottom. Source cells are emptied, except if you move within the same rows on the same sheet. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id4021423				0	en-GB	If you move within the same rows on the same sheet, the cells in the target area shift to the right, and then the whole row shifts to fill the source area.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2783898				0	en-GB	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option+Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt+Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>keys				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2785119				0	en-GB	Cells are copied and shift the cells in the target area to the right or to the bottom. Source cells stay as they are.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id584124				0	en-GB	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option+Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt+Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift keys				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id5590990				0	en-GB	Links to the source cells are inserted and shift the cells in the target area to the right or to the bottom. Source cells stay as they are.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Navigating Through Sheet Tabs				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150769				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>sheets; showing multiple\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheet tabs;using\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>views;multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150769	4			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"multi_tables\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/multi_tables.xhp\" name=\"Navigating Through Sheet Tabs\"\>Navigating Through Sheet Tabs\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_id3153771	3			0	en-GB	By default $[officename] displays three sheets "Sheet1" to "Sheet3", in each new spreadsheet. You can switch between sheets in a spreadsheet using the sheet tabs at the bottom of the screen.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AF				0	en-GB	\<image id=\"img_id4829822\" src=\"res/helpimg/sheettabs.png\" width=\"3.3335inch\" height=\"0.7638inch\" localize=\"true\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id4829822\"\>Sheet Tabs\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_id3153144				0	en-GB	\<image id=\"img_id3156441\" src=\"res/helpimg/calcnav.png\" width=\"0.6563inch\" height=\"0.1457inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156441\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396	5			0	en-GB	Use the navigation buttons to display all the sheets belonging to your document. Clicking the button on the far left or the far right displays, respectively, the first or last sheet tab. The middle buttons allow the user to scroll forwards and backwards through all sheet tabs. To display the sheet itself click on the sheet tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_id3149379	6			0	en-GB	If there is insufficient space to display all the sheet tabs, you can increase it by pointing to the separator between the scrollbar and the sheet tabs, pressing the mouse button and, keeping the mouse button pressed, dragging to the right. In doing so you will be sharing the available space between the sheet tabs and horizontal scrollbar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Applying Multiple Operations				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147559				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>multiple operations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>what if operations;two variables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; multiple operations in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data tables; multiple operations in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cross-classified tables\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147559	5			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"multioperation\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/multioperation.xhp\" name=\"Applying Multiple Operations\"\>Applying Multiple Operations\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145171	1			0	en-GB	Multiple Operations in Columns or Rows				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id4123966				0	en-GB	The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Multiple Operations\</item\> command provides a planning tool for "what if" questions. In your spreadsheet, you enter a formula to calculate a result from values that are stored in other cells. Then, you set up a cell range in which you enter some fixed values, and the Multiple Operations command will calculate the results depending on the formula.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3156424	2			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Formula\</emph\> field, enter the cell reference to the formula that applies to the data range. In the \<emph\>Column input cell/Row input cell\</emph\> field, enter the cell reference to the corresponding cell that is part of the formula. This can be explained best by examples:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159153	7			0	en-GB	Examples				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3153189	8			0	en-GB	You produce toys which you sell for £10 each. Each toy costs £2 to make, in addition to which you have fixed costs of £10,000 per year. How much profit will you make in a year if you sell a particular number of toys?				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id6478774				0	en-GB	\<image id=\"img_id1621753\" src=\"res/helpimg/what-if.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1621753\"\>what-if sheet area\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145239	41			0	en-GB	Calculating With One Formula and One Variable				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3146888	42			0	en-GB	To calculate the profit, first enter any number as the quantity (items sold) - in this example 2000. The profit is found from the formula Profit = Quantity * (Selling price - Direct costs) - Fixed costs. Enter this formula in B5.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3157875	43			0	en-GB	In column D enter a number of annual sales values, one below the other; for example, in steps of 500 from 500 to 5000.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3159115	44			0	en-GB	Select the range D2:E11, i.e. the values in column D and the empty cells alongside in column E.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149723	45			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Data - Multiple operations\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149149	46			0	en-GB	With the cursor in the \<emph\>Formulae\</emph\> field, click cell B5.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149355	47			0	en-GB	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Column input cell\</emph\> field and click cell B4. This means that B4, the quantity, is the variable in the formula, which is replaced by the selected column values.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149009	48			0	en-GB	Close the dialogue box with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. You will see the profits for the different quantities in column E.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148725	49			0	en-GB	Calculating with Several Formulae Simultaneously				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3146880	50			0	en-GB	Delete column E.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154675	51			0	en-GB	Enter the following formula in C5: = B5 / B4. You are now calculating the annual profit per item sold.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3148885	52			0	en-GB	Select the range D2:F11, thus three columns.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3147474	53			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Data - Multiple Operations\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154846	54			0	en-GB	With the cursor in the \<emph\>Formulae\</emph\> field, select cells B5 thru C5.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3153931	55			0	en-GB	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Column input cell\</emph\> field and click cell B4.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3150862	56			0	en-GB	Close the dialogue box with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. You will now see the profits in column E and the annual profit per item in column F.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146139	3			0	en-GB	Multiple Operations Across Rows and Columns				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3148584	4			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> allows you to carry out joint multiple operations for columns and rows in so-called cross-tables. The formula cell must refer to both the data range arranged in rows and the one arranged in columns. Select the range defined by both data ranges and call the multiple operation dialogue box. Enter the reference to the formula in the \<emph\>Formula\</emph\> field. The \<emph\>Row input cell\</emph\> field is used to enter the reference to the first cell of the range arranged in rows, and the \<emph\>Column input cell\</emph\> field the first cell of the range arranged in columns.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149949	57			0	en-GB	Calculating with Two Variables				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154808	58			0	en-GB	Consider columns A and B of the sample table above. You now want to vary not just the quantity produced annually, but also the selling price, and you are interested in the profit in each case.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149731	59			0	en-GB	Expand the table shown above. D2 thru D11 contain the numbers 500, 1000 and so on, up to 5000. In E1 through H1 enter the numbers 8, 10, 15 and 20.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3152810	95			0	en-GB	Select the range D1:H11.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3153620	96			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Data - Multiple Operations\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149981	97			0	en-GB	With the cursor in the \<emph\>Formulae\</emph\> field, click cell B5.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113	98			0	en-GB	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Row input cell\</emph\> field and click cell B1. This means that B1, the selling price, is the horizontally entered variable (with the values 8, 10, 15 and 20).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154049	99			0	en-GB	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Column input cell\</emph\> field and click in B4. This means that B4, the quantity, is the vertically entered variable.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149141	100			0	en-GB	Close the dialogue box with OK. You will see the profits for the different selling prices in the range E2:H11.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3155104	101			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12060000.xhp\" name=\"Multiple operations\"\>Multiple operations\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Applying Multiple Sheets				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154759				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>sheets; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; selecting multiple\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>appending sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating;multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154759	9			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"multitables\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/multitables.xhp\" name=\"Applying Multiple Sheets\"\>Applying Multiple Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148576	10			0	en-GB	Inserting a Sheet				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3154731	4			0	en-GB	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Sheet\</item\> to insert a new sheet or an existing sheet from another file.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id05092009140203598				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens a dialogue box where you can assign macros to sheet events.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id05092009140203523				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens a window where you can assign a colour to the sheet tab.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id050920091402035				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to select all sheets in the document.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200914020391				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to deselect all sheets in the document, except the current sheet.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154491	11			0	en-GB	Selecting Multiple Sheets				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3145251	6			0	en-GB	The sheet tab of the current sheet is always visible in white in front of the other sheet tabs. The other sheet tabs are grey when they are not selected. By clicking other sheet tabs while pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>you can select multiple sheets.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B7				0	en-GB	You can use Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Page Up or Page Down to select multiple sheets using the keyboard.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155600	12			0	en-GB	Undoing a Selection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969	13			0	en-GB	To undo the selection of a sheet, click its sheet tab again while pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key. The sheet that is currently visible cannot be removed from the selection.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156382	15			0	en-GB	Calculating Across Multiple Sheets				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333	16			0	en-GB	You can refer to a range of sheets in a formula by specifying the first and last sheet of the range, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>=SUM(Sheet1.A1:Sheet3.A1) \</item\>sums up all A1 cells on Sheet1 through Sheet3.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Inserting and Editing Comments				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153968				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>comments; on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells;comments\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>remarks on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;comments on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>viewing;comments on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>displaying; comments\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153968	31			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"note_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/note_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting and Editing Comments\"\>Inserting and Editing Comments\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150440	32			0	en-GB	You can assign a comment to each cell by choosing \<link href=\"text/shared/01/04050000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Comment\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Comment\</emph\>\</link\>. The comment is indicated by a small red square, the comment indicator, in the cell.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750	34			0	en-GB	The comment is visible whenever the mouse pointer is over the cell, provided you have activated \<emph\>Help - Tips\</emph\> or - \<emph\>Extended Tips\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575	33			0	en-GB	When you select the cell, you can choose \<emph\>Show Comment\</emph\> from the context menu of the cell. Doing so keeps the comment visible until you deactivate the \<emph\>Show Comment\</emph\> command from the same context menu.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958	35			0	en-GB	To edit a permanently visible comment, just click in it. If you delete the entire text of the comment, the comment itself is deleted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN10699				0	en-GB	Move or resize each comment as you like.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069D				0	en-GB	Format each comment by specifying background colour, transparency, border style, and text alignment. Choose the commands from the context menu of the comment.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764	38			0	en-GB	To show or hide the comment indicator, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\> and mark or unmark the \<emph\>Comment indicator\</emph\> check box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150715	39			0	en-GB	To display a help tip for a selected cell, use \<emph\>Data - Validity - Input Help\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707	36			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/04050000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Comment\"\>Insert - Comment\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Converting Text to Numbers				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145068				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>formats; text as numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>time format conversion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>date formats;conversion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>converting;text, into numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id0908200901265171				0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"numbers_text\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/numbers_text.xhp\" name=\"Converting Text to Numbers\"\>Converting Text to Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265127				0	en-GB	Calc converts text inside cells to the respective numeric values if an unambiguous conversion is possible. If no conversion is possible, Calc returns a #VALUE! error.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265196				0	en-GB	Only integer numbers including exponent are converted, and ISO 8601 dates and times in their extended formats with separators. Anything else, like fractional numbers with decimal separators or dates other than ISO 8601, is not converted, as the text string would be locale dependent. Leading and trailing blanks are ignored.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265220				0	en-GB	The following ISO 8601 formats are converted:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265288				0	en-GB	CCYY-MM-DD				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265267				0	en-GB	CCYY-MM-DDThh:mm				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265248				0	en-GB	CCYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265374				0	en-GB	CCYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss,s				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265327				0	en-GB	CCYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss.s				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265399				0	en-GB	hh:mm				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265347				0	en-GB	hh:mm:ss				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265349				0	en-GB	hh:mm:ss,s				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265342				0	en-GB	hh:mm:ss.s				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265491				0	en-GB	The century code CC may not be omitted. Instead of the T date and time separator, exactly one space character may be used.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265467				0	en-GB	If a date is given, it must be a valid Gregorian calendar date. In this case the optional time must be in the range 00:00 to 23:59:59.99999...				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265420				0	en-GB	If only a time string is given, it may have an hours value of more than 24, while minutes and seconds can have a maximum value of 59.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265448				0	en-GB	The conversion is done for single arguments only, as in =A1+A2, or ="1E2"+1. Cell range arguments are not affected, so SUM(A1:A2) differs from A1+A2 if at least one of the two cells contain a convertible string.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id090820090126540				0	en-GB	Strings inside formulae are also converted, such as in ="1999-11-22"+42, which returns the date 42 days after November 22nd, 1999. Calculations involving localised dates as strings inside the formula return an error. For example, the localised date string "11/22/1999" or "22.11.1999" cannot be used for the automatic conversion.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id1005200903485368				0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id1005200903485359				0	en-GB	In A1 enter the text \<item type=\"literal\"\>'1e2\</item\> (which is converted to the number 100 internally).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id1005200903485341				0	en-GB	In A2 enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>=A1+1\</item\> (which correctly results in 101).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265544				0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cells - Numbers\"\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
