helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153194	1			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"print_exact\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/print_exact.xhp\" name=\"Defining Number of Pages for Printing\"\>Defining Number of Pages for Printing\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3153771	2			0	en-GB	If a sheet is too large for a single printed page, $[officename] Calc will print the current sheet evenly divided over several pages. Since the automatic page break does not always take place in the optimal position, you can define the page distribution yourself.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3159155	3			0	en-GB	Go to the sheet to be printed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3150012	4			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>View - Page Break Preview\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974	5			0	en-GB	You will see the automatic distribution of the sheet across the print pages. The automatically created print ranges are indicated by dark blue lines, and the user-defined ones by light blue lines. The page breaks (line breaks and column breaks) are marked as black lines.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3152578	6			0	en-GB	You can move the blue lines with the mouse. You will find further options in the Context menu, including adding an additional print range, removing the scaling and inserting additional manual line and column breaks.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073	7			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"View - Page Break Preview\"\>View - Page Break Preview\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Printing Sheets in Landscape Format				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153418				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>printing; sheet selections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; printing in landscape\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing; landscape\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>landscape printing\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153418	1			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"print_landscape\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/print_landscape.xhp\" name=\"Printing Sheets in Landscape Format\"\>Printing Sheets in Landscape Format\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3149257	2			0	en-GB	In order to print a sheet you have a number of interactive options available under \<emph\>View - Page Break Preview\</emph\>. Drag the delimiter lines to define the range of printed cells on each page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963	15			0	en-GB	To print in landscape format, proceed as follows:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3154020	3			0	en-GB	Go to the sheet to be printed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3150786	4			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3150089	5			0	en-GB	The command is not visible if the sheet has been opened with write protection on. In that case, click the \<emph\>Edit File\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3166430	6			0	en-GB	Select the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab. Select the \<emph\>Landscape\</emph\> paper format and click OK.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3150885	7			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>. You will see the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3156288	8			0	en-GB	Depending on the printer driver and the operating system, it may be necessary to click the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> button and to change your printer to landscape format there.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3149404	9			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Print \</emph\>dialogue box, in the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab page, select the contents to be printed:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3153305	10			0	en-GB	\<emph\>All sheets\</emph\> - All sheets will be printed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3148871	12			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Selected sheets\</emph\> - Only the selected sheets will be printed. All sheets whose names (at the bottom on the sheet tabs) are selected will be printed. By pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while clicking a sheet name you can change this selection.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3764763				0	en-GB	\<emph\>Selected cells\</emph\> - All selected cells are printed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id5538804				0	en-GB	From all the paper pages that result from the above selection, you can select the range of paper pages to be printed:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id14343				0	en-GB	\<emph\>All pages\</emph\> - Print all resulting pages.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3148699	11			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Pages\</emph\> - Enter the pages to be printed. The pages will also be numbered from the first sheet onwards. If you see in the Page Break Preview that Sheet1 will be printed on 4 pages and you want to print the first two pages of Sheet2, enter 5-6 here.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3145076	13			0	en-GB	If under \<emph\>Format - Print ranges\</emph\> you have defined one or more print ranges, only the contents of these print ranges will be printed.				20130618 17:22:18
