helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN108D7				0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"printranges\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/printranges.xhp\"\>Defining Print Ranges on a Sheet\</link\> \</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN108F5				0	en-GB	You can define which range of cells on a spreadsheet to print.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN108FB				0	en-GB	The cells on the sheet that are not part of the defined print range are not printed or exported. Sheets without a defined print range are not printed and not exported to a PDF file, unless the document uses the Microsoft Excel file format.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077A				0	en-GB	For files opened in Microsoft Excel format, all sheets that do not contain a defined print range are printed. The same behaviour occurs when you export the Microsoft Excel formatted spreadsheet to a PDF file.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN108FE				0	en-GB	To Define a Print Range				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10905				0	en-GB	Select the cells that you want to print.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10909				0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Format - Print Ranges - Define\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10910				0	en-GB	To Add Cells to a Print Range				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10917				0	en-GB	Select the cells that you want to add to the existing print range.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN1091B				0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Format - Print Ranges - Add\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
