helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145068	46			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"text_numbers\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/text_numbers.xhp\" name=\"Formatting Numbers as Text\"\>Formatting Numbers as Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280	43			0	en-GB	You can format numbers as text in $[officename] Calc. Open the context menu of a cell or range of cells and choose \<emph\>Format Cells - Numbers\</emph\>, then select "Text" from the \<emph\>Category\</emph\> list. Any numbers subsequently entered into the formatted range are interpreted as text. The display of these "numbers" is left-justified, just as with other text.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377	44			0	en-GB	If you have already entered normal numbers in cells and have afterwards changed the format of the cells to "Text", the numbers will remain normal numbers. They will not be converted. Only numbers entered afterwards, or numbers which are then edited, will become text numbers.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3144765	45			0	en-GB	If you decide to enter a number directly as a text string, enter an apostrophe (') first. For example, for years in column headings, you can enter '1999, '2000 and '2001. The apostrophe is not visible in the cell, it only indicates that the entry is to be recognised as text and not as a number. This is useful if, for example, you enter a telephone number or bank account number that begins with a zero (0), because a zero (0) at the beginning of a sequence of digits is removed in normal number formats.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3156284	47			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cells - Numbers\"\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Rotating Text				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151112				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>cells; rotating text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rotating; text in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text in cells; writing vertically\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151112	1			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"text_rotate\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/text_rotate.xhp\" name=\"Rotating Text\"\>Rotating Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171	2			0	en-GB	Select the cells whose text you want to rotate.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155133	3			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\>. You will see the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854	4			0	en-GB	Click the \<emph\>Alignment\</emph\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147426	5			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Text direction\</emph\> area use the mouse to select in the preview wheel the direction in which the text is to be rotated. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3148456	7			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05020000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cells\"\>Format - Cells\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
