helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149528	20			0	en-GB	Date				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3150887	21			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_DATE\"\>Creates a date series using the defined increment and end date.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150202	22			0	en-GB	AutoFill				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3156288	23			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_AUTOFILL\"\>Forms a series directly in the sheet.\</ahelp\> The AutoFill function takes account of customised lists. For example, by entering \<emph\>January\</emph\> in the first cell, the series is completed using the list defined under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - Sort Lists\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3155811	24			0	en-GB	AutoFill tries to complete a value series by using a defined pattern. The series 1, 3, 5 is automatically completed with 7, 9, 11, 13 and so on. Date and time series are completed accordingly; for example, after 01/01/1999 and 15/01/1999, an interval of 14 days is used.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148700	25			0	en-GB	Unit of Time				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153308	26			0	en-GB	In this area you can specify the desired unit of time. This area is only active if the \<emph\>Date\</emph\> option has been chosen in the \<emph\>Series type\</emph\> area.				20130618 17:22:18
