helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153122	48			0	en-GB	In this page you can view the structure of the function.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149350	4			0	en-GB	If you start the \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\> while the cell cursor is positioned in a cell that already contains a function, the \<emph\>Structure\</emph\> tab is opened and shows the composition of the current formula.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149014	49			0	en-GB	Structure				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150481	50			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SC_FAP_STRUCT\"\>Displays a hierarchical representation of the current function.\</ahelp\> You can hide or show the arguments by a click on the plus or minus sign in front.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148886	63			0	en-GB	Blue dots denote correctly entered arguments. Red dots indicate incorrect data types. For example: if the SUM function has one argument entered as a text string, this is highlighted in red as SUM only permits number entries.				20130618 17:22:18
