helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155260	43			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ANZAHLLEEREZELLEN\"\>Returns the number of empty cells.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145144	44			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153931	45			0	en-GB	COUNTBLANK(Range)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3149512	46			0	en-GB	Returns the number of empty cells in the cell range \<emph\>Range\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146139	47			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3148586	48			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTBLANK(A1:B2)\</item\> returns 4 if cells A1, A2, B1 and B2 are all empty.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153114				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>ACOS function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153114	50			0	en-GB	ACOS				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145163	51			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ARCCOS\"\>Returns the inverse trigonometric cosine (arc cosine) of a number.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153565	52			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150020	53			0	en-GB	ACOS(Number)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159134	54			0	en-GB	This function returns the inverse trigonometric cosine of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, that is the angle (in radians) whose cosine is Number. The angle returned is in the range 0.0 to +PI.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id679647				0	en-GB	To return the angle in degrees, use the DEGREES function.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149882	55			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150128	56			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ACOS(-1)\</item\> returns 3.14159265358979 (PI radians)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id8792382				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DEGREES(ACOS(0.5))\</item\> returns 60. The cosine of 60 degrees is 0.5.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145355				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>ACOSH function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
