helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145295	62			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151017	63			0	en-GB	ACOSH(Number)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3149000	64			0	en-GB	This function returns the inverse hyperbolic cosine of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, that is the number whose hyperbolic cosine is Number. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6393932				0	en-GB	 Number must be greater than or equal to +1.0.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150566	65			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145629	66			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ACOSH(1)\</item\> returns 0.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id951567				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ACOSH(COSH(4))\</item\> returns 4.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149027				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>ACOT function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149027	70			0	en-GB	ACOT				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155818	71			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ARCCOT\"\>Returns the inverse trigonometric cotangent (arc cotangent) of the given number.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153225	72			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158419	73			0	en-GB	ACOT(Number)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154948	74			0	en-GB	This function returns the inverse trigonometric cotangent of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, that is the angle (in radians) whose cotangent is Number. The angle returned is in the range 0.0 to +PI.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5834528				0	en-GB	To return the angle in degrees, use the DEGREES function.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147538	75			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155375	76			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ACOT(1)\</item\> returns 0.785398163397448 (PI/4 radians).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id8589434				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DEGREES(ACOT(1))\</item\> returns 45. The tangent of 45 degrees is 1. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148426				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>ACOTH function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
