helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150964	94			0	en-GB	This function returns the inverse trigonometric sine of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, that is the angle (in radians) whose sine is Number. The angle returned is in the range -PI/2 to +PI/2.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id203863				0	en-GB	To return the angle in degrees, use the DEGREES function.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149448	95			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3156100	96			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ASIN(0)\</item\> returns 0.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6853846				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ASIN(1)\</item\> returns 1.5707963267949 (PI/2 radians). 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id8772240				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DEGREES(ASIN(0.5))\</item\> returns 30. The sine of 30 degrees is 0.5.				20130618 17:22:18
