helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155139	259			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Value\</emph\> is the value to be checked.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9027680				0	en-GB	If Value is not an integer any digits after the decimal point are ignored. The sign of Value is also ignored.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163723	260			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155345	261			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISODD(33)\</item\> returns TRUE				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9392986				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISODD(48)\</item\> returns FALSE				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5971251				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISODD(3.999)\</item\> returns TRUE				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id4136478				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISODD(-3.1)\</item\> returns TRUE				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145213				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>LCM function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>least common multiples\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lowest common multiples\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145213	265			0	en-GB	LCM				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3146814	266			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KGV\"\>Returns the least common multiple of one or more integers.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148632	267			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3147279	268			0	en-GB	LCM(Integer1; Integer2; ... Integer30)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3156348	269			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Integer1; Integer2; ... Integer30\</emph\> are 1 to 30 integers for which the lowest common multiple is to be calculated.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156431	270			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154914	271			0	en-GB	If you enter the numbers \<item type=\"input\"\>512\</item\>, \<item type=\"input\"\>1024\</item\> and \<item type=\"input\"\>2000\</item\> in the Integer 1, 2 and 3 text boxes, 128000 will be returned as the result.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154230				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>LCM_ADD function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
