helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145122	689			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145135	690			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LCM_ADD(5;15;25)\</item\> returns 75.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155802				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>COMBIN function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of combinations\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155802	273			0	en-GB	COMBIN				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3156172	274			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KOMBINATIONEN\"\>Returns the number of combinations for a given number of objects (without repetition).\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156193	275			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150223	276			0	en-GB	COMBIN(Count1; Count2)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150313	277			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Count1\</emph\> is the number of items in the set.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153830	278			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Count2\</emph\> is the number of items to choose from the set.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6807458				0	en-GB	COMBIN returns the number of ordered ways to choose these items. For example if there are 3 items A, B and C in a set, you can choose 2 items in 3 different ways, namely AB, AC and BC.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7414471				0	en-GB	COMBIN implements the formula: Count1!/(Count2!*(Count1-Count2)!)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153171	279			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153517	280			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COMBIN(3;2)\</item\> returns 3.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150284				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>COMBINA function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of combinations with repetitions\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150284	282			0	en-GB	COMBINA				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157894	283			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KOMBINATIONEN2\"\>Returns the number of combinations of a subset of items including repetitions.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145752	284			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145765	285			0	en-GB	COMBINA(Count1; Count2)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153372	286			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Count1\</emph\> is the number of items in the set.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155544	287			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Count2\</emph\> is the number of items to choose from the set.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1997131				0	en-GB	COMBINA returns the number of unique ways to choose these items, where the order of choosing is irrelevant, and repetition of items is allowed. For example if there are 3 items A, B and C in a set, you can choose 2 items in 6 different ways, namely AB, BA, AC, CA, BC and CB.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2052064				0	en-GB	COMBINA implements the formula: (Count1+Count2-1)! / (Count2!(Count1-1)!)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154584	288			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152904	289			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COMBINA(3;2)\</item\> returns 6.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156086				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>TRUNC function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>decimal places;cutting off\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156086	291			0	en-GB	TRUNC				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157866	292			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KUERZEN\"\>Truncates a number by removing decimal places.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148499	293			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3148511	294			0	en-GB	TRUNC(Number; Count)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150796	295			0	en-GB	Returns \<emph\>Number\</emph\> with at most \<emph\>Count\</emph\> decimal places. Excess decimal places are simply removed, irrespective of sign.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150816	296			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"literal\"\>TRUNC(Number; 0)\</item\> behaves as \<item type=\"literal\"\>INT(Number)\</item\> for positive numbers, but effectively rounds towards zero for negative numbers.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3148548	557			0	en-GB	The \<emph\>visible\</emph\> decimal places of the result correspond to the number of decimal places specified in \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060500.xhp\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - Calculate\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152555	297			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152569	298			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=TRUNC(1.239;2)\</item\> returns 1.23. The 9 is omitted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7050080				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=TRUNC(-1.234999;3)\</item\> returns -1.234. All the 9s are omitted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153601				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>LN function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>natural logarithm\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153601	301			0	en-GB	LN				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154974	302			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_LN\"\>Returns the natural logarithm based on the constant e of a number.\</ahelp\> The constant e has a value of approximately 2.71828182845904.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154993	303			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155284	304			0	en-GB	LN(Number)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155297	305			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value for which the natural logarithm is to be calculated.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153852	306			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153866	307			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LN(3)\</item\> returns the natural logarithm of 3 (approximately 1.0986).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5747245				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LN(EXP(321))\</item\> returns 321.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3109813				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>LOG function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>logarithms\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3109813	311			0	en-GB	LOG				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3109841	312			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_LOG\"\>Returns the logarithm of a number to the specified base.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144719	313			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144732	314			0	en-GB	LOG(Number; Base)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144746	315			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value for which the logarithm is to be calculated.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152840	316			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Base\</emph\> (optional) is the base for the logarithm calculation. If omitted, Base 10 is assumed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152860	317			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154429	318			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LOG(10;3)\</item\> returns the logarithm to base 3 of 10 (approximately 2.0959).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5577562				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LOG(7^4;7)\</item\> returns 4.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154187				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>LOG10 function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>base-10 logarithm\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154187	322			0	en-GB	LOG10				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155476	323			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_LOG10\"\>Returns the base-10 logarithm of a number.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155494	324			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159294	325			0	en-GB	LOG10(Number)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159308	326			0	en-GB	Returns the logarithm to base 10 of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159328	327			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157916	328			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LOG10(5)\</item\> returns the base-10 logarithm of 5 (approximately 0.69897).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152518				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>CEILING function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rounding;up to multiples of significance\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152518	332			0	en-GB	CEILING				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153422	558			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_OBERGRENZE\"\>Rounds a number up to the nearest multiple of Significance.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153440	334			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153454	335			0	en-GB	CEILING(Number; Significance; Mode)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153467	336			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the number that is to be rounded up.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155000	337			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Significance\</emph\> is the number that the value is to be rounded up to a multiple of.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155020	559			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Mode\</emph\> is an optional value. If the Mode parameter is supplied and is not equal to zero and if Number and Significance are negative, rounding up is carried out based on the absolute value of Number. This parameter is omitted when exporting to Microsoft Excel since Excel does not support a third parameter for this function.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163792	629			0	en-GB	If both parameters Number and Significance are negative and the Mode value is equal to zero or is not given, the results in $[officename] and Microsoft Excel will differ after the import has been completed. If you export the spreadsheet to Microsoft Excel, use Mode = 1 to see the same results in Microsoft Excel as in Calc.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145697	338			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145710	339			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CEILING(-11;-2)\</item\> returns -10				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145725	340			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CEILING(-11;-2;0)\</item\> returns -10				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145740	341			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CEILING(-11;-2;1)\</item\> returns -12				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3157762				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>PI function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157762	343			0	en-GB	PI				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157790	344			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_PI\"\>Returns 3.14159265358979..., the value of the mathematical constant PI to 14 decimal places.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157809	345			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157822	346			0	en-GB	PI()				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157836	347			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152370	348			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=PI()\</item\> returns 3.14159265358979... as a rounded value.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152418				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>MULTINOMIAL function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152418	635			0	en-GB	MULTINOMIAL				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152454	636			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_MULTINOMIAL\"\> Returns the factorial of the sum of the arguments divided by the product of the factorials of the arguments.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155646	637			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155660	638			0	en-GB	MULTINOMIAL(Number(s))				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155673	639			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Number(s)\</emph\> is a list of 1 to 30 numbers.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155687	640			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155701	641			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MULTINOMIAL(F11:H11)\</item\> returns 1260, if F11 to H11 contain the values \<item type=\"input\"\>2\</item\>, \<item type=\"input\"\>3\</item\> and \<item type=\"input\"\>4\</item\>. This corresponds to the formula =(2+3+4)! / (2!*3!*4!)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155717				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>POWER function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155717	350			0	en-GB	POWER				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159495	351			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_POTENZ\"\>Returns the result of a number raised to a power.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159513	352			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159526	353			0	en-GB	POWER(Base; Power) or Base ^ Power				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159540	354			0	en-GB	Returns \<emph\>Base\</emph\> raised to the power of \<emph\>Power\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5081637				0	en-GB	The same result may be achieved by using the exponentiation operator ^:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9759514				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"literal\"\>Base^Power\</item\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159580	356			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159594	357			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=POWER(4;3)\</item\> returns 64, which is 4 to the power of 3.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1614429				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=4^3\</item\> also returns 4 to the power of 3.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152651				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>SERIESSUM function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152651	642			0	en-GB	SERIESSUM				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152688	643			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Returns a sum of powers of the number x\</ahelp\> in accordance with the following formula:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152708	644			0	en-GB	SERIESSUM(x;n;m;coefficients) = coefficient_1*x^n + coefficient_2*x^(n+m) + coefficient_3*x^(n+2m) +...+ coefficient_i*x^(n+(i-1)m)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152724	645			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_idN11BD9				0	en-GB	SERIESSUM(X; N; M; Coefficients)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152737	646			0	en-GB	\<emph\>X\</emph\> is the input value for the power series.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144344	647			0	en-GB	\<emph\>N\</emph\> is the initial power				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144357	648			0	en-GB	\<emph\>M\</emph\> is the increment by which to increase N				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144370	649			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Coefficients\</emph\> is a series of coefficients. For each coefficient the series sum is extended by one section.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3144386				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>PRODUCT function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers;multiplying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>multiplying;numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144386	361			0	en-GB	PRODUCT				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144414	362			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_PRODUKT\"\>Multiplies all the numbers given as arguments and returns the product.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144433	363			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144446	364			0	en-GB	PRODUCT(Number1; Number2; ... Number30)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144460	365			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Number1; Number2; ... Number30\</emph\> are 1 to 30 arguments whose product is to be calculated.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1589098				0	en-GB	PRODUCT returns Number1 * Number2 * Number_3 * ... Number_N				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144480	366			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144494	367			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=PRODUCT(2;3;4)\</item\> returns 24.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3160340				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>SUMSQ function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>square number additions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sums;of square numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3160340	369			0	en-GB	SUMSQ				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3160368	370			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_QUADRATESUMME\"\>If you want to calculate the sum of the squares of numbers (totalling up of the squares of the arguments), enter these into the text fields.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3160388	371			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3160402	372			0	en-GB	SUMSQ(Number1; Number2; ... Number30)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3160415	373			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Number1; Number2; ... Number30\</emph\> are 1 to 30 arguments the sum of whose squares is to be calculated.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3160436	374			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3160449	375			0	en-GB	If you enter the numbers \<item type=\"input\"\>2\</item\>, \<item type=\"input\"\>3\</item\> and \<item type=\"input\"\>4\</item\> in the Number 1, 2 and 3 text boxes, 29 is returned as the result.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3158247				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>MOD function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>remainders of divisions\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158247	387			0	en-GB	MOD				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158276	388			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_REST\"\>Returns the remainder after a number is divided by a divisor.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158294	389			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158308	390			0	en-GB	MOD(Dividend; Divisor)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158321	391			0	en-GB	For integer arguments this function returns \<emph\>Dividend\</emph\> modulo \<emph\>Divisor\</emph\>, that is the remainder when \<emph\>Dividend\</emph\> is divided by \<emph\>Divisor\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158341	392			0	en-GB	This function is implemented as \<item type=\"literal\"\>Dividend - Divisor * INT(Dividend/Divisor)\</item\> and this formula gives the result if the arguments are not integer.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158361	393			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158374	394			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MOD(22;3)\</item\> returns 1, the remainder when 22 is divided by 3.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1278420				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MOD(11.25;2.5)\</item\> returns 1.25.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3144592				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>QUOTIENT function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>divisions\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144592	652			0	en-GB	QUOTIENT				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144627	653			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_QUOTIENT\"\>Returns the integer result of a division operation.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144646	654			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144659	655			0	en-GB	QUOTIENT(Numerator; Denominator)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9038972				0	en-GB	Returns the integer part of \<emph\>Numerator\</emph\> divided by \<emph\>Denominator\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7985168				0	en-GB	QUOTIENT is equivalent to \<item type=\"literal\"\>INT(Numerator/Denominator)\</item\>, except that it may report errors with different error codes.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144674	656			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144687	657			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=QUOTIENT(11;3)\</item\> returns 3. The remainder of 2 is omitted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3144702				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>RADIANS function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting;degrees, into radians\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144702	377			0	en-GB	RADIANS				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158025	378			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_RAD\"\>Converts degrees to radians.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158042	379			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158055	380			0	en-GB	RADIANS(Number)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158069	381			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the angle in degrees to be converted to radians.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id876186				0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3939634				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=RADIANS(90)\</item\> returns 1.5707963267949, which is PI/2 to Calc's accuracy.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3158121				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>ROUND function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158121	398			0	en-GB	ROUND				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158150	399			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_RUNDEN\"\>Returns a number rounded to a certain number of decimal places.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158169	400			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158182	401			0	en-GB	ROUND(Number; Count)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158196	402			0	en-GB	Returns \<emph\>Number\</emph\> rounded to \<emph\>Count\</emph\> decimal places. If \<emph\>Count\</emph\> is omitted or zero, the function rounds to the nearest integer. If \<emph\>Count\</emph\> is negative, the function rounds to the nearest 10, 100, 1000, etc.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id599688				0	en-GB	This function rounds to the nearest number. See ROUNDDOWN and ROUNDUP for alternatives.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145863	404			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145876	405			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUND(2.348;2)\</item\> returns 2.35				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145899	406			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUND(-32.4834;3)\</item\> returns -32.483. Change the cell format to see all decimals.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1371501				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUND(2.348;0)\</item\> returns 2.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id4661702				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUND(2.5)\</item\> returns 3. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7868892				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUND(987.65;-2)\</item\> returns 1000.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145991				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>ROUNDDOWN function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145991	24			0	en-GB	ROUNDDOWN				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3146020	25			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ABRUNDEN\"\>Rounds a number down, towards zero, to a certain precision.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146037	26			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3146051	27			0	en-GB	ROUNDDOWN(Number; Count)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3146064	28			0	en-GB	Returns \<emph\>Number\</emph\> rounded down (towards zero) to \<emph\>Count\</emph\> decimal places. If Count is omitted or zero, the function rounds down to an integer. If Count is negative, the function rounds down to the next 10, 100, 1000, etc.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2188787				0	en-GB	This function rounds towards zero. See ROUNDUP and ROUND for alternatives.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163164	30			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163178	31			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDDOWN(1.234;2)\</item\> returns 1.23.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5833307				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDDOWN(45.67;0)\</item\> returns 45.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7726676				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDDOWN(-45.67)\</item\> returns -45.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3729361				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDDOWN(987.65;-2)\</item\> returns 900.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3163268				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>ROUNDUP function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163268	140			0	en-GB	ROUNDUP				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163297	141			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_AUFRUNDEN\"\>Rounds a number up, away from zero, to a certain precision.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163315	142			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163328	143			0	en-GB	ROUNDUP(Number; Count)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163342	144			0	en-GB	Returns \<emph\>Number\</emph\> rounded up (away from zero) to \<emph\>Count\</emph\> decimal places. If Count is omitted or zero, the function rounds up to an integer. If Count is negative, the function rounds up to the next 10, 100, 1000, etc.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9573961				0	en-GB	This function rounds away from zero. See ROUNDDOWN and ROUND for alternatives.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163381	146			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144786	147			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDUP(1.1111;2)\</item\> returns 1.12.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7700430				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDUP(1.2345;1)\</item\> returns 1.3.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1180455				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDUP(45.67;0)\</item\> returns 46.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3405560				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDUP(-45.67)\</item\> returns -46.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3409527				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDUP(987.65;-2)\</item\> returns 1000.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3144877				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>SIN function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144877	408			0	en-GB	SIN				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144906	409			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SIN\"\>Returns the sine of the given angle (in radians).\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144923	410			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144937	411			0	en-GB	SIN(Number)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144950	412			0	en-GB	Returns the (trigonometric) sine of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, the angle in radians.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id8079470				0	en-GB	To return the sine of an angle in degrees, use the RADIANS function.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144969	413			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144983	414			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SIN(PI()/2)\</item\> returns 1, the sine of PI/2 radians.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3916440				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SIN(RADIANS(30))\</item\> returns 0.5, the sine of 30 degrees.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3163397				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>SINH function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163397	418			0	en-GB	SINH				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163426	419			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SINHYP\"\>Returns the hyperbolic sine of a number.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163444	420			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163457	421			0	en-GB	SINH(Number)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163471	422			0	en-GB	Returns the hyperbolic sine of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163491	423			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163504	424			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SINH(0)\</item\> returns 0, the hyperbolic sine of 0.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3163596				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>SUM function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adding;numbers in cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163596	428			0	en-GB	SUM				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163625	429			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SUMME\"\>Adds all the numbers in a range of cells.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163643	430			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163656	431			0	en-GB	SUM(Number1; Number2; ...)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163671	432			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Number1; Number2; ...\</emph\> are 1 to 30 arguments whose sum is to be calculated.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163690	433			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163704	434			0	en-GB	If you enter the numbers \<item type=\"input\"\>2\</item\>, \<item type=\"input\"\>3\</item\> and \<item type=\"input\"\>4\</item\> in the Number 1, 2 and 3 text boxes, 9 will be returned as the result.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151740	556			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SUM(A1;A3;B5)\</item\> calculates the sum of the three cells. \<item type=\"input\"\>=SUM(A1:E10)\</item\> calculates the sum of all cells in the A1 to E10 cell range.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151756	619			0	en-GB	Conditions linked by AND can be used with the function SUM() in the following manner:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151774	620			0	en-GB	Example assumption: You have entered invoices into a table. Column A contains the date value of the invoice, column B the amounts. You want to find a formula that you can use to return the total of all amounts for only a specific month, e.g. only the amount for the period >=2008-01-01 to <2008-02-01. The range with the date values covers A1:A40, the range containing the amounts to be totalled is B1:B40. C1 contains the start date, \<item type=\"input\"\>2008-01-01\</item\>, of the invoices to be included and C2 the date, \<item type=\"input\"\>2008-02-01\</item\>, that is no longer included.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151799	621			0	en-GB	Enter the following formula as an array formula:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151813	622			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SUM((A1:A40>=C1)*(A1:A40<C2)*B1:B40)\</item\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151828	623			0	en-GB	In order to enter this as an array formula, you must press the Shift\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>+Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>+ Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+ Enter keys instead of simply pressing the Enter key to close the formula. The formula will then be shown in the \<emph\>Formula\</emph\> bar enclosed in braces { }.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151869	624			0	en-GB	{=SUM((A1:A40>=C1)*(A1:A40<C2)*B1:B40)}				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151884	625			0	en-GB	The formula is based on the fact that the result of a comparison is 1 if the criterion is met and 0 if it is not. The individual comparison results will be treated as an array and used in matrix multiplication and at the end the individual values will be totalled to give the result matrix.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151957				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>SUMIF function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adding;specified numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151957	436			0	en-GB	SUMIF				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151986	437			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SUMMEWENN\"\>Adds the cells specified by a given criteria.\</ahelp\> This function is used to browse a range when you search for a certain value.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152015	438			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152028	439			0	en-GB	SUMIF(Range; Criteria; SumRange)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152043	440			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Range\</emph\> is the range to which the criteria are to be applied.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152062	441			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Criteria\</emph\> is a reference to a cell containing the search criterion, or the search criterion itself. If the criterion is written into the formula, it must be enclosed with double quotes.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152083	442			0	en-GB	\<emph\>SumRange\</emph\> is the range from which values are summed. If this parameter has not been indicated, the values found in the Range are summed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id8347422				0	en-GB	SUMIF supports the reference concatenation operator (~) only in the Criteria parameter and only if the optional SumRange parameter is not given.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152110	443			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152148	626			0	en-GB	To sum only negative numbers: \<item type=\"input\"\>=SUMIF(A1:A10;"<0")\</item\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6670125				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SUMIF(A1:A10;">0";B1:10)\</item\> - sums values from the range B1:B10 only if the corresponding values in the range A1:A10 are >0.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6062196				0	en-GB	See COUNTIF() for some more syntax examples that can be used with SUMIF().				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152195				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>TAN function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
