helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143339	482			0	en-GB	PRODUCT				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143366	483			0	en-GB	7				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143389	484			0	en-GB	STDEV				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143416	485			0	en-GB	8				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143439	486			0	en-GB	STDEVP				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143466	487			0	en-GB	9				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143489	488			0	en-GB	SUM				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143516	489			0	en-GB	10				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143539	490			0	en-GB	VAR				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143566	491			0	en-GB	11				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143589	492			0	en-GB	VARP				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143606	498			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Range\</emph\> is the range of cells included.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143625	499			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143638	562			0	en-GB	You have a table in the cell range A1:B5 containing cities in column A and accompanying figures in column B. You have used an AutoFilter so that you only see rows containing the city Glasgow. You want to see the sum of the figures that are displayed; that is, just the subtotal for the filtered rows. In this case the correct formula would be:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143658	563			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SUBTOTAL(9;B2:B5)\</item\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143672				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>euro; converting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>EUROCONVERT function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143672	564			0	en-GB	EUROCONVERT				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143708	565			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_UMRECHNEN\"\>Converts between old European national currency and to and from euro.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143731	566			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143748	567			0	en-GB	EUROCONVERT(Value; "From_currency"; "To_currency", full_precision, triangulation_precision)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143763	568			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Value\</emph\> is the amount in the currency to be converted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143782	569			0	en-GB	\<emph\>From_currency\</emph\> and \<emph\>To_currency\</emph\> are the currency units to convert from and to respectively. These must be text, the official abbreviation for the currency (for example, "EUR"). The rates (shown per euro) were set by the European Commission.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200904301810				0	en-GB	\<emph\>Full_precision\</emph\> is optional. If omitted or False, the result is rounded according to the decimals of the To currency. If Full_precision is True, the result is not rounded.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200904301815				0	en-GB	\<emph\>Triangulation_precision\</emph\> is optional. If Triangulation_precision is given and >=3, the intermediate result of a triangular conversion (currency1,EUR,currency2) is rounded to that precision. If Triangulation_precision is omitted, the intermediate result is not rounded. Also if To currency is "EUR", Triangulation_precision is used as if triangulation was needed and conversion from EUR to EUR was applied.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143819	570			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Examples\</emph\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143837	571			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=EUROCONVERT(100;"ATS";"EUR")\</item\> converts 100 Austrian Schillings into euro.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143853	572			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=EUROCONVERT(100;"EUR";"DEM")\</item\> converts 100 euro into German Marks.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id0908200902090676				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>CONVERT function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id0908200902074836				0	en-GB	CONVERT				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200902131122				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Converts a value from one unit of measurement to another unit of measurement. The conversion factors are given in a list in the configuration.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200902475420				0	en-GB	At one time the list of conversion factors included the legacy European currencies and the euro (see examples below). We suggest using the new function EUROCONVERT for converting these currencies.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id0908200902131071				0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200902131191				0	en-GB	CONVERT(value;"text";"text")				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id0908200902131152				0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id090820090213112				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CONVERT(100;"ATS";"EUR")\</item\> returns the euro value of 100 Austrian Schillings.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200902475431				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CONVERT(100;"EUR";"DEM")\</item\> converts 100 euro into German Marks. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3157177				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>ODD function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rounding;up/down to nearest odd integer\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157177	502			0	en-GB	ODD				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157205	503			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_UNGERADE\"\>Rounds a positive number up to the nearest odd integer and a negative number down to the nearest odd integer.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157223	504			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157237	505			0	en-GB	ODD(Number)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157250	506			0	en-GB	Returns \<emph\>Number\</emph\> rounded to the next odd integer up, away from zero.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157270	507			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157283	508			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ODD(1.2)\</item\> returns 3.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id8746910				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ODD(1)\</item\> returns 1.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9636524				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ODD(0)\</item\> returns 1.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5675527				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ODD(-3.1)\</item\> returns -5.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3157404				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>FLOOR function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rounding;down to nearest multiple of significance\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157404	512			0	en-GB	FLOOR				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157432	513			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_UNTERGRENZE\"\>Rounds a number down to the nearest multiple of Significance.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157451	514			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157464	515			0	en-GB	FLOOR(Number; Significance; Mode)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157478	516			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the number that is to be rounded down.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157497	517			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Significance\</emph\> is the value that the number is to be rounded down to a multiple of.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157517	561			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Mode\</emph\> is an optional value. If the Mode parameter is supplied and is not equal to zero, and if Number and Significance are negative, rounding up is carried out based on the absolute value of Number. This parameter is omitted when exporting to Microsoft Excel as Excel does not support a third parameter for this function.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163894	630			0	en-GB	If both parameters \<emph\>Number\</emph\> and \<emph\>Significance\</emph\> are negative, and if the \<emph\>Mode\</emph\> value is equal to zero or is not specified, then the results in $[officename] Calc and Microsoft Excel will differ after exporting. If you export the spreadsheet to Microsoft Excel, use Mode = 1 to see the same results in Microsoft Excel as in Calc.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163932	518			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163945	519			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=FLOOR( -11;-2)\</item\> returns -12				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163966	520			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=FLOOR( -11;-2;0)\</item\> returns -12				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163988	521			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=FLOOR( -11;-2;1)\</item\> returns -10				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164086				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>SIGN function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>algebraic signs\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164086	523			0	en-GB	SIGN				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164115	524			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_VORZEICHEN\"\>Returns the sign of a number. Returns +1 if the number is positive, -1 if negative and 0 if zero.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164136	525			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164150	526			0	en-GB	SIGN(Number)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164164	527			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the number of which the sign is to be determined.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164183	528			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164197	529			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SIGN(3.4)\</item\> returns 1.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164212	530			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SIGN(-4.5)\</item\> returns -1.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164252				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>MROUND function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>nearest multiple\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164252	658			0	en-GB	MROUND				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164288	659			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_MROUND\"\>Returns a number rounded to the nearest multiple of another number.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164306	660			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164320	661			0	en-GB	MROUND(Number; Multiple)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3486434				0	en-GB	Returns \<emph\>Number\</emph\> rounded to the nearest multiple of \<emph\>Multiple\</emph\>. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3068636				0	en-GB	An alternative implementation would be \<item type=\"literal\"\>Multiple * ROUND(Number/Multiple)\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164333	662			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164347	663			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MROUND(15.5;3)\</item\> returns 15, as 15.5 is closer to 15 (= 3*5) than to 18 (= 3*6).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_idN14DD6				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MROUND(1.4;0.5)\</item\> returns 1.5 (= 0.5*3).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164375				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>SQRT function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>square roots;positive numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164375	532			0	en-GB	SQRT				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164404	533			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_WURZEL\"\>Returns the positive square root of a number.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164424	534			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164437	535			0	en-GB	SQRT(Number)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164451	536			0	en-GB	Returns the positive square root of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6870021				0	en-GB	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> must be positive.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164471	537			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164484	538			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SQRT(16)\</item\> returns 4.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3591723				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SQRT(-16)\</item\> returns an \<item type=\"literal\"\>invalid argument\</item\> error.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164560				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>SQRTPI function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>square roots;products of Pi\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164560	665			0	en-GB	SQRTPI				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164596	666			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_SQRTPI\"\>Returns the square root of (PI times a number).\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164614	667			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164627	668			0	en-GB	SQRTPI(Number)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1501510				0	en-GB	Returns the positive square root of (PI multiplied by \<emph\>Number\</emph\>).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9929197				0	en-GB	This is equivalent to \<item type=\"literal\"\>SQRT(PI()*Number)\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164641	669			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164654	670			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SQRTPI(2)\</item\> returns the square root of (2PI), approximately 2.506628.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164669				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>random numbers; between limits\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>RANDBETWEEN function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164669	671			0	en-GB	RANDBETWEEN				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164711	672			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_RANDBETWEEN\"\>Returns an integer random number in a specified range.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164745	673			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164758	674			0	en-GB	RANDBETWEEN(Bottom; Top)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7112338				0	en-GB	Returns an integer random number between integers \<emph\>Bottom\</emph\> and \<emph\>Top\</emph\> (both inclusive).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2855616				0	en-GB	This function produces a new random number each time that Calc recalculates. To force Calc to recalculate manually press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F9.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2091433				0	en-GB	To generate random numbers which never recalculate, copy cells containing this function and use \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Paste Special\</item\> (with \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Paste All\</item\> and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formulae\</item\> not marked and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbers\</item\> marked).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164772	675			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164785	676			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=RANDBETWEEN(20;30)\</item\> returns an integer in the range 20 to 30.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164800				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>RAND function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>random numbers;between 0.0 and 1.0\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164800	542			0	en-GB	RAND				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164829	543			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZUFALLSZAHL\"\>Returns a random number in the range 0.0 to 1.0.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164870	545			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164884	546			0	en-GB	RAND()				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5092318				0	en-GB	This function produces a new random number each time that Calc recalculates. To force Calc to recalculate manually press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F9.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9312417				0	en-GB	To generate random numbers which never recalculate, copy cells each containing =RAND() and use \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Paste Special\</item\> (with \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Paste All\</item\> and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formulae\</item\> not marked and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbers\</item\> marked).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id9089022				0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9569078				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=RAND()\</item\> returns a random number in the range 0.0 to 1.0.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164897				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>COUNTIF function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>counting;specified cells\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164897	547			0	en-GB	COUNTIF				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164926	548			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZAEHLENWENN\"\>Returns the number of cells that meet with certain criteria within a cell range.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164953	549			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164967	550			0	en-GB	COUNTIF(Range; Criteria)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164980	551			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Range\</emph\> is the range to which the criteria are to be applied.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165000	552			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Criteria\</emph\> indicates the criteria in the form of a number, an expression or a text string. These criteria determine which cells are counted. You may also enter search text in the form of a regular expression, e.g. "b.*" for all words that begin with b. You may also indicate a cell range that contains the search criterion. If you search for literal text, enclose the text in double quotes.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3165037	553			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3166505	627			0	en-GB	A1:A10 is a cell range containing the numbers \<item type=\"input\"\>2000\</item\> to \<item type=\"input\"\>2009\</item\>. Cell B1 contains the number \<item type=\"input\"\>2006\</item\>. In cell B2, you enter a formula:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3581652				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTIF(A1:A10;2006)\</item\> - this returns 1				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id708639				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTIF(A1:A10;B1)\</item\> - this returns 1				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5169225				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTIF(A1:A10;">=2006")\</item\> - this returns 4				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2118594				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTIF(A1:A10;"<"&B1)\</item\> - when B1 contains \<item type=\"input\"\>2006\</item\>, this returns 6				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id166020				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTIF(A1:A10;C2)\</item\> where cell C2 contains the text \<item type=\"input\"\>>2006\</item\> counts the number of cells in the range A1:A10 which are > 2006 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6386913				0	en-GB	To count only negative numbers: \<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTIF(A1:A10;"<0")\</item\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Array Functions				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147273				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>matrices; functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Function Wizard; arrays\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>array formulae\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inline array constants\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulae;arrays\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>functions;array functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; array formulae\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; array formulae\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adjusting array ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating;conditional calculations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>matrices; calculations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>conditional calculations with arrays\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>implicit array handling\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>forced array handling\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147273	1			0	en-GB	Array Functions				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3154744	2			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"matrixtext\"\>This category contains the array functions. \</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146084	257			0	en-GB	What is an Array?				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3154298	258			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"wasmatrix\"\>An array is a linked range of cells on a spreadsheet containing values. \</variable\> A square range of 3 rows and 3 columns is a 3 x 3 array:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3154692	260			0	en-GB	A				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3150117	261			0	en-GB	B				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3155325	262			0	en-GB	C				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3153104	263			0	en-GB	1				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3146996	264			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>7\</item\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3150529	265			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>31\</item\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3148831	266			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>33\</item\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3148943	267			0	en-GB	2				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3149771	268			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>95\</item\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3158407	269			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>17\</item\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3148806	270			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>2\</item\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3154904	271			0	en-GB	3				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3150779	272			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>5\</item\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3148449	273			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>10\</item\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3147238	274			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>50\</item\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3153583	277			0	en-GB	The smallest possible array is a 1 x 2 or 2 x 1 array with two adjacent cells.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148474	275			0	en-GB	What is an array formula?				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3155355	276			0	en-GB	A formula in which the individual values in a cell range are evaluated is referred to as an array formula. The difference between an array formula and other formulae is that the array formula deals with several values simultaneously instead of just one.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3151052	278			0	en-GB	Not only can an array formula process several values, but it can also return several values. The results of an array formula is also an array.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3158432	279			0	en-GB	To multiply the values in the individual cells by 10 in the above array, you do not need to apply a formula to each individual cell or value. Instead you just need to use a single array formula. Select a range of 3 x 3 cells on another part of the spreadsheet, enter the formula \<item type=\"input\"\>=10*A1:C3\</item\> and confirm this entry using the key combination \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+Enter. The result is a 3 x 3 array in which the individual values in the cell range (A1:C3) are multiplied by a factor of 10.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3149156	280			0	en-GB	In addition to multiplication, you can also use other operators on the reference range (an array). With $[officename] Calc, you can add (+), subtract (-), multiply (*), divide (/), use exponents (^), concatenation (&) and comparisons (=, <>, <, >, <=, >=). The operators can be used on each individual value in the cell range and return the result as an array if the array formula was entered.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3166456	326			0	en-GB	Comparison operators in an array formula treat empty cells in the same way as in a normal formula, that is, either as zero or as an empty string. For example, if cells A1 and A2 are empty the array formulae \<item type=\"input\"\>{=A1:A2=""}\</item\> and \<item type=\"input\"\>{=A1:A2=0}\</item\> will both return a 1 column 2 row array of cells containing TRUE.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150713	281			0	en-GB	When do you use array formulae?				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3149787	282			0	en-GB	Use array formulae if you have to repeat calculations using different values. If you decide to change the calculation method later, you only have to update the array formula. To add an array formula, select the entire array range and then \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060107.xhp\" name=\"make the required change to the array formula\"\>make the required change to the array formula\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3149798	283			0	en-GB	Array formulae are also a space saving option when several values must be calculated, since they are not very memory-intensive. In addition, arrays are an essential tool for carrying out complex calculations, because you can have several cell ranges included in your calculations. $[officename] has different maths functions for arrays, such as the MMULT function for multiplying two arrays or the SUMPRODUCT function for calculating the scalar products of two arrays.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155588	284			0	en-GB	Using Array Formulae in $[officename] Calc				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3152876	285			0	en-GB	You can also create a "normal" formula in which the reference range, such as parameters, indicate an array formula. The result is obtained from the intersection of the reference range and the rows or columns in which the formula is found. If there is no intersection or if the range at the intersection covers several rows or columns, a #VALUE! error message will appear. The following example illustrates this concept:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151271	313			0	en-GB	Creating Array Formulae				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3149102	314			0	en-GB	If you create an array formula using the \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\>, you must mark the \<emph\>Array\</emph\> check box each time so that the results are returned in an array. Otherwise, only the value in the upper-left cell of the array being calculated is returned.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3153392	4			0	en-GB	If you enter the array formula directly into the cell, you must use the key combination Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter instead of the Enter key. Only then does the formula become an array formula.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3151120	315			0	en-GB	Array formulae are displayed in braces { } in $[officename] Calc. You cannot create array formulae by manually entering the braces.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3154342	5			0	en-GB	The cells in a results array are automatically protected against changes. However, you can edit or copy the array formula by selecting the entire array cell range.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id8834803				0	en-GB	Using Inline Array Constants in Formulae				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id985747				0	en-GB	Calc supports inline matrix/array constants in formulae. An inline array is enclosed with braces '{' and '}'. Elements can be each a number (including negatives), a logical constant (TRUE, FALSE), or a literal string. Non-constant expressions are not allowed. Arrays can be entered with one or more rows, and one or more columns. All rows must consist of the same number of elements, all columns must consist of the same number of elements. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id936613				0	en-GB	The column separator (separating elements in one row) is the ';' semicolon. The row separator is a '|' pipe symbol. The separators are not language and locale dependent. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id1877498				0	en-GB	Arrays can not be nested.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id4262520				0	en-GB	\<emph\>Examples:\</emph\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id9387493				0	en-GB	={1;2;3}				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id8207037				0	en-GB	An array with one row consisting of the three numbers 1, 2, and 3.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id6757103				0	en-GB	To enter this array constant, you select three cells in a row, then you type the formula \<item type=\"input\"\>={1;2;3}\</item\> using braces { } and semicolons, then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+Enter.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id8868068				0	en-GB	={1;2;3|4;5;6}				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id6626483				0	en-GB	An array with two rows and three values in each row.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id5262916				0	en-GB	={0;1;2|FALSE;TRUE;"two"}				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id1623889				0	en-GB	A mixed data array.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id7781914				0	en-GB	=SIN({1;2;3})				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id300912				0	en-GB	Entered as a matrix formula, delivers the result of three SIN calculations with the arguments 1, 2, and 3.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148660	316			0	en-GB	Editing Array Formulae				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3149241	317			0	en-GB	Select the cell range or array containing the array formula. To select the whole array, position the cell cursor inside the array range, then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+ /, where / is the Division key on the numeric keypad.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3143274	318			0	en-GB	Either press F2 or position the cursor in the input line. Both of these actions let you edit the formula.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3154798	319			0	en-GB	After you have made changes, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+Enter.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3150628	334			0	en-GB	You can format the separate parts of an array. For example, you can change the font colour. Select a cell range and then change the attribute you want.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145608	320			0	en-GB	Copying Array Formulae				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3149585	321			0	en-GB	Select the cell range or array containing the array formula.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3154619	322			0	en-GB	Either press F2 or position the cursor in the input line.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3150994	323			0	en-GB	Copy the formula into the input line by pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3146787	324			0	en-GB	Select a range of cells into which you want to insert the array formula and either press F2 or position the cursor in the input line.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3154419	325			0	en-GB	Paste the formula by pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V in the selected space and confirm it by pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+Enter. The selected range now contains the array formula.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154834	328			0	en-GB	Adjusting an Array Range				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3148679	329			0	en-GB	If you want to edit the output array, do the following:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3151102	330			0	en-GB	Select the cell range or array containing the array formula.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3147096	331			0	en-GB	Below the selection, to the right, you will see a small icon with which you can zoom in or out on the range using your mouse.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3150974	332			0	en-GB	When you adjust the array range, the array formula will not automatically be adjusted. You are only changing the range in which the result will appear.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3146080	333			0	en-GB	By holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key, you can create a copy of the array formula in the given range.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN10D47				0	en-GB	Conditional Array Calculations				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN10D4B				0	en-GB	A conditional array calculation is an array or matrix formula that includes an IF() or CHOOSE() function. The condition argument in the formula is an area reference or a matrix result.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN10D4E				0	en-GB	In the following example, the >0 test of the {=IF(A1:A3>0;"yes";"no")} formula is applied to each cell in the range A1:A3 and the result is copied to the corresponding cell.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN10D65				0	en-GB	A				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN10D6B				0	en-GB	B (formula)				20130618 17:22:18
