helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148522				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Function Wizard; spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>functions; spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148522	1			0	en-GB	Spreadsheet Functions				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3144508	2			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"tabelletext\"\>This section contains descriptions of the \<emph\>Spreadsheet\</emph\> functions together with an example.\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146968				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>ADDRESS function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146968	3			0	en-GB	ADDRESS				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3155762	4			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ADRESSE\"\>Returns a cell address (reference) as a text string, according to the specified row and column numbers.\</ahelp\> You can determine whether the address is interpreted as an absolute address (for example, $A$1) or as a relative address (as A1) or in a mixed form (A$1 or $A1). You can also specify the name of the sheet.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id1027200802301348				0	en-GB	For interoperability the ADDRESS and INDIRECT functions support an optional parameter to specify whether the R1C1 address notation instead of the usual A1 notation should be used.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id1027200802301445				0	en-GB	In ADDRESS, the parameter is inserted as the fourth parameter, shifting the optional sheet name parameter to the fifth position.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id102720080230153				0	en-GB	In INDIRECT, the parameter is appended as the second parameter.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id102720080230151				0	en-GB	In both functions, if the argument is inserted with the value 0, then the R1C1 notation is used. If the argument is not given or has a value other than 0, then the A1 notation is used. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id1027200802301556				0	en-GB	In case of R1C1 notation, ADDRESS returns address strings using the exclamation mark '!' as the sheet name separator, and INDIRECT expects the exclamation mark as sheet name separator. Both functions still use the dot '.' sheet name separator with A1 notation.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id1027200802301521				0	en-GB	When opening documents from ODF 1.0/1.1 format, the ADDRESS functions that show a sheet name as the fourth paramater will shift that sheet name to become the fifth parameter. A new fourth parameter with the value 1 will be inserted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id1027200802301650				0	en-GB	When storing a document in ODF 1.0/1.1 format, if ADDRESS functions have a fourth parameter, that parameter will be removed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id102720080230162				0	en-GB	Do not save a spreadsheet in the old ODF 1.0/1.1 format if the ADDRESS function's new fourth parameter was used with a value of 0.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id1027200802301756				0	en-GB	The INDIRECT function is saved without conversion to ODF 1.0/1.1 format. If the second parameter was present, an older version of Calc will return an error for that function.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151196	5			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154707	6			0	en-GB	ADDRESS(Row; Column; Abs; A1; "Sheet")				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3147505	7			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Row\</emph\> is the row number for the cell reference				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3145323	8			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Column\</emph\> is the column number for the cell reference (the number, not the letter)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153074	9			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Abs\</emph\> determines the type of reference:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153298	10			0	en-GB	1: absolute ($A$1)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150431	11			0	en-GB	2: row reference type is absolute; column reference is relative (A$1)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3146096	12			0	en-GB	3: row (relative); column (absolute) ($A1)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153334	13			0	en-GB	4: relative (A1)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id1027200802465915				0	en-GB	\<emph\>A1\</emph\> (optional) - if set to 0, the R1C1 notation is used. If this parameter is absent or set to another value than 0, the A1 notation is used.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153962	14			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Sheet\</emph\> is the name of the sheet. It must be placed in double quotes.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147299	15			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3148744	16			0	en-GB	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=ADDRESS(1;1;2;;"Sheet2")\</item\> returns the following: Sheet2.A$1				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3159260	17			0	en-GB	If the cell A1 in sheet 2 contains the value \<item type=\"input\"\>-6\</item\>, you can refer indirectly to the referenced cell using a function in B2 by entering \<item type=\"input\"\>=ABS(INDIRECT(B2))\</item\>. The result is the absolute value of the cell reference specified in B2, which in this case is 6.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150372				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>AREAS function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150372	19			0	en-GB	AREAS				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150036	20			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_BEREICHE\"\>Returns the number of individual ranges that belong to a multiple range.\</ahelp\> A range can consist of contiguous cells or a single cell.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id061020090307073				0	en-GB	The function expects a single argument. If you state multiple ranges, you must enclose them within additional parentheses (round brackets). Multiple ranges can be entered using the semicolon (;) as divider, but this gets automatically converted to the tilde (~) operator. The tilde is used to join ranges.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145222	21			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3155907	22			0	en-GB	AREAS(Reference)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153118	23			0	en-GB	Reference is the reference to a cell or cell range.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148891	24			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149946	25			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=AREAS((A1:B3;F2;G1))\</item\> returns 3, as it is a reference to three cells and/or areas. After entry this gets converted to =AREAS((A1:B3~F2~G1)).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3146820	26			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=AREAS(All)\</item\> returns 1 if you have defined an area named All under \<emph\>Data - Define Range\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148727				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>DDE function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148727	28			0	en-GB	DDE				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149434	29			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DDE\"\>Returns the result of a DDE-based link.\</ahelp\> If the contents of the linked range or section changes, the returned value will also change. You must reload the spreadsheet or choose \<emph\>Edit - Links\</emph\> to see the updated links. Cross-platform links, for example from a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> installation running on a Windows machine to a document created on a Linux machine, are not allowed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150700	30			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3148886	31			0	en-GB	DDE("Server"; "File"; "Range"; Mode)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154842	32			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Server\</emph\> is the name of a server application. \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>applications have the server name "Soffice".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153034	33			0	en-GB	\<emph\>File\</emph\> is the complete file name, including path specification.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3147472	34			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Range\</emph\> is the area containing the data to be evaluated.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3152773	184			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Mode\</emph\> is an optional parameter that controls the method by which the DDE server converts its data into numbers.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154383	185			0	en-GB	                     \<emph\>Mode\</emph\>                  				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3145146	186			0	en-GB	                     \<emph\>Effect\</emph\>                  				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154558	187			0	en-GB	0 or missing				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3145596	188			0	en-GB	Number format from the "Default" cell style				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3152785	189			0	en-GB	1				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154380	190			0	en-GB	Data are always interpreted in the standard format for US English				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150279	191			0	en-GB	2				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153775	192			0	en-GB	Data are retrieved as text strings; no conversion to numbers				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149546	35			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3148734	36			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DDE("soffice";"c:\\office\\document\\data1.sxc";"sheet1.A1")\</item\> reads the contents of cell A1 in sheet1 of the \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc spreadsheet data1.sxc.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153081	37			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DDE("soffice";"c:\\office\\document\\motto.sxw";"Today's motto")\</item\> returns a motto in the cell containing this formula. First, you must enter a line in the motto.sxw document containing the motto text and define it as the first line of a section named \<item type=\"literal\"\>Today's Motto\</item\> (in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer under \<emph\>Insert - Section\</emph\>). If the motto is modified (and saved) in the \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer document, the motto is updated in all \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc cells in which this DDE link is defined.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153114				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>ERRORTYPE function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153114	38			0	en-GB	ERRORTYPE				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3148568	39			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_FEHLERTYP\"\>Returns the number corresponding to an \<link href=\"text/scalc/05/02140000.xhp\" name=\"error value\"\>error value\</link\> occurring in a different cell.\</ahelp\> With the aid of this number, you can generate an error message text.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149877	40			0	en-GB	The Status Bar displays the predefined error code from \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> if you click the cell containing the error.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154327	41			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3151322	42			0	en-GB	ERRORTYPE(Reference)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150132	43			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Reference\</emph\> contains the address of the cell in which the error occurs.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145248	44			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3146904	45			0	en-GB	If cell A1 displays Err:518, the function \<item type=\"input\"\>=ERRORTYPE(A1)\</item\> returns the number 518.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151221				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>INDEX function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151221	47			0	en-GB	INDEX				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150268	48			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_INDEX\"\>INDEX returns a subrange, specified by row and column number or an optional range name. Depending on context, INDEX returns a reference or content.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156063	49			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149007	50			0	en-GB	INDEX(Reference; Row; Column; Range)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153260	51			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Reference\</emph\> is a reference, entered either directly or by specifying a range name. If the reference consists of multiple ranges, you must enclose the reference or range name in parentheses (round brackets).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3145302	52			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Row\</emph\> (optional) is the row index of the reference range for which to return a value. In the case of zero (no specific row) all referenced rows are returned.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154628	53			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Column\</emph\> (optional) is the column index of the reference range for which to return a value. In the case of zero (no specific column) all referenced columns are returned.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3155514	54			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Range\</emph\> (optional) is the index of the subrange if referring to a multiple range.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145264	55			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3159112	56			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=INDEX(Prices;4;1)\</item\> returns the value from row 4 and column 1 of the database range defined in \<emph\>Data - Define\</emph\> as \<emph\>Prices\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150691	57			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=INDEX(SumX;4;1)\</item\> returns the value from the range \<emph\>SumX\</emph\> in row 4 and column 1 as defined in \<emph\>Insert - Names - Define\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id4109012				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=INDEX(A1:B6;1)\</item\> returns a reference to the first row of A1:B6.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id9272133				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=INDEX(A1:B6;0;1 )\</item\> returns a reference to the first column of A1:B6.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3158419	58			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=INDEX((multi);4;1)\</item\> indicates the value contained in row 4 and column 1 of the (multiple) range, which you named under \<emph\>Insert - Names - Set\</emph\> as \<emph\>multi\</emph\>. The multiple range may consist of several rectangular ranges, each with a row 4 and column 1. If you now want to call the second block of this multiple range enter the number \<item type=\"input\"\>2\</item\> as the \<emph\>range\</emph\> parameter.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3148595	59			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=INDEX(A1:B6;  1;1)\</item\> indicates the value in the upper-left of the A1:B6 range.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id9960020				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=INDEX((multi);0;0;2)\</item\> returns a reference to the second range of the multiple range.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153181				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>INDIRECT function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153181	62			0	en-GB	INDIRECT				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3147169	63			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_INDIREKT\"\>Returns the \<emph\>reference\</emph\> specified by a text string.\</ahelp\> This function can also be used to return the area of a corresponding string.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153717	64			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149824	65			0	en-GB	INDIRECT(Reference; A1)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154317	66			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Reference\</emph\> is a reference to a cell or an area (in text form) for which to return the contents.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id1027200802470312				0	en-GB	\<emph\>A1\</emph\> (optional) - if set to 0, the R1C1 notation is used. If this parameter is absent or set to another value than 0, the A1 notation is used.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CAE				0	en-GB	If you open a Microsoft Excel spreadsheet that uses indirect addresses calculated from string functions, the sheet addresses will not be translated automatically. For example, the Microsoft Excel address in INDIRECT("filename!sheetname"&B1) is not converted into the Calc address in INDIRECT("filename.sheetname"&B1).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150389	67			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150608	68			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=INDIRECT(A1)\</item\> equals 100 if A1 contains C108 as a reference and cell C108 contains a value of \<item type=\"input\"\>100\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3083286	181			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SUM(INDIRECT("a1:" & ADDRESS(1;3)))\</item\> totals the cells in the area of A1 up to the cell whose address is defined by row 1 and column 3. Thhis means that area A1:C1 is totalled.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154818				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>COLUMN function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154818	70			0	en-GB	COLUMN				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149711	193			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SPALTE\"\>Returns the column number of a cell reference.\</ahelp\> If the reference is a cell the column number of the cell is returned; if the parameter is a cell area, the corresponding column numbers are returned in a single-row \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060107.xhp#wasmatrix\" name=\"array\"\>array\</link\> if the formula is entered \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060107.xhp#somatrixformel\" name=\"as an array formula\"\>as an array formula\</link\>. If the COLUMN function with an area reference parameter is not used for an array formula, only the column number of the first cell within the area is determined.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149283	72			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149447	73			0	en-GB	COLUMN(Reference)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3156310	74			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Reference\</emph\> is the reference to a cell or cell area whose first column number is to be found.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3155837	194			0	en-GB	If no reference is entered, the column number of the cell in which the formula is entered is found. \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc automatically sets the reference to the current cell.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152932	75			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571	76			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COLUMN(A1)\</item\> equals 1. Column A is the first column in the table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3147079	77			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COLUMN(C3:E3)\</item\> equals 3. Column C is the third column in the table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3146861	195			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COLUMN(D3:G10)\</item\> returns 4 because column D is the fourth column in the table and the COLUMN function is not used as an array formula. (In this case, the first value of the array is always used as the result.)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3156320	196			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>{=COLUMN(B2:B7)}\</item\> and \<item type=\"input\"\>=COLUMN(B2:B7)\</item\> both return 2 because the reference only contains column B as the second column in the table. Because single-column areas have only one column number, it does not make a difference whether or not the formula is used as an array formula.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150872	197			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COLUMN()\</item\> returns 3 if the formula was entered in column C.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153277	198			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>{=COLUMN(Rabbit)}\</item\> returns the single-row array (3, 4) if "Rabbit" is the named area (C1:D3).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154643				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>COLUMNS function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154643	79			0	en-GB	COLUMNS				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3151182	80			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SPALTEN\"\>Returns the number of columns in the given reference.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149141	81			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154047	82			0	en-GB	COLUMNS(Array)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154745	83			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Array\</emph\> is the reference to a cell range whose total number of columns is to be found. The argument can also be a single cell.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153622	84			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149577	200			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COLUMNS(B5)\</item\> returns 1 because a cell only contains one column.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3145649	85			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COLUMNS(A1:C5)\</item\> equals 3. The reference comprises three columns.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3155846	201			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COLUMNS(Rabbit)\</item\> returns 2 if \<item type=\"literal\"\>Rabbit\</item\> is the named range (C1:D3).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153152				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>vertical search function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>VLOOKUP function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153152	87			0	en-GB	VLOOKUP				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149984	88			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SVERWEIS\"\>Vertical search with reference to adjacent cells to the right.\</ahelp\> This function checks if a specific value is contained in the first column of an array. The function then returns the value in the same row of the column named by \<item type=\"literal\"\>Index\</item\>. If the \<item type=\"literal\"\>SortOrder\</item\> parameter is omitted or set to TRUE or one, it is assumed that the data is sorted in ascending order. In this case, if the exact \<item type=\"literal\"\>SearchCriterion\</item\> is not found, the last value that is smaller than the criterion will be returned. If \<item type=\"literal\"\>SortOrder\</item\> is set to FALSE or zero, an exact match must be found, otherwise the error \<emph\>Error: Value Not Available\</emph\> will be the result. Thus with a value of zero the data does not need to be sorted in ascending order.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146898	89			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150156	90			0	en-GB	=VLOOKUP(SearchCriterion; Array; Index; SortOrder)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149289	91			0	en-GB	\<emph\>SearchCriterion\</emph\> is the value searched for in the first column of the array.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153884	92			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Array\</emph\> is the reference, which is to comprise at least two columns.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3156005	93			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Index\</emph\> is the number of the column in the array that contains the value to be returned. The first column has the number 1.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3151208	94			0	en-GB	\<emph\>SortOrder\</emph\> is an optional parameter that indicates whether the first column in the array is sorted in ascending order. Enter the Boolean value FALSE or zero if the first column is not sorted in ascending order. Sorted columns can be searched much faster and the function always returns a value, even if the search value was not matched exactly, if it is between the lowest and highest value of the sorted list. In unsorted lists, the search value must be matched exactly. Otherwise the function will return this message: \<emph\>Error: Value Not Available\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147487	95			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154129	96			0	en-GB	You want to enter the number of a dish on the menu in cell A1, and the name of the dish is to appear as text in the neighbouring cell (B1) immediately. The Number to Name assignment is contained in the D1:E100 array. D1 contains \<item type=\"input\"\>100\</item\>, E1 contains the name \<item type=\"input\"\>Vegetable Soup\</item\>, and so forth, for 100 menu items. The numbers in column D are sorted in ascending order; thus, the optional \<item type=\"literal\"\>SortOrder\</item\> parameter is not necessary.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3145663	97			0	en-GB	Enter the following formula in B1:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3151172	98			0	en-GB	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=VLOOKUP(A1;D1:E100;2)\</item\>         				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149200	99			0	en-GB	As soon as you enter a number in A1 B1 will show the corresponding text contained in the second column of reference D1:E100. Entering a non-existent number displays the text with the next number down. To prevent this, enter FALSE as the last parameter in the formula so that an error message is generated when a non-existent number is entered.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153905				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>sheet numbers; looking up\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>SHEET function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153905	215			0	en-GB	SHEET				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150309	216			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_TABELLE\"\>Returns the sheet number of a reference or a string representing a sheet name.\</ahelp\> If you do not enter any parameters, the result is the sheet number of the spreadsheet containing the formula.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148564	217			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153095	218			0	en-GB	SHEET(Reference)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154588	219			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Reference\</emph\> is optional and is the reference to a cell, an area, or a sheet name string.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155399	220			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3146988	221			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SHEET(Sheet2.A1)\</item\> returns 2 if Sheet2 is the second sheet in the spreadsheet document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148829				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>number of sheets; function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>SHEETS function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148829	222			0	en-GB	SHEETS				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3148820	223			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_TABELLEN\"\>Determines the number of sheets in a reference.\</ahelp\> If you do not enter any parameters, it returns the number of sheets in the current document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154220	224			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150777	225			0	en-GB	SHEETS(Reference)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153060	226			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Reference\</emph\> is the reference to a sheet or an area. This parameter is optional.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149766	227			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150507	228			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SHEETS(Sheet1.A1:Sheet3.G12)\</item\> returns 3 if Sheet1, Sheet2, and Sheet3 exist in the sequence indicated.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3158407				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>MATCH function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158407	101			0	en-GB	MATCH				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154896	102			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_VERGLEICH\"\>Returns the relative position of an item in an array that matches a specified value.\</ahelp\> The function returns the position of the value found in the lookup_array as a number.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153834	103			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3159152	104			0	en-GB	MATCH(SearchCriterion; LookupArray; Type)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149336	105			0	en-GB	\<emph\>SearchCriterion\</emph\> is the value which is to be searched for in the single-row or single-column array.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3159167	106			0	en-GB	\<emph\>LookupArray\</emph\> is the reference searched. A lookup array can be a single row or column, or part of a single row or column.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3147239	107			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> may take the values 1, 0, or -1. If Type = 1 or if this optional parameter is omitted, it is assumed that the first column of the search array is sorted in ascending order. If Type = -1 it is assumed that the column is sorted in descending order. This corresponds to the same function in Microsoft Excel.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154265	231			0	en-GB	If Type = 0, only exact matches are found. If the search criterion is found more than once, the function returns the index of the first matching value. Only if Type = 0 can you search for regular expressions.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3147528	232			0	en-GB	If Type = 1 or the third parameter is omitted, the index of the last value that is smaller than or equal to the search criterion is returned. This applies even when the search array is not sorted. For Type = -1, the index of the first value that is larger than or equal is returned.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155119	108			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3155343	109			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MATCH(200;D1:D100)\</item\> searches the area D1:D100, which is sorted by column D, for the value 200. As soon as this value is reached, the number of the row in which it was found is returned. If a higher value is found during the search in the column, the number of the previous row is returned.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3158430				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>OFFSET function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158430	111			0	en-GB	OFFSET				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149167	112			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_VERSCHIEBUNG\"\>Returns the value of a cell offset by a certain number of rows and columns from a given reference point.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146952	113			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3159194	114			0	en-GB	OFFSET(Reference; Rows; Columns; Height; Width)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3152360	115			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Reference\</emph\> is the cell from which the function searches for the new reference.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3156032	116			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Rows\</emph\> is the number of rows by which the reference was corrected up (negative value) or down.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3166458	117			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Columns\</emph\> (optional) is the number of columns by which the reference was corrected to the left (negative value) or to the right.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150708	118			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Height\</emph\> (optional) is the vertical height for an area that starts at the new reference position.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3147278	119			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Width\</emph\> (optional) is the horizontal width for an area that starts at the new reference position.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id8662373				0	en-GB	Arguments \<emph\>Rows\</emph\> and \<emph\>Columns\</emph\> must not lead to zero or negative start row or column.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id9051484				0	en-GB	Arguments \<emph\>Height\</emph\> and \<emph\>Width\</emph\> must not lead to zero or negative count of rows or columns.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_idN1104B				0	en-GB	            \<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>         				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155586	120			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149744	121			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=OFFSET(A1;2;2)\</item\> returns the value in cell C3 (A1 moved by two rows and two columns down). If C3 contains the value \<item type=\"input\"\>100\</item\> this function returns the value 100.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id7439802				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=OFFSET(B2:C3;1;1)\</item\> returns a reference to B2:C3 moved down by 1 row and one column to the right (C3:D4).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3009430				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=OFFSET(B2:C3;-1;-1)\</item\> returns a reference to B2:C3 moved up by 1 row and one column to the left (A1:B2).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id2629169				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=OFFSET(B2:C3;0;0;3;4)\</item\> returns a reference to B2:C3 resized to 3 rows and 4 columns (B2:E4).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id6668599				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=OFFSET(B2:C3;1;0;3;4)\</item\> returns a reference to B2:C3 moved down by one row resized to 3 rows and 4 columns (B2:E4).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153739	122			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SUM(OFFSET(A1;2;2;5;6))\</item\> determines the total of the area that starts in cell C3 and has a height of 5 rows and a width of 6 columns (area=C3:H7).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159273				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>LOOKUP function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159273	123			0	en-GB	LOOKUP				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153389	124			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_VERWEIS\"\>Returns the content of a cell either from a one-row or one-column range or from an array.\</ahelp\> Optionally, the assigned value (of the same index) is returned in a different column and row. As opposed to \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060109.xhp\" name=\"VLOOKUP\"\>VLOOKUP\</link\> and \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060109.xhp\" name=\"HLOOKUP\"\>HLOOKUP\</link\>, search and result vector may be at different positions; they do not have to be adjacent. Additionally, the search vector for the LOOKUP must be sorted in ascending order, otherwise the search will not return any usable results.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id4484084				0	en-GB	If LOOKUP cannot find the search criterion, it matches the largest value in the search vector that is less than or equal to the search criterion.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152947	125			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154104	126			0	en-GB	LOOKUP(SearchCriterion; SearchVector; ResultVector)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150646	127			0	en-GB	\<emph\>SearchCriterion\</emph\> is the value to be searched for; entered either directly or as a reference.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154854	128			0	en-GB	\<emph\>SearchVector\</emph\> is the single-row or single-column area to be searched.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149925	129			0	en-GB	\<emph\>ResultVector\</emph\> is another single-row or single-column range from which the result of the function is taken. The result is the cell of the result vector with the same index as the instance found in the search vector.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148624	130			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149809	131			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LOOKUP(A1;D1:D100;F1:F100)\</item\> searches the corresponding cell in range D1:D100 for the number that you entered in A1. For the instance found, the index is determined, for example, the 12th cell in this range. Then, the contents of the 12th cell is returned as the value of the function (in the result vector).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149425				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>STYLE function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149425	133			0	en-GB	STYLE				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150826	134			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_VORLAGE\"\>Applies a style to the cell containing the formula.\</ahelp\> After a set amount of time, another style can be applied. This function always returns the value 0, allowing you to add it to another function without changing the value. Together with the CURRENT function you can apply a colour to a cell regardless of the value. For example: =...+STYLE(IF(CURRENT()>3;"red";"green")) applies the style "red" to the cell if the value is greater than 3, otherwise the style "green" is applied. Both cell formats have to be defined beforehand.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145373	135			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149302	136			0	en-GB	STYLE("Style"; Time; "Style2")				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150596	137			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Style\</emph\> is the name of a cell style assigned to the cell. Style names must be entered in quotation marks.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3156149	138			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Time\</emph\> is an optional time range in seconds. If this parameter is omitted the style will not be changed after a certain amount of time has passed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149520	139			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Style2\</emph\> is the optional name of a cell style assigned to the cell after a certain amount of time has passed. If this parameter is omitted "Default" is assumed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_idN111CA				0	en-GB	            \<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>         				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159254	140			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3151374	141			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=STYLE("Invisible";60;"Default")\</item\> formats the cell in transparent format for 60 seconds after the document was recalculated or loaded, then the Default format is assigned. Both cell formats have to be defined beforehand.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id8056886				0	en-GB	Since STYLE() has a numeric return value of zero, this return value gets appended to a string. This can be avoided using T() as in the following example 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3668935				0	en-GB	            \<item type=\"input\"\>="Text"&T(STYLE("myStyle"))\</item\>         				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3042085				0	en-GB	See also CURRENT() for another example.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150430				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>CHOOSE function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150430	142			0	en-GB	CHOOSE				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3143270	143			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_WAHL\"\>Uses an index to return a value from a list of 1 to 30 values.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153533	144			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3155425	145			0	en-GB	CHOOSE(Index; Value1; Value2; ... Value30)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3144755	146			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Index\</emph\> is a reference or number in the range 1 to 30 indicating which value is to be taken from the list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149939	147			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Value1; Value2; ... Value30\</emph\> is the list of values entered either as a reference to a cell or as 1 to 30 individual values.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151253	148			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150625	149			0	en-GB	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=CHOOSE(A1;B1;B2;B3;"Today";"Yesterday";"Tomorrow")\</item\>, for example, returns the contents of cell B2 for A1 = 2; for A1 = 4, the function returns the text "Today".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151001				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>HLOOKUP function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151001	151			0	en-GB	HLOOKUP				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3148688	152			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_WVERWEIS\"\>Searches for a value and reference to the cells below the selected area.\</ahelp\> This function tests whether the first row of an array contains a certain value. The function returns the value in a row of the array, named in the \<emph\>Index\</emph\>, in the same column.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154661	153			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3146070	154			0	en-GB	HLOOKUP(SearchCriteria; Array; Index; Sorted)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3148672	155			0	en-GB	See also:\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060109.xhp\" name=\"VLOOKUP\"\>VLOOKUP\</link\> (columns and rows are exchanged)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147321				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>ROW function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147321	157			0	en-GB	ROW				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154564	203			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZEILE\"\>Returns the row number of a cell reference.\</ahelp\> If the reference is a cell, it returns the row number of the cell. If the reference is a cell range, it returns the corresponding row numbers in a one-column \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060107.xhp#wasmatrix\" name=\"Array\"\>Array\</link\> if the formula is entered \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060107.xhp#somatrixformel\" name=\"as an array formula\"\>as an array formula\</link\>. If the ROW function with a range reference is not used in an array formula, only the row number of the first range cell will be returned.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158439	159			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154916	160			0	en-GB	ROW(Reference)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3156336	161			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Reference\</emph\> is a cell, an area, or the name of an area.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3151109	204			0	en-GB	If you do not indicate a reference, the row number of the cell in which the formula is entered will be found. \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc automatically sets the reference to the current cell.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155609	162			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154830	205			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROW(B3)\</item\> returns 3 because the reference refers to the third row in the table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3147094	206			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>{=ROW(D5:D8)}\</item\> returns the single-column array (5, 6, 7, 8) because the reference specified contains rows 5 through 8.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153701	207			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROW(D5:D8)\</item\> returns 5 because the ROW function is not used as array formula and only the number of the first row of the reference is returned.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150996	208			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>{=ROW(A1:E1)}\</item\> and \<item type=\"input\"\>=ROW(A1:E1)\</item\> both return 1 because the reference only contains row 1 as the first row in the table. (Because single-row areas only have one row number it does not make any difference whether or not the formula is used as an array formula.)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153671	209			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROW()\</item\> returns 3 if the formula was entered in row 3.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153790	210			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>{=ROW(Rabbit)}\</item\> returns the single-column array (1, 2, 3) if "Rabbit" is the named area (C1:D3).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145772				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>ROWS function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145772	166			0	en-GB	ROWS				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3148971	167			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZEILEN\"\>Returns the number of rows in a reference or array.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156051	168			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154357	169			0	en-GB	ROWS(Array)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3155942	170			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Array\</emph\> is the reference or named area for which the total number of rows is to be determined.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155869	171			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154725	212			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROWS(B5)\</item\> returns 1 because a cell only contains one row.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150102	172			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROWS(A10:B12)\</item\> returns 3.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3155143	213			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROWS(Rabbit)\</item\> returns 3 if "Rabbit" is the named area (C1:D3).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id9959410				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>HYPERLINK function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_idN11798				0	en-GB	HYPERLINK				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_idN117F1				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_HYPERLINK\"\>When you click a cell that contains the HYPERLINK function, the hyperlink opens.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_idN11800				0	en-GB	If you use the optional \<emph\>CellText\</emph\> parameter, the formula locates the URL, and then displays the text or number.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_idN11803				0	en-GB	To open a hyperlinked cell with the keyboard, select the cell, press F2 to enter the Edit mode, move the cursor in front of the hyperlink, press Shift+F10, and then choose \<emph\>Open Hyperlink\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_idN1180A				0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_idN1180E				0	en-GB	HYPERLINK("URL") or HYPERLINK("URL"; "CellText")				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_idN11811				0	en-GB	\<emph\>URL\</emph\> specifies the link target. The optional \<emph\>CellText\</emph\> parameter is the text string that is displayed in the cell and will be returned as the result of the function. If the \<emph\>CellText\</emph\> parameter is omitted, the \<emph\>URL\</emph\> is displayed in the cell text and will be returned as the result of the function.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id0907200912224576				0	en-GB	The number 0 is returned for empty cells and matrix elements.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_idN11823				0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_idN11827				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=HYPERLINK("http://www.example.org")\</item\> displays the text "http://www.example.org" in the cell and executes the hyperlink http://www.example.org when clicked.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_idN1182A				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=HYPERLINK("http://www.example.org";"Click here")\</item\> displays the text "Click here" in the cell and executes the hyperlink http://www.example.org when clicked.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id0907200912224534				0	en-GB	=HYPERLINK("http://www.example.org";12345) displays the number 12345 and executes the hyperlink http://www.example.org when clicked.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_idN1182D				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=HYPERLINK($B4)\</item\> where cell B4 contains \<item type=\"input\"\>http://www.example.org\</item\>. The function adds "http://www.example.org" to the URL of the hyperlink cell and returns the same text string, which is used as the formula result.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_idN11830				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=HYPERLINK("http://www.";"Click ") & "example.org"\</item\> displays the text "Click example.org" in the cell and executes the hyperlink http://www.example.org when clicked.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id8859523				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=HYPERLINK("#Sheet1.A1";"Go to top")\</item\> displays the text Go to top and jumps to cell Sheet1.A1 in this document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id2958769				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=HYPERLINK("file:///C:/writer.odt#Specification";"Go to Writer bookmark")\</item\> displays the text Go to Writer bookmark, loads the specified text document and jumps to bookmark "Specification".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id7682424				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>GETPIVOTDATA function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3747062				0	en-GB	GETPIVOTDATA				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3593859				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The GETPIVOTDATA function returns a result value from a pivot table. The value is addressed using field and item names, so it remains valid if the layout of the pivot table changes.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id9741508				0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id909451				0	en-GB	Two different syntax definitions can be used:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id1665089				0	en-GB	GETPIVOTDATA(TargetField; pivot table; [ Field 1; Item 1; ... ])				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id4997100				0	en-GB	GETPIVOTDATA(pivot table; Constraints)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id1672109				0	en-GB	The second syntax is assumed if exactly two parameters are given, of which the first parameter is a cell or cell range reference. The first syntax is assumed in all other cases. The Function Wizard shows the first syntax.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id9464094				0	en-GB	First Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id9302346				0	en-GB	            \<emph\>TargetField\</emph\> is a string that selects one of the pivot table's data fields. The string can be the name of the source column, or the data field name as shown in the table (like "Sum - Sales").				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id8296151				0	en-GB	            \<emph\>pivot table\</emph\> is a reference to a cell or cell range that is positioned within a pivot table or contains a pivot table. If the cell range contains several pivot tables, the table that was created last is used.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id4809411				0	en-GB	If no \<emph\>Field n / Item n\</emph\> pairs are given, the grand total is returned. Otherwise, each pair adds a constraint that the result must satisfy. \<emph\>Field n\</emph\> is the name of a field from the pivot table. \<emph\>Item n\</emph\> is the name of an item from that field.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id6454969				0	en-GB	If the pivot table table contains only a single result value that fulfils all of the constraints, or a subtotal result that summarises all matching values, that result is returned. If there is no matching result, or several ones without a subtotal for them, an error is returned. These conditions apply to results that are included in the pivot table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id79042				0	en-GB	If the source data contains entries that are hidden by settings of the pivot table, they are ignored. The order of the Field/Item pairs is not significant. Field and item names are not case-sensitive.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id7928708				0	en-GB	If no constraint for a page field is given, the field's selected value is implicitly used. If a constraint for a page field is given, it must match the field's selected value, or an error is returned. Page fields are the fields at the top left of a pivot table, populated using the "Page Fields" area of the pivot table layout dialogue box. From each page field, an item (value) can be selected, which means only that item is included in the calculation.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3864253				0	en-GB	Subtotal values from the pivot table are only used if they use the function "auto" (except when specified in the constraint, see \<item type=\"literal\"\>Second Syntax\</item\> below).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144016				0	en-GB	Second Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id9937131				0	en-GB	            \<emph\>pivot table\</emph\> has the same meaning as in the first syntax.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id5616626				0	en-GB	\<emph\>Constraints\</emph\> is a space-separated list. Entries can be quoted (single quotes). The whole string must be enclosed in quotes (double quotes), unless you reference the string from another cell.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id4076357				0	en-GB	One of the entries can be the data field name. The data field name can be left out if the pivot table contains only one data field, otherwise it must be present.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id8231757				0	en-GB	Each of the other entries specifies a constraint in the form \<item type=\"literal\"\>Field[Item]\</item\> (with literal characters [ and ]), or only \<item type=\"literal\"\>Item\</item\> if the item name is unique within all fields that are used in the pivot table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3168736				0	en-GB	A function name can be added in the form \<emph\>Field[Item;Function]\</emph\>, which will cause the constraint to match only subtotal values which use that function. The possible function names are Sum, Count, Average, Max, Min, Product, Count (Numbers only), StDev (Sample), StDevP (Population), Var (Sample), and VarP (Population), case-insensitive.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Text Functions				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145389				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>text in cells; functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>functions; text functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Function Wizard;text\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
