helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id2355113				0	en-GB	See also JIS function.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	bm_id9323709				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>BAHTTEXT function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id6695455				0	en-GB	BAHTTEXT				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id354014				0	en-GB	Converts a number to Thai text, including the Thai currency names.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id9942014				0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id8780785				0	en-GB	BAHTTEXT(Number)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id1539353				0	en-GB	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is any number. "Baht" is appended to the integral part of the number, and "Satang" is appended to the decimal part of the number.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id9694814				0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3289284				0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=BAHTTEXT(12.65)\</item\> returns a string in Thai characters with the meaning of "Twelve Baht and sixty five Satang".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153072				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>BASE function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153072	213			0	en-GB	BASE				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3153289	214			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_BASIS\"\>Converts a positive integer to a specified base into a text string from the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#zahlensystem\" name=\"numbering system\"\>numbering system\</link\>.\</ahelp\> The digits 0-9 and the letters A-Z are used.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146097	215			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3155743	216			0	en-GB	BASE(Number; Radix; [MinimumLength])				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3151339	217			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the positive integer to be converted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3159262	218			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Radix\</emph\> indicates the base of the number system. It may be any positive integer in the range 2 to 36.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3148746	219			0	en-GB	\<emph\>MinimumLength\</emph\> (optional) determines the minimum length of the character sequence that has been created. If the text is shorter than the indicated minimum length, zeros are added to the left of the string.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146323	220			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156399				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>decimal system; converting to\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3156399	221			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=BASE(17;10;4)\</item\> returns 0017 in the decimal system.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	bm_id3157871				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>binary system; converting to\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3157871	222			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=BASE(17;2)\</item\> returns 10001 in the binary system.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145226				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>hexadecimal system; converting to\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3145226	223			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=BASE(255;16;4)\</item\> returns 00FF in the hexadecimal system.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149321				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>CHAR function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149321	201			0	en-GB	CHAR				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3149150	202			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZEICHEN\"\>Converts a number into a character according to the current code table.\</ahelp\> The number can be a two-digit or three-digit integer number.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149945	203			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
