helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3155906	205			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is a number in the range 1 to 255 representing the code value for the character.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152982	207			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3149890	208			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CHAR(100)\</item\> returns the character \<emph\>d\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id0907200910283297				0	en-GB	="abc" & CHAR(10) & "def" inserts a newline character into the string.				20130618 17:22:18
