helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3147286	26			0	en-GB	REPLACE("Text"; Position; Length; "NewText")				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3149797	27			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Text\</emph\> refers to text of which a part will be replaced.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3166451	28			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Position\</emph\> refers to the position within the text where the replacement will begin.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3156040	29			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Length\</emph\> is the number of characters in \<emph\>Text\</emph\> to be replaced.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3159188	30			0	en-GB	\<emph\>NewText\</emph\> refers to the text which replaces \<emph\>Text\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146958	31			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3154096	32			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=REPLACE("1234567";1;1;"444")\</item\> returns the text string \<emph\>444234567\</emph\>. One character at position 1 is replaced by the complete \<item type=\"literal\"\>NewText\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
