helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3148728	10			0	en-GB	To calculate the intercept, use cells D3:D9 as the y-values and C3:C9 as the x-values from the example spreadsheet. Input will be as follows:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149013	11			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=INTERCEPT(D3:D9;C3:C9)\</item\> = 2.15.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148437				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>COUNT function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers;counting\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
