helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149254	18			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149953	19			0	en-GB	The entries 2, 4, 6 and eight in the Value 1 ... 4 fields are to be counted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154558	20			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNT(2;4;6;"eight")\</item\> = 3. The count of numbers is therefore 3.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149729				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>COUNTA function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of entries\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149729	22			0	en-GB	COUNTA				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150142	23			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ANZAHL2\"\>Counts how many values are in the list of arguments.\</ahelp\> Text entries are also counted, even when they contain an empty string of length 0. If an argument is an array or reference, empty cells within the array or reference are ignored.				20130618 17:22:18
