helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143228	76			0	en-GB	BINOMDIST				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3146897	77			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_BINOMVERT\"\>Returns the individual term binomial distribution probability.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149289	78			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3156009	79			0	en-GB	BINOMDIST(X; Trials; SP; C)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154304	80			0	en-GB	\<emph\>X\</emph\> is the number of successes in a set of trials.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3147492	81			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Trials\</emph\> is the number of independent trials.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3146085	82			0	en-GB	\<emph\>SP\</emph\> is the probability of success on each trial.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149760	83			0	en-GB	\<emph\>C\</emph\> = 0 calculates the probability of a single event and \<emph\>C\</emph\> = 1 calculates the cumulative probability.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151171	84			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3145666	85			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=BINOMDIST(A1;12;0.5;0)\</item\> shows (if the values \<item type=\"input\"\>0\</item\> to \<item type=\"input\"\>12\</item\> are entered in A1) the probabilities for 12 flips of a coin that \<emph\>Heads\</emph\> will come up exactly the number of times entered in A1.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150120	86			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=BINOMDIST(A1;12;0.5;1)\</item\> shows the cumulative probabilities for the same series. For example, if A1 = \<item type=\"input\"\>4\</item\>, the cumulative probability of the series is 0, 1, 2, 3 or 4 times \<emph\>Heads\</emph\> (non-exclusive OR).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id0119200902432928				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>CHISQINV function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id0119200902421451				0	en-GB	CHISQINV				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200902421449				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Returns the inverse of CHISQDIST.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id0119200902475241				0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200902475286				0	en-GB	            \<emph\>Probability\</emph\> is the probability value for which the inverse of the chi-square distribution is to be calculated.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200902475282				0	en-GB	            \<emph\>Degrees Of Freedom\</emph\> is the degrees of freedom for the chi-square function.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148835				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>CHIINV function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148835	88			0	en-GB	CHIINV				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149906	89			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_CHIINV\"\>Returns the inverse of the one-tailed probability of the chi-square distribution.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159157	90			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150504	91			0	en-GB	CHIINV(Number; DegreesFreedom)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154898	92			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value of the error probability.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154294	93			0	en-GB	\<emph\>DegreesFreedom\</emph\> is the degrees of freedom of the experiment.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154208	94			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150777	130			0	en-GB	A die is thrown 1020 times. The numbers on the die 1 through 6 come up 195, 151, 148, 189, 183 and 154 times respectively (observation values). The hypothesis that the die is not fixed is to be tested.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3153062	131			0	en-GB	The chi-square distribution of the random sample is determined by the formula given above. Since the expected value for a given number on the die for n throws is n times 1/6, thus 1020/6 = 170, the formula returns a chi-square value of 13.27.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3148806	132			0	en-GB	If the (observed) chi-square is greater than or equal to the (theoretical) chi-square CHIINV, the hypothesis will be discarded, since the deviation between theory and experiment is too great. If the observed chi-square is less that CHIINV, the hypothesis is confirmed with the indicated probability of error.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149763	95			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CHIINV(0.05;5)\</item\> returns 11.07.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3159142	133			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CHIINV(0.02;5)\</item\> returns 13.39.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3158401	134			0	en-GB	If the probability of error is 5%, the die is not true. If the probability of error is 2%, there is no reason to believe it is fixed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154260				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>CHITEST function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154260	97			0	en-GB	CHITEST				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3151052	98			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_CHITEST\"\>Returns the probability of a deviance from a random distribution of two test series based on the chi-square test for independence.\</ahelp\> CHITEST returns the chi-square distribution of the data.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3148925	135			0	en-GB	The probability determined by CHITEST can also be determined with CHIDIST, in which case the chi-square of the random sample must then be passed as a parameter instead of the data row.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154280	99			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149162	100			0	en-GB	CHITEST(DataB; DataE)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3158421	101			0	en-GB	\<emph\>DataB\</emph\> is the array of the observations.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3166453	102			0	en-GB	\<emph\>DataE\</emph\> is the range of the expected values.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146946	103			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154096	136			0	en-GB	Data_B (observed)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3152948	137			0	en-GB	Data_E (expected)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3152876	138			0	en-GB	1				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3159279	139			0	en-GB	                     \<item type=\"input\"\>195\</item\>                  				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149105	140			0	en-GB	                     \<item type=\"input\"\>170\</item\>                  				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149922	141			0	en-GB	2				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3148621	142			0	en-GB	                     \<item type=\"input\"\>151\</item\>                  				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3148987	143			0	en-GB	                     \<item type=\"input\"\>170\</item\>                  				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149417	144			0	en-GB	3				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3148661	145			0	en-GB	                     \<item type=\"input\"\>148\</item\>                  				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3151128	146			0	en-GB	                     \<item type=\"input\"\>170\</item\>                  				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3148467	147			0	en-GB	4				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149237	148			0	en-GB	                     \<item type=\"input\"\>189\</item\>                  				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3145304	149			0	en-GB	                     \<item type=\"input\"\>170\</item\>                  				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149927	150			0	en-GB	5				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150630	151			0	en-GB	                     \<item type=\"input\"\>183\</item\>                  				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150423	152			0	en-GB	                     \<item type=\"input\"\>170\</item\>                  				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3143275	153			0	en-GB	6				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3144750	154			0	en-GB	                     \<item type=\"input\"\>154\</item\>                  				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3153947	155			0	en-GB	                     \<item type=\"input\"\>170\</item\>                  				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149481	104			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CHITEST(A1:A6;B1:B6)\</item\> equals 0.02. This is the probability which suffices the observed data of the theoretical chi-square distribution.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148690				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>CHIDIST function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148690	106			0	en-GB	CHIDIST				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3156338	156			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_CHIVERT\"\>Returns the probability value from the indicated chi-square that a hypothesis is confirmed.\</ahelp\> CHIDIST compares the chi-square value to be given for a random sample that is calculated from the sum of (observed value-expected value)^2/expected value for all values with the theoretical chi-square distribution and determines from this the probability of error for the hypothesis to be tested.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3151316	157			0	en-GB	The probability determined by CHIDIST can also be determined by CHITEST.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155123	108			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3158439	109			0	en-GB	CHIDIST(Number; DegreesFreedom)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3148675	110			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the chi-square value of the random sample used to determine the error probability.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3155615	111			0	en-GB	\<emph\>DegreesFreedom\</emph\> are the degrees of freedom of the experiment.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146787	112			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3145774	113			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CHIDIST(13.27; 5)\</item\> equals 0.02.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3156141	158			0	en-GB	If the chi-square value of the random sample is 13.27 and if the experiment has 5 degrees of freedom, then the hypothesis is assured with a probability of error of 2%.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id0119200902231887				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>CHISQDIST function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chi-square distribution\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id0119200901583452				0	en-GB	CHISQDIST				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200901583471				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Returns the value of the probability density function or the cumulative distribution function for the chi-square distribution.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id0119200902395520				0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200902395679				0	en-GB	CHISQDIST(Number; Degrees Of Freedom; Cumulative)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id011920090239564				0	en-GB	            \<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the number for which the function is to be calculated.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200902395660				0	en-GB	            \<emph\>Degrees Of Freedom\</emph\> is the degrees of freedom for the chi-square function.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200902395623				0	en-GB	            \<emph\>Cumulative\</emph\> (optional): 0 or False calculates the probability density function. Other values or True or omitted calculates the cumulative distribution function.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150603				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>EXPONDIST function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exponential distributions\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150603	115			0	en-GB	EXPONDIST				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149563	116			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_EXPONVERT\"\>Returns the exponential distribution.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153789	117			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150987	118			0	en-GB	EXPONDIST(Number; Lambda; C)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154663	119			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value of the function.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154569	120			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Lambda\</emph\> is the parameter value.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3147332	121			0	en-GB	\<emph\>C\</emph\> is a logical value that determines the form of the function. \<emph\>C = 0\</emph\> calculates the density function, and \<emph\>C = 1\</emph\> calculates the distribution.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146133	122			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150357	123			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=EXPONDIST(3;0.5;1)\</item\> returns 0.78.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Statistical Functions Part Two				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154372	1			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"fh\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060182.xhp\" name=\"Statistical Functions Part Two\"\>Statistical Functions Part Two\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145388				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>FINV function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inverse F probability distribution\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145388	2			0	en-GB	FINV				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3155089	3			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_FINV\"\>Returns the inverse of the F-distribution.\</ahelp\> The F-distribution is used for F-tests in order to set the relation between two differing data sets.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153816	4			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3153068	5			0	en-GB	FINV(Number; DegreesFreedom1; DegreesFreedom2)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3146866	6			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the probability value for which the inverse F-distribution is to be calculated.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3153914	7			0	en-GB	\<emph\>DegreesFreedom1\</emph\> is the number of degrees of freedom in the numerator of the F-distribution.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3148607	8			0	en-GB	\<emph\>DegreesFreedom2\</emph\> is the number of degrees of freedom in the denominator of the F-distribution.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156021	9			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3145073	10			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=FINV(0.5;5;10)\</item\> yields 0.93.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150888				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>FISHER function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
