helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200903205379				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Returns the Gamma function value.\</ahelp\> Note that GAMMAINV is not the inverse of GAMMA, but of GAMMADIST.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id0119200903271613				0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200903271614				0	en-GB	            \<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the number for which the Gamma function value is to be calculated.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154841				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>GAMMAINV function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154841	47			0	en-GB	GAMMAINV				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3153932	48			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_GAMMAINV\"\>Returns the inverse of the Gamma cumulative distribution GAMMADIST.\</ahelp\> This function allows you to search for variables with different distribution.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149949	49			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3155828	50			0	en-GB	GAMMAINV(Number; Alpha; Beta)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3145138	51			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the probability value for which the inverse Gamma distribution is to be calculated.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3152785	52			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Alpha\</emph\> is the parameter Alpha of the Gamma distribution.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3154561	53			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Beta\</emph\> is the parameter Beta of the Gamma distribution.				20130618 17:22:18
