helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3149287	116			0	en-GB	HARMEAN(Number1; Number2; ... Number30)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3154303	117			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Number1; Number2; ... Number30\</emph\> are 1 to 30 values or ranges that can be used to calculate the harmonic mean.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159179	118			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3146093	120			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=HARMEAN(23;46;69)\</item\> = 37.64. The harmonic mean of this random sample is thus 37.64				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152801				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>HYPGEOMDIST function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sampling without replacement\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152801	122			0	en-GB	HYPGEOMDIST				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3159341	123			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_HYPGEOMVERT\"\>Returns the hypergeometric distribution.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
