helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3155388	125			0	en-GB	HYPGEOMDIST(X; NSample; Successes; NPopulation)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3154933	126			0	en-GB	\<emph\>X\</emph\> is the number of results achieved in the random sample.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3153106	127			0	en-GB	\<emph\>NSample\</emph\> is the size of the random sample.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3146992	128			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Successes\</emph\> is the number of possible results in the total population.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3148826	129			0	en-GB	\<emph\>NPopulation \</emph\>is the size of the total population.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150529	130			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3154904	131			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=HYPGEOMDIST(2;2;90;100)\</item\> yields 0.81. If 90 out of 100 pieces of buttered toast fall from the table and land on the floor buttered side down, then if 2 pieces of buttered toast are dropped from the table, the probability is 81% that both will land buttered side down.				20130618 17:22:18
