helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154511				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>MAX function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154511	2			0	en-GB	MAX				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153709	3			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MAX\"\>Returns the maximum value in a list of arguments.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id9282509				0	en-GB	Returns 0 if no numeric value and no error was encountered in the cell range(s) passed as cell reference(s). Text cells are ignored by MIN() and MAX(). The functions MINA() and MAXA() return 0 if no value (numeric or text) and no error was encountered. Passing a literal string argument to MIN() or MAX(), e.g. MIN("string"), still results in an error.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154256	4			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3147340	5			0	en-GB	MAX(Number1; Number2; ... Number30)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149568	6			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Number1; Number2; ... Number30\</emph\> are 1 to 30 numeric values or ranges. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153963	7			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3147343	8			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MAX(A1;A2;A3;50;100;200)\</item\> returns the largest value from the list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3148485	9			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MAX(A1:B100)\</item\> returns the largest value from the list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3166426				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>MAXA function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166426	139			0	en-GB	MAXA				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150363	140			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MAXA\"\>Returns the maximum value in a list of arguments. Unlike MAX, you can also use text strings. The value of a text string is 0.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id7689443				0	en-GB	The functions MINA() and MAXA() return 0 if no value (numeric or text) and no error was encountered.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150516	141			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3166431	142			0	en-GB	MAXA(Value1; Value2; ... Value30)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150202	143			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Value1; Value2; ... Value30\</emph\> are 1 to 30 values or ranges. Text has the value of 0.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156290	144			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3156446	145			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MAXA(A1;A2;A3;50;100;200;"Text")\</item\> returns the largest value from the list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149404	146			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MAXA(A1:B100)\</item\> returns the largest value from the list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153820				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>MEDIAN function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153820	11			0	en-GB	MEDIAN				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3151241	12			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MEDIAN\"\>Returns the median of a set of numbers. In a set containing an uneven number of values, the median will be the number in the middle of the set and in a set containing an even number of values, it will be the mean of the two values in the middle of the set.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148871	13			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3155264	14			0	en-GB	MEDIAN(Number1; Number2; ... Number30)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150109	15			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Number1; Number2; ... Number30\</emph\> are 1 to 30 values or ranges, which represent a sample. Each number can also be replaced by a reference.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144506	16			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145078	17			0	en-GB	for an odd number: \<item type=\"input\"\>=MEDIAN(1;5;9;20;21)\</item\> returns the middle value, 9, as the median value.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149126	165			0	en-GB	for an even number: \<item type=\"input\"\>=MEDIAN(1;5;9;20)\</item\> returns the average of the two middle values 5 and 9, i.e. 7.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154541				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>MIN function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
