helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days.xhp	0	help	par_id3155139	117			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_TAGE\"\>Calculates the difference between two date values.\</ahelp\> The result returns the number of days between the two days.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155184	118			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578	119			0	en-GB	DAYS(Date2; Date1)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days.xhp	0	help	par_id3151376	120			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Date1\</emph\> is the start date, \<emph\>Date2\</emph\> is the end date. If \<emph\>Date2\</emph\> is an earlier date than \<emph\>Date1\</emph\> the result is a negative number.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151001	121			0	en-GB	Examples				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days.xhp	0	help	par_id3159101	123			0	en-GB	=DAYS("2010-01-01"; NOW()) returns the number of days from today until 1st January 2010.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days.xhp	0	help	par_id3163720	172			0	en-GB	=DAYS("1990-10-10";"1980-10-10") returns 3652 days.				20130618 17:22:18
