helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_networkdays.xhp	0	help	par_id3151110	245			0	en-GB	\<emph\>EndDate\</emph\> is the date up until which the calculation is carried out. If the end date is a working day, the day is included in the calculation.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_networkdays.xhp	0	help	par_id3154115	246			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Holidays\</emph\> (optional) is a list of holidays. These are non-working days. Enter a cell range in which the holidays are listed individually.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_networkdays.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146902	247			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_networkdays.xhp	0	help	par_id3154661	248			0	en-GB	How many working days fall between 2001-12-15 and 2002-01-15? The start date is located in C3 and the end date in D3. Cells F3 to J3 contain the following Christmas and New Year holidays: "2001-12-24", "2001-12-25", "2001-12-26", "2001-12-31", "2002-01-01".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_networkdays.xhp	0	help	par_id3147328	249			0	en-GB	=NETWORKDAYS(C3;D3;F3:J3) returns 17 working days.				20130618 17:22:18
