helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	WEEKDAY 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154925				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>WEEKDAY function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154925	136			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"weekday\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_weekday.xhp\"\>WEEKDAY\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3154228	137			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_WOCHENTAG\"\>Returns the day of the week for the given date value.\</ahelp\> The day is returned as an integer in the range 1 (Sunday) to 7 (Saturday) if Type is omitted or Type=1 is specified. If Type=2, numbering begins at Monday=1; and if Type=3 numbering begins at Monday=0.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147217	138			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3149033	139			0	en-GB	WEEKDAY(Number; Type)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3149046	140			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Number\</emph\>, as a date value, is a decimal for which the weekday is to be returned.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3154394	141			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> determines the type of calculation. For Type=1, the weekdays are counted starting from Sunday (this is the default if the Type parameter is omitted). For Type=2, the weekdays are counted starting from Monday=1. For Type=3, the weekdays are counted starting from Monday=0.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3156188	142			0	en-GB	These values apply only to the standard date format that you select under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - Calculate\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153836	143			0	en-GB	Examples				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3150317	144			0	en-GB	=WEEKDAY("14/06/2000") returns 4 (the Type parameter is omitted, therefore the standard count is used. The standard count starts with Sunday as day number 1. 14th June 2000 was a Wednesday and therefore day number 4).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3153174	145			0	en-GB	=WEEKDAY("1996-07-24";2) returns 3 (the Type parameter is 2, therefore Monday is day number 1. 24th July 1996 was a Wednesday and therefore day number 3).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3153525	146			0	en-GB	=WEEKDAY("1996-07-24";1) returns 4 (the Type parameter is 1, therefore Sunday is day number 1. 24th July 1996 was a Wednesday and therefore day number 4).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3150575	147			0	en-GB	=WEEKDAY(NOW()) returns the number of the current day.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3150588	171			0	en-GB	To obtain a function indicating whether a day in A1 is a business day, use the IF and WEEKDAY functions as follows: \<br/\>IF(WEEKDAY(A1;2) < 6;"Business day";"Weekend")				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknum.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	WEEKNUM				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknum.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159161				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>WEEKNUM function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknum.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159161	54			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"weeknum\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_weeknum.xhp\"\>WEEKNUM\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknum.xhp	0	help	par_id3149770	55			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KALENDERWOCHE\"\>WEEKNUM calculates the week number of the year for the internal date value.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknum.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E4				0	en-GB	The International Standard ISO 8601 has decreed that Monday shall be the first day of the week. A week that lies partly in one year and partly in another is assigned a number in the year in which most of its days lie. That means that week number 1 of any year is the week that contains 4th January.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknum.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153055	56			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknum.xhp	0	help	par_id3147236	57			0	en-GB	WEEKNUM(Number; Mode)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknum.xhp	0	help	par_id3147511	58			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the internal date number.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknum.xhp	0	help	par_id3154269	59			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Mode\</emph\> sets the start of the week and the calculation type.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknum.xhp	0	help	par_id3148930	60			0	en-GB	1 = Sunday				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknum.xhp	0	help	par_id3154280	61			0	en-GB	2 = Monday				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknum.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146948	62			0	en-GB	Examples				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknum.xhp	0	help	par_id3150704	65			0	en-GB	=WEEKNUM("1995-01-01";1) returns 1 (1st January 1995 was a Sunday)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknum.xhp	0	help	par_id3149792	64			0	en-GB	=WEEKNUM("1995-01-01";2) returns 52. If the week starts on Monday, Sunday belongs to the last week of the previous year.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknumadd.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	WEEKNUM_ADD 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknumadd.xhp	0	help	bm_id3166443				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>WEEKNUM_ADD function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknumadd.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166443	222			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"weeknumadd\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_weeknumadd.xhp\"\>WEEKNUM_ADD\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknumadd.xhp	0	help	par_id3152945	223			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_WEEKNUM\"\>The result indicates the number of the calendar week for a date.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknumadd.xhp	0	help	par_idN105DD				0	en-GB	The WEEKNUM_ADD function is designed to calculate week numbers exactly as Microsoft Excel does. Use the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_weeknum.xhp\"\>WEEKNUM\</link\> function, or format your date cells using the WW formatting code, when you need ISO 8601 week numbers.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknumadd.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153745	224			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknumadd.xhp	0	help	par_id3153685	225			0	en-GB	WEEKNUM_ADD(Date; ReturnType)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknumadd.xhp	0	help	par_id3159277	226			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Date\</emph\> is the date within the calendar week.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknumadd.xhp	0	help	par_id3154098	227			0	en-GB	\<emph\>ReturnType\</emph\> is 1 for week beginning on a Sunday, 2 for week beginning on a Monday.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknumadd.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152886	228			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknumadd.xhp	0	help	par_id3149973	229			0	en-GB	In which week number does 24/12/2001 fall?				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknumadd.xhp	0	help	par_id3149914	230			0	en-GB	\<item type=\"input\"\>=WEEKNUM_ADD("24/12/2001";1)\</item\> returns 52.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	WORKDAY				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149012				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>WORKDAY function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149012	186			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"workday\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_workday.xhp\"\>WORKDAY\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3149893	187			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_WORKDAY\"\> The result is a date number that can be formatted as a date. You then see the date of a day that is a certain number of \<emph\>working days\</emph\> away from the \<emph\>start date\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146944	188			0	en-GB	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3154844	189			0	en-GB	WORKDAY(StartDate; Days; Holidays)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3147469	190			0	en-GB	\<emph\>StartDate\</emph\> is the date from which the calculation is carried out. If the start date is a working day, the day is included in the calculation.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3153038	191			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Days\</emph\> is the number of working days. Positive value for a result after the start date, negative value for a result before the start date.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3150693	192			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Holidays\</emph\> (optional) is a list of holidays. These are non-working days. Enter a cell range in which the holidays are listed individually.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150141	193			0	en-GB	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3152782	194			0	en-GB	What date came 17 working days after 1st December 2001? Enter the start date "2001-12-01" in C3 and the number of working days in D3. Cells F3 to J3 contain the following Christmas and New Year holidays: "2001-12-24", "2001-12-25", "2001-12-26", "2001-12-31", "2002-01-01".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3146142	195			0	en-GB	=WORKDAY(C3;D3;F3:J3) returns 2001-12-28. Format the serial date number as a date, for example in the format DD/MM/YYYY.				20130618 17:22:18
