helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410	2			0	en-GB	Under Windows only, you can view any $[officename] document in a window of the Microsoft Internet Explorer. Install the ActiveX control in the $[officename] Setup program.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156346	3			0	en-GB	Installing the ActiveX control				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3153821	4			0	en-GB	Close $[officename] and the Quickstarter.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771	5			0	en-GB	Click the Start button on the Windows taskbar. Choose \<emph\>Control Panel\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E8				0	en-GB	In the Control Panel, click \<emph\>Add or Remove Programs\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3156155	6			0	en-GB	In the list, click %PRODUCTNAME, then click \<emph\>Change\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
