helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Turning off Automatic URL Recognition				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149346				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function; URL recognition\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>recognising URLs automatically\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic hyperlink formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>URL;turning off URL recognition\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks;turning off automatic recognition\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>links;turning off automatic recognition\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>predictive text, see also AutoCorrect function/AutoFill function/AutoInput function/word completion/text completion\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149346	6			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"autocorr_url\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/autocorr_url.xhp\" name=\"Turning off Automatic URL Recognition\"\>Turning off Automatic URL Recognition\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410	7			0	en-GB	When you enter text, $[officename] automatically recognises a word that may be a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#url\" name=\"URL\"\>URL\</link\> and replaces the word with a hyperlink. $[officename] formats the hyperlink with direct font attributes (colour and underline) the properties of which are obtained from certain Character Styles.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561	2			0	en-GB	If you do not want $[officename] to automatically recognise URLs as you are typing, there are several ways of turning off this feature.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154306	8			0	en-GB	Undo URL Recognition				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233	3			0	en-GB	When you are typing and notice that some text has just been automatically converted into a hyperlink, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Z to undo this formatting.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3149235	4			0	en-GB	If you do not notice this conversion until later, select the hyperlink and choose the menu command \<emph\>Format - Default Formatting\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152350	9			0	en-GB	Turn off URL Recognition				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3149514	10			0	en-GB	Load a document of the type for which you want to modify the URL recognition.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3151246	11			0	en-GB	If you want to modify the URL recognition for text documents, open a text document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413	12			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550	13			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>AutoCorrect\</emph\> dialogue box, select the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360	14			0	en-GB	If you unmark \<emph\>URL Recognition\</emph\>, words will no longer be automatically replaced with hyperlinks.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3156423	15			0	en-GB	In $[officename] Writer there are two check boxes in front of \<emph\>URL Recognition\</emph\>. The box in the first column is for later post-editing and the box in the second column is for AutoCorrect as you type.				20130618 17:22:18
