helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_id3149797	6			0	en-GB	If the \<emph\>Always create a backup copy\</emph\> option is selected, the old version of the file is saved to the backup directory whenever you save the current version of the file.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685	7			0	en-GB	You can change the backup directory by choosing \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - Paths\</emph\>, then change the \<emph\>Backups\</emph\> path in the dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_id3149415	8			0	en-GB	The backup copy has the same name as the document, but the extension is .BAK. If the backup folder already contains such a file, it will be overwritten without warning.				20130618 17:22:18
