helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3153092	20			0	en-GB	If you click the arrow next to the \<emph\>New\</emph\> icon, a sub-menu opens in which you can select another document type.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id0820200803501358				0	en-GB	System File Dialogue Boxes or %PRODUCTNAME Dialogue Boxes				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803501356				0	en-GB	On most operating systems, you can choose to use the system file dialogue boxes or %PRODUCTNAME dialogue boxes.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803501429				0	en-GB	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - General\</item\> to switch the type of open/save dialogue boxes.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803501449				0	en-GB	The %PRODUCTNAME dialogue boxes support file download and upload using secure https connections.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id0820200803501453				0	en-GB	Opening Files from a Web Server				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3153126	9			0	en-GB	You can enter a URL in the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box of the \<emph\>Open\</emph\> dialogue boxes. The URL must start with file:/// or ftp:// or http://.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803501548				0	en-GB	If you use the %PRODUCTNAME dialogue box, you can use the https:// prefix for a secure connection, and you can save a document on the web server.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_idN107C4				0	en-GB	When you open a file by a URL from the Windows file dialogue box, Windows will open a local copy of the file, located in the Internet Explorer cache. The %PRODUCTNAME file dialogue box opens a local copy of the file in the system's temp folder.				20130618 17:22:18
