helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154927	49			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_gallery\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_gallery.xhp\" name=\"Adding Graphics to the Gallery\"\>Adding Graphics to the Gallery\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267	50			0	en-GB	You can place a graphic from a document such as an HTML page in the Gallery by drag-and-drop.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823	56			0	en-GB	Display the Gallery theme to which you want to add the graphic.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748	51			0	en-GB	Position the mouse pointer above the graphic, without clicking.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346	52			0	en-GB	If the mouse pointer changes to a hand symbol, the graphic refers to a hyperlink. In this case, click the graphic while pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key to select it without executing the respective link.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578	53			0	en-GB	If the mouse pointer does not change to a hand symbol, you can simply click the graphic to select it.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3145120	54			0	en-GB	Once the graphic is selected, release the mouse button. Click again on the graphic image, keeping the mouse button pressed for more than two seconds. The graphic image is copied to the internal memory.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3150772	55			0	en-GB	Without releasing the mouse button, drag the graphic into the Gallery.				20130618 17:22:18
