helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150616	17			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"error_report\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/error_report.xhp\" name=\"Error Report Tool\"\>Error Report Tool\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345	1			0	en-GB	The Error Report Tool starts automatically when a program crash occurs.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088	2			0	en-GB	The Error Report Tool gathers all necessary information that can help the program developers to improve the code, so that in later versions this error can possibly be avoided. Please help us to improve the software and send the generated error report.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148538	4			0	en-GB	Starting the Error Report Tool				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811	5			0	en-GB	With most program crashes the Error Report Tool will start automatically.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154046	7			0	en-GB	Completing the Report				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335	8			0	en-GB	On the main Error Report Tool dialogue box, you can enter some additional information that may help the developers to localise the error. For example, if the error only appears after a change in your hardware or software environment, or if you clicked on a button, please include that information.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159399	9			0	en-GB	Sending the Error Report				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3150504	10			0	en-GB	The Error Report Tool uses the HTTP PUT / SOAP protocol to send the report data. You may optionally enter some descriptive text that will help us to identify the context of the program crash. Then click the \<emph\>Send\</emph\> button.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670	11			0	en-GB	You will not get an answer to your error report. If you need support, please visit the \<link href=\"text/shared/main0108.xhp\"\>support forum\</link\> on the Internet.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3153526	12			0	en-GB	You may choose to respond to questions that the developers may have about the reported error. Mark the check box if you allow to be contacted by e-mail, should additional information be required. By default this check box is not marked, so you will not get any e-mail.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792	13			0	en-GB	What Data is Sent?				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366	14			0	en-GB	The error report consists of several files. The main file contains information about the error type, operating system name and version, memory usage, and the description that you entered. You can click the \<emph\>Show Report\</emph\> button on the main dialogue box of the Error Report Tool to view what will get sent in the main file.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3151177	15			0	en-GB	In addition, relevant memory contents and stack traces are gathered by some system standard tools ("dbhhelp.dll" on Windows systems, "pstack" on UNIX systems). This information will be sent also.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\export_ms.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Saving Documents in Other Formats				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\export_ms.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159233				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>documents; saving in other formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving; documents in other formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>files; saving in other formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text documents;saving in other formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; saving in other formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawings; saving in other formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; saving in other formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting; to Microsoft Office formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Word documents; saving as\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Excel; saving as\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>PowerPoint; saving as\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\export_ms.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149416	6			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"export_ms\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/export_ms.xhp\" name=\"Saving Documents in Other Formats\"\>Saving Documents in Other Formats\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\export_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084	2			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>File - Save as\</emph\>. You will see the \<emph\>Save as\</emph\> dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\export_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3153348	3			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Save as type\</emph\> or \<emph\>File type\</emph\> list box, select the desired format.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\export_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3150985	4			0	en-GB	Enter a name in the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\export_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3153252	7			0	en-GB	If you want the file dialogue boxes to offer another file format as default, select that format in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Load/Save - General\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Default file format\</emph\> area.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\export_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669	5			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070000.xhp\" name=\"Save As\"\>Save As\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Sending Faxes and Configuring $[officename] for Faxing				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156426				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>faxes; sending\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>faxes;configuring $[officename]\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sending; documents as faxes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>configuring;fax icon\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156426	5			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"fax\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/fax.xhp\" name=\"Sending Faxes and Configuring $[officename] for Faxing\"\>Sending Faxes and Configuring $[officename] for Faxing\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410	3			0	en-GB	To send a fax directly from $[officename], you need a fax modem and a fax driver that allows applications to communicate with the fax modem.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166410	6			0	en-GB	Sending a Fax Through the Print Dialogue Box				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996	7			0	en-GB	Open the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialogue box by choosing \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\> and select the fax driver in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> list box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3155135	8			0	en-GB	Clicking \<emph\>OK\</emph\> opens the dialogue box for your fax driver, in which you can select the fax recipient.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153825	9			0	en-GB	Configuring $[officename] a Fax Icon				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3153822	10			0	en-GB	You can configure $[officename] so that a single click on an icon automatically sends the current document as a fax:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315	11			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040400.xhp\" name=\"Writer - Print\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Print\</link\>\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3150985	12			0	en-GB	Select the fax driver from the \<emph\>Fax\</emph\> list box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EB				0	en-GB	Click the arrow icon at the end of the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar. In the drop-down menu, choose \<emph\>Customise\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F6				0	en-GB	The \<emph\>Toolbar\</emph\>s tab page of the \<emph\>Customise\</emph\> dialogue box will appear.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FA				0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>Add Commands\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN10702				0	en-GB	Select the "Documents" category, then select the "Send Default Fax" command.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN10706				0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> and then \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN10712				0	en-GB	On the \<emph\>Toolbars\</emph\> tab page, click the down arrow button to position the new icon where you want it. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN10715				0	en-GB	Your \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar now has a new icon to send the current document as a fax.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Using the Filter Navigator				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150322				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>filters; Navigator\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filter conditions;connecting\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A3				0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"filternavigator\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/filternavigator.xhp\"\>Using the Filter Navigator\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3150322	13			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FormFilterNavigator\"\>To connect several filter conditions with Boolean OR, click the \<emph\>Filter navigation\</emph\> icon on the filter bar.\</ahelp\> The \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\> window will appear.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3153711	14			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FILTER_NAVIGATOR\"\>The filter conditions that have been set appear in the \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\>. As soon as a filter is set, you see a blank filter entry at the bottom of the \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\>. You can select this entry by clicking the word "Or". Once you have selected the blank filter entry, you can enter additional filter conditions in the form. These conditions are linked by Boolean OR to the previously defined conditions.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3145620	15			0	en-GB	The context menu can be called for each entry in the \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\>. \<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_FILTER_IS_NOT_NULL\"\>You can edit the filter conditions in this area directly as text. If you wish to check if a field has content or no content, you can select the filter conditions "empty" (SQL:"Is Null") or "not empty" (SQL: "Is not Null").\</ahelp\> It is also possible to delete the entry by using the context menu.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3156374	16			0	en-GB	You can move filter conditions in the \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\> by dragging-and-dropping, or use the keys \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Alt+Up Arrow or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Alt+Down Arrow. To copy filter conditions, drag them while holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Searching for Attributes				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	bm_id5681020				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>fonts;finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>font attributes;finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text attributes;finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>attributes; finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>finding; attributes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resetting;Find & Replace mode\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN10663				0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"find_attributes\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/find_attributes.xhp\"\>Searching for Attributes\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN10681				0	en-GB	You can search for text with attributes that are applied either by direct formatting or by styles. For example, if you search for the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> attribute, all instances of text that do not use the default font are found. All text that has a directly coded font attribute, and all text where a style switches the font attribute, are found.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN10688				0	en-GB	If you want to find text with any font by name, click the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> button in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100000.xhp\"\>Find & Replace\</link\> dialogue box of %PRODUCTNAME Writer.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069D				0	en-GB	After you select the attributes that you want to search for, the \<emph\>Search for Styles\</emph\> box in the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> area of the %PRODUCTNAME Writer \<emph\>Find & Replace\</emph\> dialogue box changes to \<emph\>Including Styles\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B0				0	en-GB	If you want to search for text in which attributes were set by using direct formatting and styles, select the \<emph\>Including Styles\</emph\> box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B7				0	en-GB	The search criteria for attributes are listed below the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BE				0	en-GB	To search for all font changes				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C5				0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CD				0	en-GB	Clear the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box if necessary.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D5				0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>Attributes\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DD				0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Attributes\</emph\> dialogue box, mark the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> check box and click OK.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E8				0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Find & Replace\</emph\> dialogue box, you now can read "Font" below the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F4				0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>Find\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FB				0	en-GB	All places where a font change was applied, either directly or by assigning an appropriate style, are found.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FE				0	en-GB	To reset the Find & Replace mode				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN10702				0	en-GB	To stop searching for the current attributes, reset the \<emph\>Find & Replace\</emph\> dialogue box to normal mode.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070C				0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>No Format\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071E				0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100000.xhp\"\>Find & Replace\</link\> dialogue box				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_id6837672				0	en-GB	Searching for attributes is available in the Find & Replace dialogue box for text documents.				20130618 17:22:18
