helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152801	9			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"floating_toolbar\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/floating_toolbar.xhp\" name=\"Using Toolbars\"\>Using Toolbars\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267	7			0	en-GB	Some toolbar icons, for example the \<emph\>Font Colour\</emph\> icon, can open another toolbar. Click the arrow next to the icon to open a toolbar containing further icons.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3155450	8			0	en-GB	You now have a choice: either click the icon that you want to activate, or seize the toolbar by its title bar and drag it while holding down the mouse button.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	hd_id733970				0	en-GB	Context of Toolbars				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id341196				0	en-GB	Some toolbars open automatically depending on the context. For example, when you click inside a table in a text document, the Table toolbar opens. When you click inside a numbered paragraph, the Bullets and Numbering toolbar opens.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	hd_id4224372				0	en-GB	To Close a Toolbar Temporarily				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id295724				0	en-GB	Click the icon in the toolbar's title bar, or choose \<emph\>Close Toolbar\</emph\> from the context menu. The toolbar will be shown automatically again when the context becomes active again.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	hd_id1905575				0	en-GB	To Close a Toolbar Permanently				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id9776909				0	en-GB	While the toolbar is visible, choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars\</emph\> and click the name of the toolbar to remove the check mark.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077E				0	en-GB	To Show a Closed Toolbar				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_idN10785				0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars\</emph\> and click the name of the toolbar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id7296975				0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Reset\</emph\> to reset the toolbars to their default context sensitive behaviour. Now some toolbars will be shown automatically, dependent on the context.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E9				0	en-GB	To Make a Toolbar a Floating Toolbar				20130618 17:22:18
