helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154136				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>graphics, see also pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>images, see also pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>images; inserting and editing bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>illustrations, see pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bitmaps; inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pixel graphics; inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting; bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing; bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>invert filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>smoothing filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sharpening filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>remove noise filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>solarisation filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ageing filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>posterising filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pop-art filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charcoal sketches filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>mosaic filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures;filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filters;pictures\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154136	1			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"insert_bitmap\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/insert_bitmap.xhp\" name=\"Inserting, Editing, Saving Bitmaps\"\>Inserting, Editing, Saving Bitmaps\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149811	2			0	en-GB	Inserting Bitmaps				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031	3			0	en-GB	A bitmap image can be inserted in $[officename] Writer, $[officename] Calc, $[officename] Draw and $[officename] Impress documents.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209	4			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Picture - From File\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3149236	5			0	en-GB	Select the file. In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> box you can restrict the selection to certain file types.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153126	6			0	en-GB	Click the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> box if you want a link to the original file.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3154306	7			0	en-GB	If the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> box is marked, whenever the document is updated and loaded the bitmap image is reloaded. The editing steps that you have carried out in the local copy of the image in the document are re-applied and the image is displayed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3147336	8			0	en-GB	If the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> box is not marked, you are always working with the copy created when the graphic was first inserted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153824	26			0	en-GB	To embed graphics that were first inserted as links, go to \<emph\>Edit - Links\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Break Link\</emph\> button.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3151384	9			0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\> to insert the image.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147303	10			0	en-GB	Editing Bitmaps				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id187078				0	en-GB	Icons on the Picture bar				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3148552	11			0	en-GB	When you select the bitmap image, the \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> Bar offers you the tools for editing the image. Only a local copy is edited in the document, even if you have inserted an image as a link.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413	12			0	en-GB	The \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> Bar may look slightly different depending to the module you are using.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3154124	13			0	en-GB	A number of filters are located on the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/24010000.xhp\" name=\"Graphic Filter\"\>\<emph\>Graphic Filter\</emph\>\</link\> toolbar, which you can open with the icon on the \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> Bar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id7055574				0	en-GB	The original picture file will not be changed by the filters. Filters are applied to a picture only inside the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273	14			0	en-GB	Some of the filters open a dialogue box, which you can use to select, for example, the intensity of the filter. Most filters can be applied multiple times to increase the filter effect.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3150105	15			0	en-GB	In $[officename] Draw and $[officename] Impress, you can add text and graphics, select these objects together with the bitmap, and export the selection as a new bitmap image.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id2572405				0	en-GB	The Picture dialogue box				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id6457411				0	en-GB	Right-click the picture and choose \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> from the sub-menu to open a properties dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id7991882				0	en-GB	Change the properties of the selected picture, then click OK.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153574	16			0	en-GB	Saving Bitmaps				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576	17			0	en-GB	If you want to save in a format such as GIF, JPEG or TIFF, you must select and export the bitmap image.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id0801200803544667				0	en-GB	To export a bitmap in Draw or Impress:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3155414	18			0	en-GB	Select the bitmap image. You can also select additional objects, such as text, to be exported with the image by pressing the shift key while selecting or by opening a selection frame around all objects.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3148618	19			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>File - Export\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Export\</emph\> dialogue box opens.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3157139				0	en-GB	The \<emph\>Export\</emph\> command writes the picture with all applied filter effects to a file. The \<emph\>Save as Picture\</emph\> command in the context menu saves the picture without any filter effects, if the picture was inserted as a linked picture. An embedded picture will always be saved or exported with filters applied.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3083443	20			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>File format\</emph\> field, select the file format you want, for example GIF or JPEG.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3152462	21			0	en-GB	If you only want to export the selected objects, mark the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3150874	22			0	en-GB	If \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> is not marked, the entire page of the document is exported.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3149417	23			0	en-GB	Enter a name for the file and click \<emph\>Export\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id0801200803525078				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>To export a bitmap in Writer: Right-click the bitmap, choose Save Graphics. You will see the Graphics Export dialogue box. Enter a file name and select a file type.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id1033051				0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/24010000.xhp\"\>Graphic Filter Bar from the Picture Bar\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Editing Graphic Objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145136				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>resizing, see also scaling/zooming\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>scaling, see also zooming\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawings, see also draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>graphic objects, see draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; drawing pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; drawings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; drawing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>objects; copying when moving in presentations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; adding/editing/copying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>circle drawings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>square drawings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>handles; scaling\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>scaling; objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>objects;moving and resizing with mouse\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resizing;objects, by mouse\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures;scaling/resizing\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145136	11			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"insert_graphic_drawit\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/insert_graphic_drawit.xhp\" name=\"Editing Graphic Objects\"\>Editing Graphic Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345	9			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Drawing\</emph\> to open the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, if it is not already open.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460	2			0	en-GB	Drawing objects can be subsequently edited and modified. Drawing objects created in this way are vector graphics, which you can scale freely without any loss of quality.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3148491	3			0	en-GB	To create a rectangle, click the rectangle icon and move your cursor to the place in the document where you want one corner of the rectangle to be. Press the mouse button and hold it down while dragging to the opposite corner of the rectangle. When you release the mouse button, the rectangle is inserted in the document. It is selected, and you can edit its properties through the context menu.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164	13			0	en-GB	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"DRAW\"\>To draw multiple objects of the same type, double-click the icon.\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"IMPRESS\"\>To draw multiple objects of the same type, double-click the icon.\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Draw multiple objects of the same type. Click the document without moving the mouse to stop drawing objects.\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3148473	4			0	en-GB	If you want to open up draw objects from the centre instead of dragging from one corner to the other, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while dragging. \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>With some window managers, you may need to hold down also the meta key.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id9448225				0	en-GB	Holding down the Shift key while dragging restricts the created object. For example, instead of a rectangle you get a square, instead of an ellipse you get a circle. When you drag a handle of an existing object with Shift held down, the aspect ratio of the object is retained.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153626	5			0	en-GB	To scale the objects, first select them by clicking on them with the selection tool. You then see eight handles around the object. When you drag one of the four corner handles, the opposite corner remains fixed while the other three corners move. When you drag one of the side handles, the opposite side remains fixed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id224616				0	en-GB	To scale a draw object using the keyboard, first select the object, then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab repeatedly to highlight one of the handles. Then press an arrow key. To scale in smaller steps, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while pressing an arrow key. Press Esc to leave the point edit mode.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669	6			0	en-GB	To move draw objects, first select them. To select more than one object, press the Shift key while clicking. Select text objects by clicking exactly on their edge. While holding down the mouse button, drag the objects to the new location.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id7199316				0	en-GB	To move a draw object using the keyboard, first select the object, then press an arrow key. To move in smaller steps, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while pressing an arrow key.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id7133399316				0	en-GB	To enter text to be a part of a graphics object, select the object and start typing your text. Click outside the object to end entering text. Double-click text inside an object to edit the text.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422	8			0	en-GB	To revert to normal mode after creating and editing draw objects, click in an area of the document containing no objects. If you see a drawing cursor, first exit this mode by clicking the \<emph\>Select\</emph\> icon.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145785	10			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01140000.xhp\" name=\"Information about the individual icons\"\>Information about the individual icons\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Inserting Special Characters				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154927				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>characters; special\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; special characters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>special characters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; inserting special characters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>accents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>compose key to insert special characters\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154927	1			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"insert_specialchar\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/insert_specialchar.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Special Characters\"\>Inserting Special Characters\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576	2			0	en-GB	This function allows you to insert special characters, such as tick marks, boxes, and telephone symbols, into your text.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535	3			0	en-GB	To view a selection of all characters, choose \<emph\>Insert - Special Character\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275	6			0	en-GB	In the large selection field click the desired character or several characters in succession. The characters are displayed at the bottom of the dialogue box. When you close the dialogue box with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>, all displayed characters in the selected font are inserted in the current document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031	4			0	en-GB	In any text input field (such as the input fields in the \<emph\>Find & Replace\</emph\> dialogue box) you can press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+S to open the \<emph\>Special Characters\</emph\> dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3155630	7			0	en-GB	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>At present there are three ways of entering letters with accents directly from the keyboard.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3154897	8			0	en-GB	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>\<emph\>Solaris\</emph\>: Using a Sun keyboard. First press the Compose key to the right of the space bar, then enter the first and second modifiers.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315	9			0	en-GB	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>\<emph\>Linux / NetBSD:\</emph\> Using the dead-keys. In an xterm window first press the (´) or (`) key. The character should not appear on the screen. Now press a letter, such as "e". The e is given an accent, é or è. If not, then check in the XF86Config file if a "nodeadkeys" XkbdVariant has been loaded there and replace it. You may also have set the environment variable SAL_NO_DEADKEYS, which deactivates the dead-keys.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3148943	10			0	en-GB	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>\<emph\>All Unix systems:\</emph\> (Alt Graph) as additional compose key. The (Alt Graph) key can work in $[officename] like the Compose key, if you set the environment variable SAL_ALTGR_COMPOSE. The (Alt Graph) key must trigger a mode_switch, so, for example, xmodmap -e "keysym Alt_R = Mode_switch" must be set. First press (Alt Graph), then the first modifier, then the second modifier. The characters are combined as described on a Solaris system in the file /usr/openwin/include/X11/Suncompose.h.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3149047	5			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/04100000.xhp\" name=\"Special Characters\"\>Special Characters\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896	11			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040200.xhp\" name=\"AutoCorrect\"\>AutoCorrect\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Integrating new UNO components				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149760				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>add-ons, see UNO components\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>UNO components;integrating new\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>installing;UNO components\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149760	7			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"integratinguno\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/integratinguno.xhp\" name=\"Integrating new UNO components\"\>Integrating new UNO components\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571	1			0	en-GB	Programmers can write and integrate their own UNO (Universal Network Objects) components to $[officename]. Those new components can be added to the $[officename] menus and toolbars; we call them "Add-Ons".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751	2			0	en-GB	The integration of new components is supported by some tools and services. Details can be found in the $[officename] Developer's Guide. The three main steps are as follows:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748	3			0	en-GB	Register the new components within $[officename]. This can be accomplished using the tool \<item type=\"literal\"\>unopkg\</item\>, which can be found in {installpath}\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>/ \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>\\\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>program.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345	4			0	en-GB	Integrate the new components as services. The ProtocolHandler and JobDispatch services assist you; more information can be found in the $[officename] Developer's Guide.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460	5			0	en-GB	Change the user interface (menus or toolbars). This can be done almost automatically by writing an XML text file that describes the changes. More information can be found in the $[officename] Developer's Guide.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3151110	6			0	en-GB	The Add-Ons can extend the functionality of $[officename]. They are not related to the \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"Add-Ins\"\>Add-Ins\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Add-Ins\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> that provide new functions for $[officename] Calc.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Shortcuts (%PRODUCTNAME Accessibility)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	bm_id3158421				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility;general shortcuts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>shortcut keys; %PRODUCTNAME accessibility\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158421	52			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"keyboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/keyboard.xhp\" name=\"Shortcuts (%PRODUCTNAME Accessibility)\"\>Shortcuts (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Accessibility)\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3159201	25			0	en-GB	You can control \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> without using a mouse device, using only the keyboard.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149177	24			0	en-GB	On each module's main help page (for example, the \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer or \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc main help page) there is a link to access the keyboard shortcuts' help for that module.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145382	23			0	en-GB	In addition, under the keyword "Accessibility" you find step-by-step instructions about how to control the selected module without a mouse device.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166460	22			0	en-GB	Working with the \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> user interface without mouse				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154749	39			0	en-GB	Activating menu bar, toolbars, windows, and document				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156329	38			0	en-GB	Repeatedly pressing F6 switches the focus and circles through the following objects:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150669	37			0	en-GB	menu bar,				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149234	36			0	en-GB	every toolbar from top to bottom and from left to right,				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147618	35			0	en-GB	every free window from left to right,				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154514	34			0	en-GB	document				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153252	32			0	en-GB	Press Shift+F6 to switch through objects in the opposite direction.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3152473	31			0	en-GB	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6 to switch to the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3152360	30			0	en-GB	Press F10 to switch to the menu bar and back.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896	29			0	en-GB	Escape closes an open sub-menu, a toolbar, or the current free window.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3161656	21			0	en-GB	Calling a menu command				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3151056	20			0	en-GB	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> or F6 or F10 to select the first menu (the \<emph\>File\</emph\> menu). With right arrow, the next menu to the right is selected; with left arrow, the previous menu.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153381	19			0	en-GB	Arrow down opens a selected menu. Any additional arrow down and up arrow move the selection through the menu commands. With right arrow you open any existing sub-menus.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148798	18			0	en-GB	Press Enter to execute the selected menu command.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147086	17			0	en-GB	Executing an icon command				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148922	16			0	en-GB	Press F6 repeatedly until the first icon on the toolbar is selected. Use the right and left arrows to select an icon on a horizontal toolbar. Similarly, use the up and down arrows to select an icon on a vertical toolbar. The Home key selects the first icon on a toolbar and the End key, the last.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3144433	15			0	en-GB	Press Enter to execute the selected icon. If the selected icon normally demands a consecutive mouse action, such as inserting a rectangle, then pressing the Enter key is not sufficient: in these cases press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968	28			0	en-GB	Pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter on an icon for creating a draw object. A draw object will be placed into the middle of the view, with a predefined size.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150449	27			0	en-GB	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter on the Selection tool to select the first draw object in the document. If you want to edit, size, or move the selected draw object, first use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6 to move the focus into the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041	26			0	en-GB	If a toolbar is longer than can be displayed on screen, it shows an icon at the right or lower edge. Select the toolbar and press PageUp or PageDown to display the remaining icons.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150440	14			0	en-GB	Special hints for toolbars				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149983	13			0	en-GB	Press the down arrow or right arrow to open the selected toolbar. This is equivalent to a mouse click. In the toolbar use the right arrow and left arrow keys. The Home and End keys select the first and last icon in the toolbar, respectively.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145365	12			0	en-GB	Close the toolbar with Esc. It is not possible to move the toolbar without a mouse.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151119	11			0	en-GB	Selection from a combo box				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3146986				0	en-GB	\<image id=\"img_id3148645\" src=\"res/helpimg/zellvor.png\" width=\"1.15in\" height=\"0.3165in\" localize=\"true\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148645\"\>Combo box\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149666	10			0	en-GB	Select the combo box. Press Enter.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155366	9			0	en-GB	Use the down arrow or Page Down key to scroll down the combo box entries, or the up arrow or Page Up key to scroll upwards. The Home key takes you to the first entry and the End key takes you to the last entry.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145749	8			0	en-GB	Press Enter to execute the selected entry.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150685	41			0	en-GB	Selection in Tables				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154320	42			0	en-GB	In several windows, dialogue boxes, and in the table control field, there are tables to select data, for instance, in the right part of the \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/database_main.xhp\" name=\"Data Source View\"\>Data Source View\</link\>. The following keys are used for selections in these tables:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154014	43			0	en-GB	Spacebar: switches from selection of the current row and cancellation of any selection, but not if the current cell is in edit mode.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396	44			0	en-GB	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+spacebar: switches between selection of the current row and cancellation of this selection.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149488	45			0	en-GB	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+spacebar: switches between selection of the current column and cancellation of this selection.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286	73			0	en-GB	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Up Arrow or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Down Arrow: moves the window separator between table and form, for instance in the bibliography database.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145251	147			0	en-GB	In a table control or in the data source view, the Tab key moves to the next column. To move to the next control, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab. To move to the previous control, press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150592	7			0	en-GB	Size and Position of Windows and Dialogue Boxes				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153221	6			0	en-GB	First press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+spacebar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148456	5			0	en-GB	A system menu opens with menu commands like \<emph\>Move\</emph\>, \<emph\>Resize\</emph\> and \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400	4			0	en-GB	Choose a command (down arrow, then Enter).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155083	3			0	en-GB	Now you can use the arrow keys to move or resize the dialogue box or window.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147497	2			0	en-GB	Press Enter to accept the change. Press Escape to cancel the changes.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146988	150			0	en-GB	Docking and Undocking Windows and Toolbars				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147176	151			0	en-GB	Press F6 until the window or toolbar is selected.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707	152			0	en-GB	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+F10.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154479	148			0	en-GB	Selecting objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148993	149			0	en-GB	Press Shift+F4 to select the first object in the current document. When an object is selected, press Tab to select the next object, or press Esc to go back to the text.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152962	54			0	en-GB	Edit Objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156379	53			0	en-GB	A selected OLE object can be activated with the Enter key.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155766	55			0	en-GB	Edit Position and Size of Objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148405	56			0	en-GB	Use the arrow keys to move the selected object by one grid resolution unit.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145619	57			0	en-GB	Set the grid resolution unit with \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Grid\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Resolution\</emph\> area. If you enter a number greater than 1 in the \<emph\>Subdivision\</emph\> area, you must press the arrow key as often as the number states to move the selected object by one grid resolution unit.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3166450	58			0	en-GB	Use the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and arrow keys to move the selected object by one pixel.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147345	59			0	en-GB	Use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab to enter the handle edit mode. The upper left handle is the active handle, it starts blinking. Use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab to select the next handle. Press Escape to exit the handle edit mode.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149565	60			0	en-GB	In the handle edit mode, the arrow keys move the selected handle, which changes the object size.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147361	61			0	en-GB	Edit the Anchors of Objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148534	62			0	en-GB	You can move the anchor of an object with the arrow keys. First enter the handle edit mode and select the anchor. Depending on the type of anchor, you can then move the anchor in different directions.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3163808	63			0	en-GB	Select the object.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150646	64			0	en-GB	Enter the handle edit mode with \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150940	65			0	en-GB	The upper left handle starts blinking. Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab several times, until no handle blinks. This signals that now the anchor of the object is activated. \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>In text documents you can press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+A to activate the anchor directly.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153919	66			0	en-GB	Use the arrow keys to move the anchor. The object follows the anchor as appropriate.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3152582	67			0	en-GB	You can change the anchor of the selected object for example in the object's context menu.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148393	68			0	en-GB	If the object is anchored \<emph\>To Paragraph\</emph\>, the arrow keys move the object to the previous or next paragraph.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145615	69			0	en-GB	If the object is anchored \<emph\>To page\</emph\>, the keys Page Up or Page Down move it to the previous or next page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145135	70			0	en-GB	If the object is anchored \<emph\>To character\</emph\>, the Arrow keys move it through the current paragraph.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145256	71			0	en-GB	If the object is anchored \<emph\>As character\</emph\>, no anchor icon exists. You cannot move the object.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149527	72			0	en-GB	If the object is anchored \<emph\>To frame\</emph\>, the Arrow keys move it to the next frame in the respective direction.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153270	133			0	en-GB	Controlling the Dividing Lines				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3158413	134			0	en-GB	Documents of \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc, \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Draw, and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Impress can be split horizontally and vertically into separate views. Each view can show other parts of the document. Using the mouse, you can drag a dividing line from the scrollbar into the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149814	135			0	en-GB	Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6: shows the dividing lines at default positions and focus a line.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3158444	136			0	en-GB	Arrow keys: moves the current dividing line a big step in the arrow direction.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3163668	137			0	en-GB	Shift+Arrow keys: moves the current dividing line a small step in the arrow direction.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148426	138			0	en-GB	Delete: deletes the current dividing line				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3151277	139			0	en-GB	Shift+Delete: deletes both dividing lines				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150383	140			0	en-GB	Enter: fixes the current position of the dividing lines				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150369	141			0	en-GB	Escape: resets the current dividing line to its default position				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154492	112			0	en-GB	Controlling the Data Source View				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150515	113			0	en-GB	F4: opens and closes the data source view.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3159109	114			0	en-GB	F6: switches between document and toolbars.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153229	115			0	en-GB	+ (plus key): expands the selected entry in the data source explorer.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150312	116			0	en-GB	- (minus key): collapses the selected entry in the data source explorer.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368	117			0	en-GB	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+E: switches between data source explorer and table.				20130618 17:22:18
