helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155364	2			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"protection\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/protection.xhp\" name=\"Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME\"\>Protecting Content in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153394	3			0	en-GB	The following is an overview of the different ways of protecting contents in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> from being modified, deleted or viewed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146957	4			0	en-GB	Protecting All Documents When Saving				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150775	5			0	en-GB	All documents that are saved in \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000021.xhp\" name=\"OpenDocument format\"\>OpenDocument format\</link\> can be saved with a password. Documents that are saved with a password cannot be opened without the password. The content is secured so that it cannot be read with an external editor. This applies to content, graphics and OLE objects.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410	6			0	en-GB	Turning on protection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145121	7			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> and mark the \<emph\>Save with password\</emph\> check box. Save the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154286	8			0	en-GB	Turning off protection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3148492	9			0	en-GB	Open the document, entering the correct password. Choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> and unmark the \<emph\>Save with password\</emph\> check box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145068	64			0	en-GB	Information entered in \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\> is not encrypted. This includes the name of the author, creation date, word and character counts.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149294	10			0	en-GB	Protecting Revision Marking				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3161646	11			0	en-GB	With every change made in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer, the review function records who made the change. This function can be turned on with protection, so that it can only be turned off when the correct password is entered. Until then, all changes will continue to be recorded. Acceptance or rejection of changes is not possible.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684	12			0	en-GB	Turning on protection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153104	13			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Protect Records\</emph\>. Enter and confirm a password of at least 5 characters.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3144760	14			0	en-GB	Turning off protection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3152920	15			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Protect Records\</emph\>. Enter the correct password.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155113	52			0	en-GB	Protecting Frames, Graphics, and OLE Objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153703	53			0	en-GB	You can protect the content, position and size of inserted graphics. The same applies to frames (in Writer) and OLE objects.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147131	54			0	en-GB	Turning on protection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088	55			0	en-GB	For example, for graphics inserted in Writer: Choose \<emph\>Format - Picture - Options\</emph\> tab. Under \<emph\>Protect\</emph\>, mark \<emph\>Contents\</emph\>, \<emph\>Position\</emph\> and/or \<emph\>Size\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147510	56			0	en-GB	Turning off protection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153657	57			0	en-GB	For example, for graphics inserted in Writer: Choose \<emph\>Format - Picture - Options\</emph\> tab. Under \<emph\>Protect\</emph\>, unmark as appropriate.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152992	58			0	en-GB	Protecting Drawing Objects and Form Objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3166429	59			0	en-GB	The draw objects that you insert into your documents with the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar can be protected from being accidentally moved or changed in size. You can do the same with form objects inserted with the \<emph\>Form Controls\</emph\> toolbar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153226	60			0	en-GB	Turning on protection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3148815	61			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Format - Object - Position and Size\</emph\> - \<emph\>Position and Size\</emph\> tab. Mark the \<emph\>Position\</emph\> or \<emph\>Size\</emph\> check box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3156289	62			0	en-GB	Turning off protection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154991	63			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Format - Object - Position and Size\</emph\> - \<emph\>Position and Size\</emph\> tab. Unmark the \<emph\>Position\</emph\> or \<emph\>Size\</emph\> check box.				20130618 17:22:18
