helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\sidebar_window.xhp	0	help	par_id0002				0	en-GB	The sidebar is available in WRITER, CALC, IMPRESS, and DRAW application.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\sidebar_window.xhp	0	help	hd_id0500				0	en-GB	Sidebar Window Handling				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\sidebar_window.xhp	0	help	par_id0003				0	en-GB	The sidebar is a \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/autohide.xhp\" name=\"docking\"\>dockable window\</link\>. However, you cannot dock it to the bottom or top edge of the working area but only to the left or right edge. The sensitive area for the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command-\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl-\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>double-click method of docking is small, so make sure you click the sidebar window and not its content.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\sidebar_window.xhp	0	help	par_id0004				0	en-GB	In a docked sidebar window the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Close Sidebar Deck\</item\> button in the upper-right corner of the title area minimizes the current deck, but keeps the tab bar open. To reopen the deck click the corresponding tab or drag the sidebar window frame. To close the sidebar window completely uncheck \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Sidebar\</item\> in the View menu.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\sidebar_window.xhp	0	help	par_id0005				0	en-GB	For decks with several panels click the panel title area to toggle between expanded and minimised state of the panel.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\sidebar_window.xhp	0	help	par_id0006				0	en-GB	The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>More Options\</item\> button at the top-right of a panel title opens a dialogue box which provides additional settings. Not all panels have this feature.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Inserting Protected Spaces, Hyphens and Conditional Separators				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155364				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>protected spaces;inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spaces; inserting protected spaces\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hyphens;inserting custom\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>conditional separators\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>separators; conditional\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>dashes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>non-breaking dashes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>replacing;dashes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>protected dashes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exchanging, see also replacing\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155364	30			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"space_hyphen\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/space_hyphen.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Protected Spaces, Hyphens and Conditional Separators\"\>Inserting Protected Spaces, Hyphens and Conditional Separators\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156136	61			0	en-GB	Non-breaking spaces				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008	31			0	en-GB	To prevent two words from being separated at the end of a line, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command key \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl key\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and the Shift key when you type a space between the words.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id5749687				0	en-GB	In Calc, you cannot insert non-breaking spaces.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146957	62			0	en-GB	Non-breaking dash				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3148538	32			0	en-GB	An example of a non-breaking dash is a company name such as A-Z. Obviously you would not want A- to appear at the end of a line and Z at the beginning of the next line. To solve this problem, press Shift+Ctrl+ minus sign. In other words, hold down the Shift and Ctrl keys and press the minus key.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163802	65			0	en-GB	Hyphen, dash				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749	66			0	en-GB	In order to enter longer dashes, you can find under \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</emph\>\<emph\>- Options\</emph\> the \<emph\>Replace dashes\</emph\> option. This option replaces one or two minus signs under certain conditions with an en-dash or an em-dash (see \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040100.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] Help\"\>$[officename] Help\</link\>).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561	67			0	en-GB	For additional replacements see the replacements table under \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options - \</emph\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040200.xhp\" name=\"Replace\"\>\<emph\>Replace\</emph\>\</link\>. Here you can, among other things, replace a shortcut automatically by a dash, even in another font.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153825	63			0	en-GB	Definite separator				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154306	60			0	en-GB	To support automatic hyphenation by entering a separator inside a word yourself, use the keys \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+minus sign. The word is separated at this position when it is at the end of the line, even if automatic hyphenation for this paragraph is switched off.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3151245	64			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/04100000.xhp\" name=\"Special characters\"\>Special characters\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Setting up Printer and Fax Under UNIX Based Platforms				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154422				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>spadmin\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printers; adding, UNIX\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>default printer; UNIX\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>standard printer under UNIX\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>faxes; fax programs/fax printers under UNIX\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printers; faxes under UNIX\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>PostScript; PDF converter, UNIX\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converters; PostScript, UNIX\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>PDF; PostScript to PDF converter, UNIX\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147834	1			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"spadmin\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/spadmin.xhp\" name=\"Setting up Printer and Fax Under UNIX Based Platforms\"\>Setting up Printer and Fax Under UNIX Based Platforms\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3159876				0	en-GB	%PRODUCTNAME uses the installed fonts of your system. In a text document you can select from all printable fonts. In an HTML document or in Web layout, only fonts that are visible on screen are offered. In spreadsheets and drawings you can select from all installed fonts.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233	2			0	en-GB	Under UNIX based platforms, the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\> is provided to help you set up printers and faxes for use with the $[officename] software.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410	117			0	en-GB	Call the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\> as follows:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147242	11			0	en-GB	Change to the {install_path}/program directory.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209	12			0	en-GB	Enter: ./spadmin				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349	14			0	en-GB	After it starts, the window of the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\> will appear.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149580	10			0	en-GB	Following a server installation, the system administrator first logs on as with root privileges, and starts the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\>. The administrator then creates a general printer configuration file called {install_path}/share/psprint/psprint.conf for all users. All changes are immediately available to all users.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159177	121			0	en-GB	Setting up Printers				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3159157	122			0	en-GB	Under UNIX based platforms, the $[officename] software only offers direct support for printers using the PostScript technology. Other printers must be set up as described in the section \<emph\>Printer Drivers in the $[officename] Software\</emph\>. The $[officename] software automatically provides a printer with the default driver for each system queue. You can add additional printers as needed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148564	286			0	en-GB	Adding a Printer				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147559	353			0	en-GB	Change to the {install_path}/program directory.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3152360	354			0	en-GB	Enter: ./spadmin				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360	287			0	en-GB	Click the \<emph\>New Printer\</emph\> button.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3151210	288			0	en-GB	Select the \<emph\>Create Printer\</emph\> option and click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192	289			0	en-GB	Select the appropriate driver for your printer. If you are not using a PostScript printer or your model is not listed, use the \<emph\>Generic Printer\</emph\> driver or follow the steps below. You can also add new drivers using the \<emph\>Import\</emph\> button or delete unnecessary drivers using the \<emph\>Delete\</emph\> button. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3125863	290			0	en-GB	Choose a command line that you can use to print on your printer (for example, lp -d my_queue). Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767	291			0	en-GB	Give the printer a name and determine whether it should become the default printer. Click \<emph\>Finish\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155429	292			0	en-GB	To print a test page, click on \<emph\>Test Page\</emph\>. If the test page fails to print or is incorrectly printed, check all settings as described in \<emph\>Changing Printer Settings\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146147	294			0	en-GB	Printer Drivers in the $[officename] Software				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147428	124			0	en-GB	When installing a non-PostScript printer, you must set your system so that PostScript can be converted into the language of the printer. We recommend using current PostScript conversion software such as Ghostscript (http://www.cs.wisc.edu/~ghost/).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154639	125			0	en-GB	You should set up the \<emph\>Generic Printer\</emph\> in that case. Also ensure that the page margins are set correctly.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3159153	127			0	en-GB	If you are using a printer using the PostScript technology, you should install a description file for the printer (PostScript Printer Definition - PPD) so that you can utilise the specific printer features like paper tray selection, duplex print function and all built-in fonts. You can also use the generic printer driver since it contains the most important data and is suitable for most printers. In that case, you will have to do without the paper tray selection and must correctly set the page margins.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3146976	128			0	en-GB	Some PPD files are installed as default files. If there is no matching PPD file for your printer, you will find various PPD files at http://www.adobe.com/products/printerdrivers/. You can also ask the manufacturer of your printer for PPD files.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147435	346			0	en-GB	Importing Drivers When Creating a New Printer				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149484	129			0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>Import\</emph\> in the driver selection dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260	347			0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>Browse\</emph\> to select the directory in which you unpacked the PPD files.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147443	348			0	en-GB	In the \<emph\>Selection of drivers\</emph\> list box, select the printer driver you want to install.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3145364	349			0	en-GB	Click OK.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152885	350			0	en-GB	Deleting Drivers When Creating a New Printer				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154729	130			0	en-GB	Select the printer driver.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155417	351			0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149909	352			0	en-GB	Be sure that you do not delete the generic printer driver, and remember that drivers deleted from server installations are no longer available to other users who are using the same server installation.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3148456	131			0	en-GB	If the printer has more fonts built in than the usual PostScript fonts, you must also load the AFM files for these additional fonts. Copy the AFM files into the {install_path}/share/psprint/fontmetric directory or into the {install_path}/user/psprint/fontmetric directory. You can find AFM files, for example, at ftp://ftp.adobe.com/pub/adobe/type/win/all/afmfiles/.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148388	296			0	en-GB	Changing Printer Settings				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3156284	22			0	en-GB	In the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\>, select the printer from the \<emph\>Installed printers\</emph\> list box and click \<emph\>Properties\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialogue box appears containing several tab pages. This is where you can make settings that are used according to the PPD file of the selected printer.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3148833	297			0	en-GB	Select the command on the \<emph\>Command\</emph\> tab page. You can remove superfluous commands using the \<emph\>Remove\</emph\> button.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154270	138			0	en-GB	On the \<emph\>Paper\</emph\> tab page, you can define the paper format and paper tray to be used as the default settings for this printer.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3145649	265			0	en-GB	On the \<emph\>Device\</emph\> tab page, you can activate the special options for your printer. If your printer can only print in black and white, choose "greyscale" under \<emph\>Colour\</emph\>, otherwise choose "colour". If switching to greyscale leads to unfavourable results, you can also select "colour" under \<emph\>Colour\</emph\> and see how the printer or PostScript emulator applies it. Furthermore, on this tab page you can set the precision with which colours are described as well as the PostScript level.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150752	284			0	en-GB	The \<emph\>Font Replacement\</emph\> tab page allows you to select a printer font type available in the printer for each font type installed on your computer. This way you can reduce the data volume sent to the printer. Font replacement can be turned on or off for each printer individually.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153924	266			0	en-GB	You should also set the page margins correctly on the \<emph\>Additional settings\</emph\> tab when using the generic printer driver so that your printout is not cropped. You can also enter a description in the Comments field, which will also be displayed on the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155443	267			0	en-GB	Some of these settings can also be set for the current printout in the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialogue box or the \<emph\>Printer Settings\</emph\> dialogue box in the $[officename] software with the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> button.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150042	132			0	en-GB	Renaming or Deleting Printers				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338	134			0	en-GB	Select a printer from the \<emph\>Installed printers\</emph\> list box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149258	136			0	en-GB	To rename the selected printer, click \<emph\>Rename\</emph\>. Enter an appropriate name in the dialogue box that appears and click OK. The name must be unique and should be chosen so that you can recognise the printer and the application. Printer names must be assigned the same for all users because, when documents are exchanged, the selected printer remains unchanged if the recipient has it under the same name.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963	137			0	en-GB	To delete the selected printer, click \<emph\>Remove\</emph\>. The default printer or a printer that has been created by the system administrator in a server installation cannot be removed using this dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147346	140			0	en-GB	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>Selecting a Default Printer \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3145769	31			0	en-GB	To make the printer selected from the \<emph\>Installed printers\</emph\> list box the default printer, double-click its name or click the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> button.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154204	141			0	en-GB	Using Fax Functionality				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3148463	52			0	en-GB	If you have installed a fax package such as Efax or HylaFax on your computer, you can send faxes with the $[officename] software.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154575	355			0	en-GB	Change to the {install_path}/program directory.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3151277	356			0	en-GB	Enter: ./spadmin				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3146808	298			0	en-GB	Click \<emph\>New Printer\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Add Printer\</emph\> dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3151070	299			0	en-GB	Select \<emph\>Connect a fax device\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150787	300			0	en-GB	Choose whether to use the default driver or another printer driver. If you are not using the default driver, select the appropriate driver. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155111	301			0	en-GB	Enter a command line with which to communicate with the fax in the following dialogue box. In the command line of each fax sent "(TMP)" is replaced by a temporary file and "(PHONE)" by the telephone number of the recipient fax machine. If "(TMP)" occurs in the command line, the PostScript code is transmitted in a file, otherwise as standard input through a pipe. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3146135	302			0	en-GB	Assign a name to your new fax printer and determine whether the telephone numbers (see below) marked in the text should be removed from the printout, or not. Click \<emph\>Finish\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147506	303			0	en-GB	You can now send faxes by printing to the printer that has just been created.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3148419	83			0	en-GB	Enter the fax number as text in the document. You can also enter a field that takes the fax number from your active database. In any case, the fax number must start with the characters @@# and end with @@. A valid entry would have the form @@#1234567@@.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150826	304			0	en-GB	If these characters including the telephone number are not printed, activate the \<emph\>Fax number is removed from the printout\</emph\> option under \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> on the \<emph\>Command\</emph\> tab page. If no telephone number is entered in the document, a dialogue box prompting you for it will appear after the printout.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154196	305			0	en-GB	In $[officename] you can also activate an icon for sending faxes to a default fax. To do this, choose \<emph\>Tools - Customise - Toolbars\</emph\>, click \<emph\>Add Commands\</emph\> and add from "Documents" the \<emph\>Send Default Fax\</emph\> icon. You can set which fax is used when this button is pressed under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Print\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150517	84			0	en-GB	Remember to create one separate print job for each fax, otherwise, the first recipient will receive all the faxes. In the \<emph\>Tools - Mail Merge\</emph\> dialogue box select the \<emph\>Printer\</emph\> option and then mark the \<emph\>Separate print jobs\</emph\> check box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146929	306			0	en-GB	Connecting a PostScript to PDF Converter				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154989	307			0	en-GB	If a PostScript to PDF converter such as Ghostscript or Adobe Acrobat Distiller is installed on your computer, you can quickly create PDF documents in the $[officename] software.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150524	308			0	en-GB	In spadmin, click \<emph\>New Printer\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Add Printer\</emph\> dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3145268	309			0	en-GB	Select \<emph\>Connect a PDF converter\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3156445	310			0	en-GB	Choose whether to use the default driver, the Acrobat Distiller driver or another driver. The driver "Generic Printer (T42 enabled)" prefers the type 42 fonts over type 3 fonts; this driver is a good choice for output to a software PostScript interpreter. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155128	311			0	en-GB	In the next dialogue box, enter a command line for the PostScript->PDF Converter. Enter the directory where the PDF files should be saved. If you do not provide a directory, the user's home directory will be used. In the command line "(TMP)" is replaced by a temporary file and "(OUTFILE)" by the target file, the name of which is created from the document name. If "(TMP)" occurs in the command line, the Postscript code is forwarded in a file, otherwise as standard input through a pipe. If Ghostscript or Adobe Acrobat Distiller is in the search path, you can use one of the predefined command lines. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3152889	312			0	en-GB	Assign a name to your new PDF converter. Click \<emph\>Finish\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153064	313			0	en-GB	You can now create PDF documents by printing to the converter that has just been created.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Changing Default Templates				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154285				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>modifying, see changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing, see also editing and replacing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>default templates; changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defaults;documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>custom templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating; templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>templates;editing and saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving;templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resetting;templates\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154285	36			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"standard_template\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/standard_template.xhp\" name=\"Changing Default Templates\"\>Changing Default Templates\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3152811	2			0	en-GB	When you open a new document with \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>, a blank document appears based on a $[officename] template. You can edit, modify, or replace this template so that the new document contains your customised Styles or other contents.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792	3			0	en-GB	Modifying Default Templates				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365	4			0	en-GB	First, open either an existing $[officename] template and modify it, or open a new document and edit it as necessary to create the desired template.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3159152	6			0	en-GB	You can define a document template for each $[officename] module. The following describes how to proceed for text documents.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3145748	8			0	en-GB	Save the document by choosing \<emph\>File - Templates - Save\</emph\> and saving the document in the \<emph\>My Templates\</emph\> category.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011	9			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organise\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3145799	11			0	en-GB	Double-click \<emph\>My Templates\</emph\> in the list on the left. You will see the user-defined templates in the user directory specified under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - Paths\</emph\>. Select the template you have just saved and open the context menu or open the sub-menu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> button.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146901	26			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>Set As Default Template\</emph\>. The next time that you open a new text document, the new document will be based on the new default template.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153947	27			0	en-GB	Resetting Default Templates				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3156276	12			0	en-GB	To reset the modified text template to the original default template:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146792	29			0	en-GB	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organise\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714	32			0	en-GB	Open the context menu and choose \<emph\>Reset default template\</emph\>. In the sub-menu, select the document type whose default setting you want to restore. Thereafter, when you open an empty text document, it will again correspond to the $[officename] default template for text documents.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153764	13			0	en-GB	Using Custom Templates				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3150386	14			0	en-GB	There are several ways to make your work easier by using your own custom templates.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149109	15			0	en-GB	Templates in the Template Folder				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146918	16			0	en-GB	You can save a new template with \<emph\>File - Templates - Save\</emph\> or by selecting "Template" file type in any Save dialogue box. Save the template in the user directory specified under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - Paths\</emph\> to be able to access the template from within the \<emph\>File - New - From Templates and Documents\</emph\> dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960	33			0	en-GB	You may need to update the view of the templates in the dialogue box before you can see a newly created template. In this case, choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organise\</emph\> and in the sub-menu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> button, choose \<emph\>Update\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3147343	17			0	en-GB	To open the template for editing, choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Edit\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3147315	37			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110000.xhp\" name=\"Templates\"\>Templates\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Starting the $[officename] Software With Parameters				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156410				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>start parameters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>command line parameters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>parameters;command line\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>arguments in command line\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156410	52			0	en-GB	Starting the $[officename] Software With Parameters				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147009	1			0	en-GB	By starting the $[officename] software from the command line you can assign various parameters, with which you can influence the performance. The use of command line parameters is only recommended for experienced users.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147618	2			0	en-GB	For normal handling, the use of command line parameters is not necessary. A few of the parameters require a deeper knowledge of the technical background of the $[officename] software technology.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154898	4			0	en-GB	Starting the $[officename] Software From the Command Line				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3156152	5			0	en-GB	Under Windows, select \<emph\>Run\</emph\> from the Windows Start menu, or open a Shell under UNIX® based platforms.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3152472	6			0	en-GB	Under Windows, type the following text in the \<emph\>Open\</emph\> text field and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669	53			0	en-GB	Under UNIX based systems, type the following line of text, then press \<emph\>Return\</emph\>:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147561	7			0	en-GB	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>{install}\\program\\soffice.exe {parameter} \</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>{install}/program/soffice {parameter} \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360	8			0	en-GB	Replace \<emph\>{install}\</emph\> with the path to your installation of the $[officename] software (for example, \<emph\>C:\\Program Files\\Office\</emph\>, or \<emph\>~/office\</emph\>)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3158407	9			0	en-GB	Where required, replace \<emph\>{parameter}\</emph\> with one or more of the following command line parameters.				20130618 17:22:18
