helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3148491	6			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_NUMBERFORMAT_LB_FORMAT\"\>Select how you want the contents of the selected cell(s) to be displayed.\</ahelp\> The code for the selected option is displayed in the \<emph\>Format Code\</emph\> box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154811	97			0	en-GB	Currency category list boxes				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3148563	98			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVXPAGE_NUMBERFORMAT:LB_CURRENCY\"\>Select a currency, and then scroll to the top of the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> list to view the formatting options for the currency.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150866	99			0	en-GB	The format code for currencies uses the form [$xxx-nnn], where xxx is the currency symbol, and nnn the country code. Special banking symbols, such as EUR (for euro), do not require the country code. The currency format is not dependent on the language that you select in the \<emph\>Language\</emph\> box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154071	23			0	en-GB	Language				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138	24			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVXPAGE_NUMBERFORMAT:LB_LANGUAGE\"\>Specifies the language setting for the selected \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>cells\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>fields\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>. With the language set to \<emph\>Automatic\</emph\>, $[officename] automatically applies the number formats associated with the system default language. Select any language to fix the settings for the selected \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>cells\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>fields\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3157320	102			0	en-GB	The language setting ensures that date and currency formats are preserved even when the document is opened on a system that uses a different default language setting.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155995	104			0	en-GB	Source format				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3144432	105			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_CHECKBOX_RID_SVXPAGE_NUMBERFORMAT_CB_SOURCEFORMAT\"\>Uses the same number format as the cells containing the data for the chart.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148451	7			0	en-GB	Options				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3148922	8			0	en-GB	Specify the options for the selected format.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153970	9			0	en-GB	Decimal places				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684	10			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:NUMERICFIELD:RID_SVXPAGE_NUMBERFORMAT:ED_DECIMALS\"\>Enter the number of decimal places that you want to display.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154819	11			0	en-GB	Leading zeros				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3147352	12			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:NUMERICFIELD:RID_SVXPAGE_NUMBERFORMAT:ED_LEADZEROES\"\>Enter the maximum number of zeros to display in front of the decimal point.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155131	13			0	en-GB	Negative numbers in red				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3159252	14			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:CHECKBOX:RID_SVXPAGE_NUMBERFORMAT:BTN_NEGRED\"\>Changes the font colour of negative numbers to red.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147434	15			0	en-GB	Use thousands separator				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3146148	16			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:CHECKBOX:RID_SVXPAGE_NUMBERFORMAT:BTN_THOUSAND\"\>Inserts a separator between thousands. The type of separator that is used depends on your language settings.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150103	17			0	en-GB	Format code				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3159156	18			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SVXPAGE_NUMBERFORMAT:ED_FORMAT\"\>Displays the number format code for the selected format. You can also enter a custom format.\</ahelp\> The following options are only available for user-defined number formats.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155311	19			0	en-GB	Add				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3147219	20			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_NUMBERFORMAT_TBI_ADD\"\>Adds the number format code that you entered to the user-defined category.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149263	21			0	en-GB	Delete				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154150	22			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_NUMBERFORMAT_TBI_REMOVE\"\>Deletes the selected number format.\</ahelp\> The changes are effective after you restart $[officename].				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153573	26			0	en-GB	Edit Comment				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3083444	27			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_NUMBERFORMAT_TBI_INFO\"\>Adds a comment to the selected number format.\</ahelp\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150332	95			0	en-GB	Name line				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3156060	96			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SVXPAGE_NUMBERFORMAT:ED_COMMENT\"\>Enter a comment for the selected number format and then click outside this box.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3145364				0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020301.xhp\" name=\"Number format codes\"\>Number format codes\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153095				0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020301.xhp\" name=\"Custom format codes\"\>Custom format codes\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Number Format Codes				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153514				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>format codes; numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>conditions; in number formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number formats; codes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats; of currencies/date/time\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; date, time and currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>euro; currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>date formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>times, formats\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153514	1			0	en-GB	\<variable id=\"zahlenformatcodes\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020301.xhp\" name=\"Number Format Codes\"\>Number Format Codes\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3150467	88			0	en-GB	Number format codes can consist of up to three sections separated by a semicolon (;).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3150146	108			0	en-GB	In a number format code with two sections, the first section applies to positive values and zero, and the second section applies to negative values.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3158442	109			0	en-GB	In a number format code with three sections, the first section applies to positive values, the second section to negative values, and the third section to the value zero.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3155069	110			0	en-GB	You can also assign conditions to the three sections, so that the format is only applied if a condition is met.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151262	229			0	en-GB	Decimal Places and Significant Digits				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3153624	3			0	en-GB	Use zero (0) or the number sign (#) as placeholders in your number format code to represent numbers. The (#) only displays significant digits, while the (0) displays zeros if there are fewer digits in the number than in the number format.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3153323	107			0	en-GB	Use question marks (?) to represent the number of digits to include in the numerator and the denominator of a fraction. Fractions that do not fit the pattern that you define are displayed as floating point numbers.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3148440	4			0	en-GB	If a number contains more digits to the right of the decimal delimiter than there are placeholders in the format, the number is rounded accordingly. If a number contains more digits to the left of the decimal delimiter than there are placeholders in the format, the entire number is displayed. Use the following list as a guide for using placeholders when you create a number format code:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3150902	86			0	en-GB	Placeholders				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3157896	87			0	en-GB	Explanation				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3152801	5			0	en-GB	#				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3145090	6			0	en-GB	Does not display extra zeros.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088	7			0	en-GB	0 (Zero)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3150774	8			0	en-GB	Displays extra zeros if the number has fewer places than zeros in the format.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_idN1087E				0	en-GB	Examples				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182	9			0	en-GB	Number Format				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749	10			0	en-GB	Format Code				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3148538	11			0	en-GB	3456.78 as 3456.8				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3150355	12			0	en-GB	####.#				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3154142	13			0	en-GB	9.9 as 9.900				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3159256	14			0	en-GB	#.000				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3147077	15			0	en-GB	13 as 13.0 and 1234.567 as 1234.57				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3155388	16			0	en-GB	#.0#				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578	17			0	en-GB	5.75 as 5 3/4 and 6.3 as 6 3/10				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315	18			0	en-GB	# ???/???				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3156152	19			0	en-GB	.5 as 0.5				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762	20			0	en-GB	0.##				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149276	230			0	en-GB	Thousands Separator				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3154380	21			0	en-GB	Depending on your language setting, you can use a comma or a dot-on-the-line as a thousands separator. You can also use the separator to reduce the size of the number that is displayed by a multiple of 1000.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3154905	22			0	en-GB	Number Format				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3150822	23			0	en-GB	Format Code				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3147264	24			0	en-GB	15000 as 15,000				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3151223	25			0	en-GB	#,###				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3154935	26			0	en-GB	16000 as 16				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3153961	27			0	en-GB	#,				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154836	79			0	en-GB	Including Text in Number Format Codes				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150398	231			0	en-GB	Text and Numbers				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3154224	80			0	en-GB	To include text in a number format that is applied to a cell containing numbers, place a double quotation mark (") in front of and behind the text, or a backslash (\\) before a single character. For example, enter \<emph\>#.# "metres"\</emph\> to display "3.5 metres" or \<emph\>#.# \\m\</emph\> to display "3.5 m".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148979	232			0	en-GB	Text and Text				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3153338	82			0	en-GB	To include text in a number format that is applied to a cell that might contain text, enclose the text by double quotation marks (" "), and then add an at sign (@). For example, enter \<emph\>"Total for "@\</emph\> to display "Total for December".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154330	233			0	en-GB	Spaces				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3156294	81			0	en-GB	To use a character to define the width of a space in a number format, type an underscore ( _ ) followed by the character. The width of the space varies according to the width of the character that you choose. For example, \<emph\>_M\</emph\> creates a wider space than \<emph\>_i\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155994	234			0	en-GB	Colour				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3156423	28			0	en-GB	To set the colour of a section of a number format code, insert one of the following colour names in square brackets []:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3154630	29			0	en-GB	CYAN				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3148676	30			0	en-GB	GREEN				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3154123	31			0	en-GB	BLACK				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3149167	32			0	en-GB	BLUE				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3158407	33			0	en-GB	MAGENTA				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3149560	34			0	en-GB	RED				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3147502	35			0	en-GB	WHITE				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3153368	36			0	en-GB	YELLOW				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147435	111			0	en-GB	Conditions				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148575	235			0	en-GB	Conditional Brackets				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3155312	112			0	en-GB	You can define a number format so that it only applies when the condition that you specify is met. Conditions are enclosed by square brackets [ ].				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3159179	115			0	en-GB	You can use any combination of numbers and the <, <=, >, >=, = and <> operators.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3159196	236			0	en-GB	For example, if you want to apply different colours to different temperature data, enter:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3150872	113			0	en-GB	[BLUE][<0]#,0 "°C";[RED][>30]#,0 "°C";[BLACK]#,0 "°C"				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3157870	114			0	en-GB	All temperatures below zero are blue, temperatures in the range 0 to 30 °C are black, and temperatures higher than 30 °C are red.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154833	90			0	en-GB	Positive and Negative Numbers				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3147295	91			0	en-GB	To define a number format that adds a different text string to a number depending on if the number is positive, negative, or equal to zero, use the following format:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3153727	92			0	en-GB	"plus" 0;"minus" 0;"null" 0				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149260	83			0	en-GB	Percentages and Scientific Notation				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147218	237			0	en-GB	Percentages				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3151168	84			0	en-GB	To display numbers as percentages, (numbers that are multiplied by 100) add the percent sign (%) to the number format.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156005	89			0	en-GB	Scientific Notation				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3146923	85			0	en-GB	Scientific notation lets you write very large numbers or very small fractions in a compact form. For example, in scientific notation, 650000 is written as 6.5 x 10^5, and 0.000065 as 6.5 x 10^-5. In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>, these numbers are written as 6.5E+5 and 6.5E-5, respectively. To create a number format that displays numbers using scientific notation, enter a # or 0, and then one of the following codes E-, E+, e- or e+.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159080	98			0	en-GB	Number Format Codes of Currency Formats				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3147318	99			0	en-GB	The default currency format for the cells in your spreadsheet is determined by the regional setting of your operating system. If you want, you can apply a custom currency symbol to a cell. For example, enter #,##0.00 € to display 4.50 € (euro).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3150032	167			0	en-GB	You can also specify the locale setting for the currency by entering the locale code for the country after the symbol. For example, [$€-407] represents euro in Germany. To view the locale code for a country, select the country in the \<emph\>Language\</emph\> list on the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab of the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157309	238			0	en-GB	Date and Time Formats				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153740	37			0	en-GB	Date Formats				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3152791	38			0	en-GB	To display days, months and years, use the following number format codes.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id610980				0	en-GB	Not all format codes give meaningful results for all languages.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3152376	39			0	en-GB	Format				20130618 17:22:18
