helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3148397	228			0	en-GB	To enter a date in a cell, use the Gregorian calendar format. For example, in a (British) English locale, enter 01/02/2002 for 2nd Jan 2002.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3153274	137			0	en-GB	All date formats are dependent on the locale that is set in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language settings - Languages\</emph\>. For example, if your locale is set to 'Japanese', then the Gengou calendar is used. The default date format in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> uses the Gregorian Calendar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3153795	216			0	en-GB	To specify a calendar format that is independent of the locale, add a modifier in front of the date format. For example, to display a date using the Jewish calendar format in a non-Hebrew locale, enter: [~jewish]DD/MM/YYYY.				20130618 17:22:18
