helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148482	66			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Arc\"\>Draws an arc in the current document. To draw an arc, drag an oval to the size you want, and then click to define the starting point of the arc. Move your pointer to where you want to place the endpoint and click. You do not need to click on the oval. To draw an arc that is based on a circle, hold down Shift while you drag.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153924	30			0	en-GB	Ellipse Pie				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154363				0	en-GB	\<image id=\"img_id3159186\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_pie.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3159186\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156383	67			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Pie\"\>Draws a filled shape that is defined by the arc of an oval and two radius lines in the current document. To draw an ellipse pie, drag an oval to the size you want, and then click to define the first radius line. Move your pointer to where you want to place the second radius line and click. You do not need to click on the oval. To draw a circle pie, hold down Shift while you drag.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154964	33			0	en-GB	Circle Segment				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151017				0	en-GB	\<image id=\"img_id3147315\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_circlecut.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147315\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149106	68			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:CircleCut\"\>Draws a filled shape that is defined by the arc of a circle and a diameter line in the current document. To draw a circle segment, drag a circle to the size you want, and then click to define the starting point of the diameter line. Move your pointer to where you want to place the endpoint of the diameter line and click. You do not need to click on the circle. To draw an ellipse segment, hold down Shift while you drag.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145150	36			0	en-GB	Text				20130618 17:22:18
