helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155500	227			0	en-GB	Meaning				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149408	63			0	en-GB	_blank				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146770	64			0	en-GB	The next document is created in a new empty frame.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149771	65			0	en-GB	_parent				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3159143	66			0	en-GB	The next document is created in a parent frame. If no parent exists, the document is created in the same frame.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151374	67			0	en-GB	_self				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148600	68			0	en-GB	The next document is created in the same frame.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153067	69			0	en-GB	_top				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149174	70			0	en-GB	The next document is created in a top-level window, that is, in the highest frame of the hierarchy; if the current frame is already a top window, the document is created in the current frame.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156172	185			0	en-GB	The Frame property is relevant for HTML forms, but not for database forms.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146950	114			0	en-GB	Graphics				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154344	115			0	en-GB	An image button has a \<emph\>Graphics\</emph\> property. \<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_IMAGE_URL\"\>The \<emph\>Graphics\</emph\> property specifies the graphic's path and file name that you want to have displayed on the button.\</ahelp\> If you select the graphic file with the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button, the path and file name will be automatically included in the text box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150530	208			0	en-GB	Help text				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156310	209			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_HELPTEXT\"\>Provides the option of entering a help text that will be displayed as a tip on the control.\</ahelp\> The tip shows the text in user mode when the mouse is moved over the control.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153287	210			0	en-GB	For URL type buttons, the help text appears as the extended tip instead of the URL address entered under URL.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145377	212			0	en-GB	Help URL				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148649	213			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_HELPURL\"\>Specifies a batch label in URL spelling which refers to a help document and which can be called with the help of the control field.\</ahelp\> The help for the control field help can be opened if the focus is positioned on the control field and the user presses F1.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152541	3			0	en-GB	Background colour				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155073	4			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_BACKGROUNDCOLOR\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sets the background colour of the control field.\</ahelp\>A background colour is available for most control fields. If you click on \<emph\>Background colour\</emph\>, a list will open which enables you to select among various colours. The "Standard" option adopts the system setting. If the desired colour is not listed, click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button to define a colour in the \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010501.xhp\" name=\"Colour\"\>\<emph\>Colour\</emph\>\</link\> dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148971	40			0	en-GB	Scrollbar				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3144430	41			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_HSCROLL\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Adds the scrollbar type that you specify to a text box.\</ahelp\>Adds the scrollbar type that you specify to a text box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1110B				0	en-GB	Incr./decrement value				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1110F				0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Determines intervals to add or subtract with each activation of the spin button control.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146779	85			0	en-GB	Value step				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155096	86			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_VALUESTEP\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines spin button intervals.\</ahelp\>You can preset the value intervals for numeric and currency spin buttons. Use the up and down arrow buttons of the spin button to increase or decrease the value.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145756	73			0	en-GB	List entries				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151300	120			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_STRINGITEMLIST\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Defines the list entries visible in the document. Open this list and type your text. Use Shift+Enter for a new line. With list and combo boxes, you can define the list entries that will be visible in the document. Open the \<emph\>List entries\</emph\> field and type your text.\</ahelp\> Please note the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170100.xhp\" name=\"tips\"\>tips\</link\> referring to the keyboard controls.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152874	228			0	en-GB	The predefined default list entry is entered into the \<emph\>Default selection combo\</emph\> box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154610	186			0	en-GB	Note that the list entries entered here are only incorporated into the form if, on the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab under \<emph\>List Content Type\</emph\>, the option "Value List" is selected.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154767	188			0	en-GB	If you do not want the list entries to be written to the database or transmitted to the recipient of the web form, but rather assigned values that are not visible in the form, you can assign the list entries to other values in a value list. The value list is determined on the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170102.xhp\" name=\"Data\"\>\<emph\>Data\</emph\>\</link\> tab. Under \<emph\>Type of List Contents\</emph\>, select the option "Value List". Then enter the values under \<emph\>List Contents\</emph\> that are to be assigned to the corresponding visible list entries of the form. For the correct assignment, the order in the value list is relevant.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150511	189			0	en-GB	For HTML documents, a list entry entered on the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab corresponds to the HTML tag <OPTION>; an entry of the value list entered on the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab under \<emph\>List Contents\</emph\> corresponds to the <OPTION VALUE=...> tag.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154290	121			0	en-GB	Date latest				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148637	122			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DATEMAX\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines a date which can not be exceeded by another value introduced by the user.\</ahelp\>Determines a date which can not be exceeded by another value introduced by the user.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149804	123			0	en-GB	Max text length				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150776	124			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_MAXTEXTLEN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Defines the maximum number of characters that the user can enter.\</ahelp\>For text and combo boxes, you can define the maximum number of characters that the user can enter. If this control field property is uncertain, the default setting will be zero.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153813	190			0	en-GB	If the control is linked to a database and the text length is to be accepted from the field definition of the database, you must not enter the text length here. The settings are only accepted from the database if the control property was not defined ("Not Defined" state).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145599	125			0	en-GB	Value max				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154733	126			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_EFFECTIVEMAX\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Defines a value for the control field which can not be exceeded by another value introduced by the user.\</ahelp\>For numeric and currency fields, you can determine the maximum value that the user can enter.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154835	127			0	en-GB	Time max				20130618 17:22:18
