helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154873	2			0	en-GB	On the ruler, set the tabs for the current paragraph, or all selected paragraphs, using the mouse.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148520	3			0	en-GB	Initially the default tabs are shown on the horizontal ruler. Once you set a tab, only the default tabs to the right of the tab that you have set are available.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-GB	Setting Indents, Margins, and Columns				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148668				0	en-GB	\<bookmark_value\>margins; setting with the mouse\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; setting with the mouse\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paragraphs; indents, margins and columns\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148668	1			0	en-GB	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/13020000.xhp\" name=\"Setting Indents, Margins, and Columns\"\>Setting Indents, Margins, and Columns\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155364	2			0	en-GB	You can define the indents and margins for the current paragraph, or for all selected paragraphs, using the mouse.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152594	3			0	en-GB	If you split the page into columns, or the cursor is placed in a multiple-column text frame, you can change the column width and the column spacing by dragging them on the ruler with the mouse.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154398	4			0	en-GB	When an object, an image, or a draw object is selected, you will see the borders of the object in the ruler. You can change the borders by dragging them on the ruler with the mouse.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146130	5			0	en-GB	If the cursor is placed in a table cell, you can change the indents for the contents of the cell by dragging them with the mouse on the ruler. You can change the boundary lines of the table on the ruler or by dragging the actual boundary line.				20130618 17:22:18
