helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01013000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149809	3			0	en-GB	Options for high-contrast appearance				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01013000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153106	4			0	en-GB	High-contrast is an operating system setting that changes the system colour scheme to improve readability. You can decide how \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> uses the high-contrast settings of the operating system.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01013000.xhp	0	help	par_id3125863	31			0	en-GB	Cell borders and shadows are always shown in text colour when high-contrast mode is active. The cell background colour is ignored then.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01013000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155132	29			0	en-GB	Automatically detect high-contrast mode of operating system				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01013000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768	30			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_CHECKBOX_RID_SVXPAGE_ACCESSIBILITYCONFIG_CB_AUTO_DETECT_HC\"\>Switches \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> into high-contrast mode when the system background colour is very dark.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01013000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154918	19			0	en-GB	Use automatic font colour for screen display				20130618 17:22:18
