helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876	17			0	en-GB	Some of the settings defined here are only valid for the current document and must be defined separately for each document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149400	47			0	en-GB	Use printer metrics for document formatting				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155602	48			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_TP_OPTLOAD_PAGE_CB_PRINTER_METRICS\"\>Specifies that printer metrics are applied for printing and also for formatting the display on the screen.\</ahelp\> If this check box is not marked, a printer independent layout will be used for screen display and printing.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155768	49			0	en-GB	If you set this option for the current document and then save the document, for example, in an older binary format, this option will not be saved. If you later open the file from the older format, this option will be set by default.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145640	9			0	en-GB	Add spacing between paragraphs and tables (in current document)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147339	18			0	en-GB	In $[officename] Writer, paragraph spacing is defined differently than in Microsoft Word documents. If you have defined spacing between two paragraphs or tables, spacing is also added in the corresponding Microsoft Word documents.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151250	19			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_OPTLOAD_PAGE:CB_MERGE_PARA_DIST\"\>Specifies whether to add Microsoft Word-compatible spacing between paragraphs and tables in $[officename] Writer text documents.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146317	29			0	en-GB	Add paragraph and table spacing at tops of pages (in current document)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333	30			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_OPTLOAD_PAGE:CB_MERGE_PARA_DIST_PAGESTART\"\>Specifies whether paragraph spacing at the top of a page will also be effective at the beginning of a page or column if the paragraph is positioned on the first page of the document.\</ahelp\> The same applies for a page break.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145789	20			0	en-GB	If you import a Microsoft Word document, the spaces are automatically added during the conversion.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149964	42			0	en-GB	Use %WRITERCOMPATIBILITYVERSIONOOO11 tab stop formatting				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152777	43			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_TP_OPTLOAD_PAGE_CB_TAB_ALIGNMENT\"\>Specifies how to align text at tab stops beyond the right margin, how to handle decimal tab stops, and how to handle tab stops close to a line break.\</ahelp\> If this check box is not marked, tab stops are handled in the same way as in other Office applications.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10810				0	en-GB	In text documents created by your current version of Writer, the new tab stop handling is used by default. In text documents created by Writer versions prior to StarOffice 8 or OpenOffice.org 2.0, the old tab stop handling is applied.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F9				0	en-GB	Do not add leading (extra space) between lines of text				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10806				0	en-GB	Specifies that additional leading (extra space) between lines of text is not added, even if the font in use contains the additional leading attribute.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10809				0	en-GB	In text documents created by your current version of Writer, the additional leading is used by default. In text documents created by Writer versions prior to StarOffice 8 or OpenOffice.org 2.0, the additional leading is not used.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN107FF				0	en-GB	Use %WRITERCOMPATIBILITYVERSIONOOO11 line spacing				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10815				0	en-GB	If the option is off, a new process for formatting text lines with proportional line spacing will be applied. If the option is on, the previous method of formatting of text lines with proportional line spacing will be applied.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10818				0	en-GB	In text documents created by your current version of Writer and in Microsoft Word documents of recent versions, the new process is used. In text documents created by Writer versions prior to StarOffice 8 or OpenOffice.org 2.0, the previous process is used.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1081B				0	en-GB	Add paragraph and table spacing at bottom of table cells				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10846				0	en-GB	Specifies that the bottom spacing is added to a paragraph, even when it is the last paragraph in a table cell.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10849				0	en-GB	If the option is off, table cells will be formatted as in Writer versions prior to StarOffice 8 or OpenOffice.org 2.0. If the option is on, an alternative method of formatting table cells will be applied. The option is on by default for new documents created with %PRODUCTNAME %PRODUCTVERSION and for documents imported from Microsoft Word format.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1084C				0	en-GB	Use %WRITERCOMPATIBILITYVERSIONOOO11 object positioning				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10864				0	en-GB	Specifies how to calculate the position of floating objects anchored to a character or paragraph with respect to the top and bottom paragraph spacing.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10867				0	en-GB	If the option is on, the floating objects are positioned as in Writer versions prior to StarOffice 8 or OpenOffice.org 2.0. If the option is off, the floating objects are positioned using an alternative method that is similar to the method used by Microsoft Word.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1086A				0	en-GB	The option will be set to off for new documents. For Writer documents created by a version prior to %PRODUCTNAME %PRODUCTVERSION the option is on.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10821				0	en-GB	Use %WRITERCOMPATIBILITYVERSIONOOO11 text wrapping around objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id4016541				0	en-GB	Writer and Microsoft Word have different approaches on wrapping text around floating screen objects. Floating screen objects are Writer frames and drawing objects, and the objects 'text box', 'graphic', 'frame', 'picture' etc. in Microsoft Word.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id7280190				0	en-GB	In current versions of Writer and in Microsoft Word, page header/footer content and footnote/endnote content does not wrap around floating screen objects. Text body content wraps around floating screen objects which are anchored in the page header.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id2782982				0	en-GB	In Writer versions prior to StarOffice 8 or OpenOffice.org 2.0, the opposite was true.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10892				0	en-GB	If the option is off, which is the default setting, the new text wrapping will be applied. If the option is on, the former text wrapping will be applied.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1092A				0	en-GB	Consider wrapping style when positioning objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10837				0	en-GB	Specifies how the complex process of positioning floating objects that are anchored to a character or paragraph should work. In Writer versions prior to StarOffice 8 or OpenOffice.org 2.0, an iterative process was used, while in current versions a straightforward process is used, which is similar to the same process in Microsoft Word.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10943				0	en-GB	If the option is off, the old %PRODUCTNAME iterative process of object positioning is used. If the option is on, the new straightforward process is used to ensure compatibility with Microsoft Word documents.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	hd_id5240028				0	en-GB	Expand word space on lines with manual line breaks in justified paragraphs				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id8599810				0	en-GB	If enabled, Writer adds spacing between words, in lines that end with Shift+Enter in justified paragraphs. If disabled, spacing between words will not be expanded to justify the lines.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id8012634				0	en-GB	This setting is on by default for .odt text documents. It will be saved and loaded with the document in the .odt text document format. This setting cannot be saved in old .sxw text documents, so this setting is off for .sxw text documents.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10845				0	en-GB	Use as Default				20130618 17:22:18
