helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148491	5			0	en-GB	Press Enter to move selection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	par_id3145119	6			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_LISTBOX_RID_SCPAGE_LAYOUT_LB_ALIGN\"\>Determines the direction that the cursor in the spreadsheet will move after you press the Enter key.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154307	8			0	en-GB	Press Enter to switch to edit mode				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	par_id3148943	9			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_LAYOUT_CB_EDITMODE\"\>Allows you to immediately edit the selected cell after pressing the Enter key.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153896	10			0	en-GB	Expand formatting				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150400	11			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_LAYOUT_CB_FORMAT\"\>Specifies whether to automatically apply the formatting attributes of the selected cell to the empty adjacent cells.\</ahelp\> If, for example, the content of the selected cell has the bold attribute, this bold attribute will also apply to adjacent cells. Cells that already have a special format will not be modified by this function. You can see the range in question by pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> + * (multiplication sign on the number pad) shortcut. This format also applies to all new values inserted within this range. The normal default settings apply to cells outside this range.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148451	14			0	en-GB	Expand references when new columns/rows are inserted				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684	15			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_LAYOUT_CB_EXPREF\"\>Specifies whether to expand references when inserting columns or rows adjacent to the reference range. This is only possible if the reference range, where the column or row is inserted, originally spanned at least two cells in the desired direction.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153194	16			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Example:\</emph\> If the range A1:B1 is referenced in a formula and you insert a new column after column B, the reference is expanded to A1:C1. If the range A1:B1 is referenced and a new row is inserted under row 1, the reference is not expanded, since there is only a single cell in the vertical direction.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150449	17			0	en-GB	If you insert rows or columns in the middle of a reference area, the reference is always expanded.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151176	18			0	en-GB	Highlight selection in column/row headings				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171	19			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_LAYOUT_CB_MARKHDR\"\>Specifies whether to highlight column and row headers in the selected columns or rows.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159252	25			0	en-GB	Use printer metrics for text formatting				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	par_id3145366	26			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_LAYOUT_CB_TEXTFMT\"\>Specifies that printer metrics are applied for printing and also for formatting the display on the screen.\</ahelp\> If this check box is not marked, a printer independent layout will be used for screen display and printing.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146146	27			0	en-GB	Show overwrite warning when pasting data				20130618 17:22:18
