helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707	28			0	en-GB	\<emph\>Example:\</emph\> Type the text 'Test' in cell A1; and the text 'test' in B1. Then type the formula "=A1=B1" in cell C1. If the \<emph\>Case-sensitive\</emph\> box is marked, FALSE will appear in the cell; otherwise, TRUE will appear in the cell.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153965	29			0	en-GB	The EXACT text function is always case-sensitive, independent of the settings in this dialogue box.				20130618 17:22:18
