helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151054	25			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DSADMIN_AUTORETRIEVEENABLED\"\>Enables $[officename] support of auto-incremented data fields for the current ODBC or JDBC data source.\</ahelp\> Mark this check box if the database does not support the auto-increment feature in its SDBCX layer. In general, the auto-increment is selected for the primary key field.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150400	26			0	en-GB	Auto-increment statement				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366	27			0	en-GB	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DSADMIN_AUTOINCREMENTVALUE\"\>Enter the SQL command specifier that instructs the data source to auto-increment a specified Integer data field.\</ahelp\> For example, a typical SQL statement to create a data field is:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159149	28			0	en-GB	CREATE TABLE "table1" ("id" INTEGER)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147084	29			0	en-GB	To auto-increment the "id" data field in a MySQL database, change the statement to:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154909	30			0	en-GB	CREATE TABLE "table1" ("id" INTEGER AUTO_INCREMENT)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933	31			0	en-GB	In other words, enter AUTO_INCREMENT into \<emph\>Auto-increment statement\</emph\> box.				20130618 17:22:18
